","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"7373":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7374":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR`","locale":"en"},"7375":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Data directory containing `settings.toml`, the database, models, experiments, and results","locale":"en"},"7376":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`RVC_NEXT_CONFIG_DIR`","locale":"en"},"7377":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Folder for `settings.toml`, when it should not sit in the data directory","locale":"en"},"7378":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`RVC_NEXT_LOG_LEVEL`","locale":"en"},"7379":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Log level: `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, or `ERROR` (default: `INFO`)","locale":"en"},"7380":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"`RVC_NEXT_<GROUP>__<FIELD>`","locale":"en"},"7381":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Override a setting, e.g. `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `RVC_NEXT_COMPUTE__DEVICE=cpu`","locale":"en"},"7382":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"The engine also reads `RVC_NEXT_CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_CACHE`: the maximum number of CUDA Graphs cached per call site (default: 8). Usually there is no need to change it.","locale":"en"},"7383":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Rules for overriding settings:","locale":"en"},"7384":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Remove the `RVC_NEXT_` prefix and convert to lowercase. `__` (two underscores) denotes the next level: for example, `RVC_NEXT_COMPUTE__GPU_JOBS` maps to `compute.gpu_jobs`, and `RVC_NEXT_LIVE__STREAM__BLOCK_MS` maps to `live.stream.block_ms`.","locale":"en"},"7385":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#environment-variables","content":"Values are parsed as JSON when possible (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), otherwise as strings. `null` or `none` means an empty value.","locale":"en"},"7386":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#view-and-change-settings-from-the-command-line","content":"Keys use dot notation and values are parsed as JSON. All settings are validated before writing; an out-of-range value or incorrect type causes an error (exit code 4), leaving the file unchanged.","locale":"en"},"7387":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#view-and-change-settings-from-the-command-line","content":"`config show` does not display the access token, only whether `access_token_configured` is set. It also lists `resolved_paths` (actual paths used when folder settings are empty), `env_overrides` (effective environment variables), and `pinned`.","locale":"en"},"7388":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#view-and-change-settings-from-the-command-line","content":"`null` can only clear nullable settings (such as `server.access_token` and `training.batch_size`). To restore a setting's default, use `config set` to write the default from the tables below.","locale":"en"},"7389":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#view-and-change-settings-from-the-command-line","content":"Whenever a running server reads settings, it checks at most once per second whether another process (`rvc-next config set` or a text editor) has changed `settings.toml`. If so, it reloads the file and notifies open Web UI sessions. When the Web UI saves settings, it also reads the file first, merges with its current contents, and writes it back without overwriting changes made elsewhere. If a manual edit cannot be parsed or fails validation, the server logs a warning and continues using the previous settings.","locale":"en"},"7390":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#all-settings","content":"In the \"Type\" column, `str?` and `int?` mean the value can be empty (`null`). An empty folder setting means \"use the default folder under the data directory\".","locale":"en"},"7391":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#server-server","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"7392":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#server-server","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"7393":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-config-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-config","t