0":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#debug-logs","content":"You can also set the log level with the `RVC_NEXT_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`; default: `INFO`). Full job logs are saved in `jobs/<job id>.log` under the data directory. View them with `rvc-next jobs show <job id> --log`.","locale":"en"},"7781":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"The root command provides Typer's completion options:","locale":"en"},"7782":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"Reopen the terminal after installation to complete commands, subcommands, and options.","locale":"en"},"7783":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#initial-preparation","content":"For networks in mainland China, you can switch the endpoint when downloading. The choice is saved in settings:","locale":"en"},"7784":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#convert-a-folder","content":"Parameters start from the voice's default preset, with command-line options overriding the corresponding values. `--preset` uses another preset as the starting point.","locale":"en"},"7785":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#convert-a-folder","content":"Without `-o`, results go to `outputs/<date>/<job id>/` under the data directory. File names are `<original name>.<voice>.<format>`; existing files are never overwritten (overwriting requires both `-o` and `--overwrite`).","locale":"en"},"7786":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#convert-a-folder","content":"For a quick preview, add `--preview 15` to convert only the first 15 seconds.","locale":"en"},"7787":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#convert-a-folder","content":"Convert the vocals of a whole song and add the accompaniment back:","locale":"en"},"7788":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#vocal-separation","content":"Without `-p`, the default separation preset from settings is used (`separation.default_preset`, default: `vocals`). Separation models must be downloaded before first use, for example with `rvc-next assets download --group separation`.","locale":"en"},"7789":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#train-a-voice-from-scratch","content":"Without `--stage`, `train run` runs all unfinished stages or stages whose inputs have changed (clean, slice, pitch, features, fit, index). Use `--stage fit --stage index` to run only the specified stages, and `--force` to force a rerun.","locale":"en"},"7790":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#train-a-voice-from-scratch","content":"Multi-speaker datasets: `train new --dataset <root directory> --multi-speaker`, with subfolders named `Name_ID_Repeat` under the root directory.","locale":"en"},"7791":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#train-a-voice-from-scratch","content":"If the dataset needs accompaniment and reverb removed first, use `--clean vocals-clean` to separate before slicing.","locale":"en"},"7792":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#import-models","content":"Files are identified by content (not extension or file name), and indexes are paired with voices by version and name. If pairing is uncertain, the command prints the import plan and exits with code 3. Specify pairs with `--pair voice.pth=index.index` (add `:spkN` for multiple speakers), or use `--keep-unassigned` to put indexes in the unassigned list and assign them later with `rvc-next model index assign`. Training checkpoints (G) are imported as base models by default; add `--extract` to extract a voice instead.","locale":"en"},"7793":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#live-voice-conversion","content":"`live run` runs until ctrl+c (or for the duration set by `--seconds`). The terminal displays one status line with latency, load, input/output levels, and underrun/overrun counts.","locale":"en"},"7794":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next-steps","content":"Command reference: parameters and options for all commands.","locale":"en"},"7795":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next-steps","content":"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables, and data directory layout.","locale":"en"},"7796":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next-steps","content":"FAQ","locale":"en"},"7797":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"page","content":"API and events","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api","locale":"en"},"7798":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Application assembly","locale":"en"},"7799":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"REST conventions","locale":"en"},"7800":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Router overview","locale":"en"},"7801":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"Uploads and media","locale":"en"},"7802":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#access-control","content":"Access control","locale":"en"},"7803":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"`SecurityMiddleware`","locale":"en"},"7804":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"Local clients and server paths","locale":"en"},"7805":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#socketio-and-events","content":"socket.io and events","locale":"en"},"7806":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"Bridging","locale":"en"},"7807":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Events and payloads","locale":"en"},"7808":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-in-openapi","content":"Events in OpenAPI","locale":"en"},"7809":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#generating-typescript-from-the-schema","content":"Generating TypeScript from the schema","locale":"en"},"7810":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#static-pages","content":"Static pages","locale":"en"},"7811":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#startup-ports-and-server_ready","content":"Startup, ports, and `SERVER_READY`","locale":"en"},"7812":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-api#adding-an-endpoint","content":"Adding an endpoint","locale":"en"},"7813":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api","content":"`rvc_next.api` is the FastAPI layer: it parses HTTP requests into core `Record` models, calls one core method, and returns the result unchanged; server-to-browser push uses socket.io. It does not import `rvc_next.engine` (the layer rules in Architecture are enforced by `tests/test_architecture.py`) or contain business logic—even the largest router file, `routers/models.py`, is just a series of routes that call the core in one line.","locale":"en"},"7814":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api","content":"This page is for maintainers adding or removing endpoints, changing security policies, or adding events: application assembly, REST conventions, uploads and media, access control, events and payloads, TypeScript generation from OpenAPI, and port selection at server startup.","locale":"en"},"7815":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"`create_app(services, bound_host, bound_port, extra_hosts, serve_ui, api_prefix)` in `api/app.py` performs these steps (every path below sits under `api_prefix`, empty by default):","locale":"en"},"7816":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Create `RvcNextAPI` (a `FastAPI` subclass; see “Events in OpenAPI” below), with `docs_url=\"/docs\"`, `openapi_url=\"/openapi.json\"`, ReDoc disabled, and `separate_input_output_schemas=False`; store `services` on `app.state.services`.","locale":"en"},"7817":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"`install_error_handlers(app)`: turn any `RvcNextError` into `{\"code\", \"message\", \"detail\"}`.","locale":"en"},"7818":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Mount the 13 router modules in `ROUTERS`, in order, under `/api`; each router has its own `/v1/<resource>` prefix, so the full path is `/api/v1/...`.","locale":"en"},"7819":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Mount socket.io at `/ws` (`SocketBridge.asgi_app()`).","locale":"en"},"7820":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Middleware: add `CORSMiddleware` when `server.allowed_origins` is nonempty; always add `GZipMiddleware(minimum_size=4096)` and `SecurityMiddleware` (the last added is outermost, so security checks run first).","locale":"en"},"7821":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"**Finally**, mount `SPAStaticFiles` at `/`, only if `webui/dist/index.html` exists; without a build, log a warning and keep the API working (Vite serves the pages during development).","locale":"en"},"7822":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"The lifecycle (`lifespan`) only starts and stops the socket bridge. The caller creates and closes the services: `rvc-next webui` uses `build_services(start_background=True)` to start job scheduling and idle unloading, then passes them to `create_app`; tests pass their own `Services`. The same `create_app` can thus serve a real process or run inside `TestClient`.","locale":"en"},"7823":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"Embedded mode (`RvcNextServer` in `embed.py`) takes the same path: `build_services(data_dir, config_dir, settings_path, settings_overrides, start_background=True)`, bind the port, `create_app(..., api_prefix=...)`, run uvicorn on a background thread, and write `server.json` as `rvc-next webui` does. `normalize_prefix()` turns `voice` and `/voice/` into `/voice`; `SecurityMiddleware` matches its protected paths under the prefix. For usage, see Embedding in another program.","locale":"en"},"7824":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#application-assembly","content":"There is one dependency: `ServicesDep = Annotated[Services, Depends(get_services)]` in `api/deps.py`, which reads services from `request.app.state`. There is no global service locator (as used by InvokeAI), so a route declares its dependencies in its signature, and tests only need to replace `app.state.services`.","locale":"en"},"7825":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Convention","locale":"en"},"7826":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Implementation","locale":"en"},"7827":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Reason","locale":"en"},"7828":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"One router per resource","locale":"en"},"7829":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"`api/routers/<resource>.py`, `APIRouter(prefix=\"/v1/<resource>\", tags=[...], responses=ERROR_RESPONSES)`","locale":"en"},"7830":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"The generated client groups endpoints by tag; each route declares its error shape","locale":"en"},"7831":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Explicit `operation_id`","locale":"en"},"7832":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Set on every route, e.g. `list_models`, `run_experiment`","locale":"en"},"7833":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Names in generated types and logs stay stable when functions are renamed","locale":"en"},"7834":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Requests and responses are `Record`","locale":"en"},"7835":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Route signatures use core models directly; a few small API-only models (`AppMeta`, `ImportSession`, `ClearedJobs`…) are defined in the router file","locale":"en"},"7836":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"API JSON has the same shape as CLI `--json` (`tests/cli/test_cli.py::test_model_json_matches_api_shape`)","locale":"en"},"7837":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Plain `def`","locale":"en"},"7838":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Routes that access disk or the database are synchronous","locale":"en"},"7839":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Starlette runs them in a thread pool without blocking the event loop","locale":"en"},"7840":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Only uploads are `async`","locale":"en"},"7841":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Write the request body to a temporary file asynchronously, then pass it to the core via `run_in_threadpool`","locale":"en"},"7842":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"See “Uploads and media” below","locale":"en"},"7843":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Long operations return `Job`","locale":"en"},"7844":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Conversion, separation, training, downloads, merging, extraction, export, and index building immediately return a `Job` snapshot","locale":"en"},"7845":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Progress arrives via `job_updated`; the HTTP request does not wait","locale":"en"},"7846":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Paginated lists","locale":"en"},"7847":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"`GET /jobs` and `GET /outputs` use `cursor` + `limit` (clamped to 1–200 and 1–500 respectively), returning `next_cursor` in `JobPage`/`OutputPage`","locale":"en"},"7848":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"History can be long","locale":"en"},"7849":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Errors are defined in `core/errors.py`; `api/errors.py` only maps them. HTTP status codes and CLI exit codes come from the same exception class (see Architecture for the full table). `ERROR_RESPONSES` declares the `ErrorResponse` model for 400/403/404/409, so the generated client knows the error body shape. A few API-specific conventions:","locale":"en"},"7850":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"`NotLocalError` (`not_local`, 403, defined in `api/deps.py`) exists only in the API: revealing files (meaningful only for a browser on the server machine).","locale":"en"},"7851":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"Errors written directly by `SecurityMiddleware` (`bad_host` 400, `bad_origin` 403, `auth_required` 401) bypass exception handlers but have the same shape.","locale":"en"},"7852":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"FastAPI request validation errors remain 422 + a `detail` array; the frontend's `toError()` maps them to `invalid_input`.","locale":"en"},"7853":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#rest-conventions","content":"`POST /convert` and `POST /separate` reject `output_dir`/`overwrite`: writing to arbitrary directories and overwriting files are CLI-only capabilities for trusted local users.","locale":"en"},"7854":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Module","locale":"en"},"7855":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Prefix","locale":"en"},"7856":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-58","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Main endpoints","locale":"en"},"7857":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-59","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`app_info`","locale":"en"},"7858":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-60","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/app`","locale":"en"},"7859":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-61","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET version`, `GET health` (`status`, `auth_required`), `GET meta` (`local`, `host`, `compute`, `live_available`, `assets_ready`, `features`, `data_dir`)","locale":"en"},"7860":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-62","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`settings`","locale":"en"},"7861":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-63","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1`","locale":"en"},"7862":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-64","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET/PATCH /settings` (deep merge; `server.access_token`: `null` clears it, an empty string is an error; the core publishes `settings_changed`, and changes to `paths` rescan the voice library), `GET/PUT /client-state/{key}` (regex-constrained keys, values up to 256 KiB)","locale":"en"},"7863":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-65","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`compute`","locale":"en"},"7864":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-66","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/compute`","locale":"en"},"7865":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-67","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET devices`, `GET usage`, `POST release` (free GPU memory; 409 when busy, `detail.busy`)","locale":"en"},"7866":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-68","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`assets`","locale":"en"},"7867":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-69","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/assets`","locale":"en"},"7868":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-70","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET \"\"`, `GET repositories`, `POST download`, `POST verify` (the same download job with `verify_only=True`), `DELETE {asset_id}`","locale":"en"},"7869":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-71","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"7870":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-72","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/models`","locale":"en"},"7871":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-73","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Voice library CRUD, `/catalog` and `/catalog/download` (demo voices), import sessions `/imports…`, unassigned indexes `/indexes…`, base models `/base…`, separation models `/separation…`, one-step import `PUT /import` and `POST /import-path`, `POST inspect`, `POST merge`, `POST extract`, legacy installations `/legacy-roots…`, `/{voice_id}/index` (upload, pair, or detach), `/{voice_id}/index/build`, `/{voice_id}/reveal`, `GET /{voice_id}/archive` (the voice as a zip)","locale":"en"},"7872":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-74","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`presets`","locale":"en"},"7873":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-75","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/presets`","locale":"en"},"7874":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-76","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"List (`ensure_default` first when `voice_id` is given), create, update, delete","locale":"en"},"7875":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-77","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`audio`","locale":"en"},"7876":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-78","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/audio`","locale":"en"},"7877":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-79","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`PUT uploads`, `GET files/{id}`, `files/{id}/content`, `files/{id}/peaks`, `files/{id}/analysis`, `GET browse`, `POST resolve-path`, `GET path-peaks`","locale":"en"},"7878":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-80","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`outputs`","locale":"en"},"7879":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-81","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/outputs`","locale":"en"},"7880":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-82","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"List, `POST zip` (streamed), individual output, `content`, `source` (original input for A/B), `peaks`, `source-peaks`, `analysis`, `source-analysis` (spectrogram and pitch curve), delete, `reveal`","locale":"en"},"7881":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-83","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`convert`","locale":"en"},"7882":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-84","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/convert`","locale":"en"},"7883":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-85","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`POST \"\"` → `Job`","locale":"en"},"7884":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-86","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`separate`","locale":"en"},"7885":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-87","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/separate`","locale":"en"},"7886":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-88","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET presets`, `POST \"\"` → `Job`","locale":"en"},"7887":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-89","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`train`","locale":"en"},"7888":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-90","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/train`","locale":"en"},"7889":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-91","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"Experiment CRUD, `dataset/scan`, `PUT/DELETE dataset/files` (uploaded audio), `speakers`, `speakers/from-folders`, `run` → `Job`, `stop`, `metrics?since=`, `checkpoints`, `samples` (one rendered training clip per save), `export` → `Job`, `try` (temporary voice), `POST /import` (legacy experiment)","locale":"en"},"7890":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`jobs`","locale":"en"},"7891":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/jobs`","locale":"en"},"7892":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"List (`state` can be a specific state or `active`/`finished`), `DELETE \"\"` (clear finished jobs, keep outputs), individual job, `log?offset=`, `cancel`, `retry`, `run-anyway`, delete","locale":"en"},"7893":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`live`","locale":"en"},"7894":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`/v1/live`","locale":"en"},"7895":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"`GET state`, `POST start/stop`, `PATCH voice`, `PATCH stream`, `PUT voice-model`, `PUT/GET devices`, `POST devices/check`, `POST devices/test-tone`, `POST meter`, `POST passthrough`, `POST/DELETE recording`","locale":"en"},"7896":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"All fixed paths in `routers/models.py` (`/catalog`, `/imports`, `/indexes`, `/base`, `/separation`, `/legacy-roots`…) precede `/{voice_id}`. FastAPI matches in registration order: new fixed paths must go above wildcard routes, or they will be treated as voice IDs. The same applies to `POST /zip` in `outputs`.","locale":"en"},"7897":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"**Live control also uses REST.** The socket only carries server push (`live_state`, `live_stats`, `devices_changed`); clients never send commands over it. This follows InvokeAI and SD Model Hub: every state-changing operation has an HTTP status code, an error shape, and an OpenAPI description, and can be reproduced with `curl` or the CLI; a disconnected socket does not lose commands.","locale":"en"},"7898":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#router-overview","content":"**One-step import endpoints.** `PUT /models/import` and `POST /models/import-path` wrap import sessions: a `confident` plan is committed directly and returns `ImportResult`; when user decisions are needed, they raise `ConflictError`, with the plan in the 409 response's `detail.plan`, so scripts can switch to the session API to submit decisions. The session API (`POST /imports` → `PUT /imports/{sid}/files` or `POST …/paths` → `GET /imports/{sid}` → `POST …/commit`) is synchronous: commit returns `ImportResult` directly, rather than a job (copying is local; even the slowest separation model load check takes only seconds; see AGENTS.md §8). See Core services for identification and pairing rules.","locale":"en"},"7899":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"**Uploads use `PUT` with a raw request body, without multipart.** `spool()` in `api/uploads.py` writes `request.stream()` in chunks to `<directory>/.incoming/<id>.part`, deleting it on error or disconnect; the route then uses `read_chunks()` to pass the file to the core in 1 MiB chunks (`services.audio.upload`, `imports.add_upload`, `models.set_index_upload`…), and always deletes the temporary file afterward, whether successful or not. The filename is a query parameter (`name` or `filename`, up to 255 characters).","locale":"en"},"7900":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-102","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"Reasons for this approach:","locale":"en"},"7901":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-103","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"Audio and models can be hundreds of MB. Multipart parsing either loads the whole body into memory or relies on `python-multipart`'s temporary-file policy; raw bodies can be written as they arrive with constant memory use.","locale":"en"},"7902":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-104","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"The frontend uses `XMLHttpRequest` to `send(file)` directly and receive upload progress (`fetch()` cannot provide it).","locale":"en"},"7903":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-105","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"`RAW_BODY` is added to the schema as `openapi_extra`, declaring `application/octet-stream`, so generated types know these endpoints accept binary data.","locale":"en"},"7904":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-106","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"**Media uses `FileResponse`.** `audio_response()` in `api/files.py` selects MIME by extension, sets `Cache-Control: private, no-cache`, and includes both an ASCII fallback filename and RFC 5987 `filename*` in `Content-Disposition` (so Chinese filenames download correctly); `?download=true` sets `attachment`. `FileResponse` supports `Range`, so seeking in long audio does not require downloading the entire file. Waveforms are not decoded in the browser: `peaks` endpoints return server-computed, cached peaks (1024 points by default).","locale":"en"},"7905":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-107","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#uploads-and-media","content":"**ZIP downloads**: `POST /outputs/zip` uses `StreamingResponse` to compress and send data as it goes, without writing a ZIP file on the server.","locale":"en"},"7906":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-108","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#access-control","content":"Access control has two layers: `SecurityMiddleware` handles who can connect, while `require_local` in routes guards operations that only make sense for a browser on the server machine.","locale":"en"},"7907":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-109","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"`api/security.py` is pure ASGI middleware for both HTTP and WebSocket. It performs three checks in order:","locale":"en"},"7908":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-110","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"7909":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-111","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"7910":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-112","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Protects against","locale":"en"},"7911":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-113","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Host","locale":"en"},"7912":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-114","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"When bound to loopback, the `Host` header must be `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1`, the bound hostname, or `extra_hosts` (kept by reference, so names added later count at once, which `RvcNextServer.allow_host()` relies on); otherwise 400 `bad_host`","locale":"en"},"7913":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-115","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"DNS rebinding: a malicious page resolves its own domain to 127.0.0.1 and calls the local API","locale":"en"},"7914":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-116","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Origin","locale":"en"},"7915":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-117","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Unsafe methods (anything except `GET`/`HEAD`/`OPTIONS`) and all WebSocket handshakes: if `Origin` is present, it must equal the page's own origin, be in `server.allowed_origins`, or share the host and port with `Host`; without `Origin`, `Sec-Fetch-Site` must be `same-origin`, `none`, or absent. Otherwise 403 `bad_origin`","locale":"en"},"7916":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-118","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Cross-site request forgery: another page sends `POST`/`DELETE` to the local service through the user's browser","locale":"en"},"7917":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-119","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Access token","locale":"en"},"7918":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-120","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"When `server.access_token` is set, requests under `/api/`, `/ws/`, `/openapi.json`, and `/docs` must carry a token; `/api/v1/app/health` is exempt. Otherwise 401 `auth_required`","locale":"en"},"7919":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-121","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Other people on the LAN or public internet","locale":"en"},"7920":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-122","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"The token can be supplied in three places (`request_token()` checks in order): `Authorization: Bearer …`, the `rvc_next_token` cookie, or the `?token=` query parameter. Comparison uses `hmac.compare_digest`. Cookies support browser-initiated requests such as `<audio src>`, which cannot attach headers. `health` is public so the page shell can load without a token, read `auth_required: true`, and open `AuthDialog` to request one.","locale":"en"},"7921":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-123","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"Rejected WebSockets close with code 1008. Settings read by the middleware are functions (`lambda: services.settings.settings.server.access_token`), so changing the token or allowed origins in Settings takes effect immediately without a restart.","locale":"en"},"7922":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-124","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#securitymiddleware","content":"The token is optional: neither a non-loopback bind nor public host names accepted through `extra_hosts` require it; `rvc-next webui` and `RvcNextServer` only log a warning. Protecting a public deployment (firewall, VPN, a reverse proxy with authentication) is left to the user.","locale":"en"},"7923":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-125","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"7924":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-126","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"Definition (`api/deps.py`)","locale":"en"},"7925":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-127","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"Used for","locale":"en"},"7926":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-128","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"`is_local`","locale":"en"},"7927":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-129","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"The client address is loopback and the `Host` is a loopback name (a public host name forwarded by a tunnel or a same-machine reverse proxy is not; `testclient` in tests also counts)","locale":"en"},"7928":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-130","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"`AppMeta.local`; `reveal`, protected by `LocalDep` (show a file in the server's file manager)","locale":"en"},"7929":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-131","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"Every client that passes the middleware may name paths on the server (browsing, resolving audio paths, importing models or indexes by path, creating experiments or updating datasets, importing legacy experiments, adding legacy RVC installations, and so on). Only `reveal` requires a local client: a remote browser has no reason to open the file manager on the server's desktop.","locale":"en"},"7930":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-132","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#local-clients-and-server-paths","content":"**Audio inputs** must be within `paths.browse_roots`: `GET /audio/browse`, `POST /audio/resolve-path`, and inputs with `kind == \"path\"` in `POST /convert` and `POST /separate` (routes call `services.audio.check_refs`). Paths outside these roots produce 400 `invalid_path`, with allowed roots in `detail.roots`. This check exists only in the API—the CLI is run directly by a trusted local user and can read any path. Model imports, dataset folders, and similar paths are not constrained by `browse_roots`.","locale":"en"},"7931":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-133","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"`SocketBridge` in `api/sockets.py` wraps `socketio.AsyncServer(async_mode=\"asgi\")`:","locale":"en"},"7932":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-134","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"`start()` subscribes to the event bus. `LocalEventBus` calls handlers synchronously on the publisher thread, usually a job thread or a thread reading worker output, so the handler only does one thing: `loop.call_soon_threadsafe(queue.put_nowait, event)`, handing the event to the event loop. A background task `_pump()` then calls `emit` for each event; serialization failures for individual events are only logged.","locale":"en"},"7933":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-135","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"Traffic is server-to-client only, broadcast to all connections; there are no rooms or client event handlers (a single-user application).","locale":"en"},"7934":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-136","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"On connection (`_on_connect`), if a token is set, verify it: check handshake `auth.token` first, then fall back to cookies, the `Authorization` header, or query parameters. The outer middleware has already checked Origin, so `cors_allowed_origins=\"*\"`.","locale":"en"},"7935":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-137","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"`asgi_app()` normalizes the mounted path with `route_path(scope)`, then lets engineio match `/socket.io`, accommodating differences in how old and new Starlette versions handle mount prefixes. Clients connect to `<deployment root>/ws/socket.io`.","locale":"en"},"7936":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-138","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#bridging","content":"**Events carry snapshots.** Each event contains a complete `Record` value (for example, `job.model_copy(deep=True)` in `JobUpdatedEvent`), never a live object still being modified by a worker: serialization occurs later on the event loop, when the job thread may already have updated progress. Snapshots also let clients replace their state immediately, without reconstructing history.","locale":"en"},"7937":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-139","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Event classes are defined in `core/events/models.py`; all inherit `EventBase` and set `__event_name__`. `EventBase.get_events()` recursively collects all named subclasses.","locale":"en"},"7938":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-140","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"7939":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-141","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Payload","locale":"en"},"7940":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-142","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Publisher and frequency","locale":"en"},"7941":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-143","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Frontend handling (`api/socket.ts`)","locale":"en"},"7942":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-144","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"`job_updated`","locale":"en"},"7943":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-145","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"`job: Job`","locale":"en"},"7944":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-146","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Job service; state changes immediately, progress throttled to 4 updates per job per second (`PROGRESS_INTERVAL = 0.25`)","locale":"en"},"7945":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-147","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Write to the jobs store and `keys.job(id)`; invalidate related lists on completion","locale":"en"},"7946":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-148","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"`job_log`","locale":"en"},"7947":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-149","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"`job_id`, `offset`, `lines` (up to 50 lines per batch)","locale":"en"},"7948":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-150","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-api#events-and-payloads","content":"Job service, one batch every 0.25 s","locale":"en"},"7949":{"id":"/en/docs/development-api-151","page_id":"/en/docs/development-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/do