s","content":"`compute_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"8219":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-190","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"503","locale":"en"},"8220":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-191","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"9","locale":"en"},"8221":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-192","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"GPU unavailable or out of memory (`detail.reason = \"out_of_memory\"`)","locale":"en"},"8222":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-193","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"`RvcNextError` (base class)","locale":"en"},"8223":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-194","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"`internal_error`","locale":"en"},"8224":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-195","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"500","locale":"en"},"8225":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-196","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"1","locale":"en"},"8226":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-197","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"Other cases","locale":"en"},"8227":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-198","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"The API layer also defines `NotLocalError` (`not_local`, 403) for operations such as “Show in folder” that only make sense for a browser on the server machine.","locale":"en"},"8228":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-199","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"Errors reach this table from three sources:","locale":"en"},"8229":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-200","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"**Engine exceptions** (`engine/errors.py`: `MissingAssetError`, `ModelFormatError`, `AudioError`, `Cancelled`) are converted by `map_engine_error()` in `core/engine_errors.py`; the engine never imports core. Out-of-memory errors are identified by `engine/runtime.is_oom()` (`torch.OutOfMemoryError`, `AcceleratorError` with code 2, MPS / DirectML error messages).","locale":"en"},"8230":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-201","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"**Worker `error` events** are reconstructed by `worker_error()`.","locale":"en"},"8231":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-202","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors-and-exit-codes","content":"**Live worker** `State.error` uses the same `code` values.","locale":"en"},"8232":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-203","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"`core/settings/models.py` is a tree of `Record` models rooted at `Settings`, with groups `server`, `paths`, `compute`, `downloads`, `convert`, `separation`, `training`, `live`. `SettingsService` owns `settings.toml` in the data directory and merges values in this order (later values override earlier ones):","locale":"en"},"8233":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-204","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"Environment variables use `__` to separate levels, for example `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000`, `RVC_NEXT_COMPUTE__DEVICE=cpu`; values are parsed as JSON if possible, otherwise as strings, with `null` / `none` meaning empty. Environment variables and overrides are never written back to the file. `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` is not a setting: it determines the data directory itself.","locale":"en"},"8234":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-205","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"`update()` deep-merges the patch, validates, writes atomically (write `.toml.tmp`, then replace) and notifies listeners, allowing a persistent server to follow settings changes without restarting. TOML has no null, so keys with `None` values are omitted when saving.","locale":"en"},"8235":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-206","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"`config set` and the API's `PATCH /settings` share the same dotted-path logic.","locale":"en"},"8236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-207","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"The public `SettingsView` excludes the access token, exposing only `access_token_configured: bool`; `env_overrides` lists names fixed by environment variables, which the UI uses to display “Set by an environment variable”.","locale":"en"},"8237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-208","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"Empty directory settings mean “inside the data directory”: `SettingsService.models_dir`, `experiments_dir`, `outputs_dir`, `assets_dir` resolve them. `paths.assets_dir` can point directly to an original RVC `assets/` directory to avoid duplicate downloads.","locale":"en"},"8238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-209","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#settings","content":"The `live` group (devices, stream parameters, last voice and parameters) lives in settings rather than client state because devices belong to the server machine and the CLI's `live run` needs the same values. Pure UI preferences (theme, language, last page) are client state. See Configuration and environment variables for each group's fields.","locale":"en"},"8239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-210","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"`core/events/models.py` defines `EventBase(Record)`, with each subclass named by its class attribute `__event_name__`; `EventBase.get_events()` collects all concrete subclasses. The API adds their JSON schemas to OpenAPI, so frontend event types are generated too. Current events:","locale":"en"},"8240":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-211","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"`job_updated`, `job_log`, `jobs_cleared`, `outputs_added`, `outputs_removed`, `models_changed`, `presets_changed`, `assets_changed`, `experiment_changed`, `train_metrics`, `live_state`, `live_stats`, `devices_changed`, `compute_changed`, `settings_changed`.","locale":"en"},"8241":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-212","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"Conventions:","locale":"en"},"8242":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-213","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"**Events carry snapshots**, rather than live objects being modified by worker threads: `job_updated` carries a copy of the entire `Job`.","locale":"en"},"8243":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-214","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"**Throttle at the source**: job progress is limited to 4 updates per second per job, and logs are batched (at most 50 lines per batch; the UI fills gaps through REST using byte offsets).","locale":"en"},"8244":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-215","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"`LocalEventBus` calls handlers **synchronously on the publisher's thread**; handler exceptions are logged without propagating. Subscribers that need to run elsewhere hand off themselves: `SocketBridge` in `api/sockets.py` uses `loop.call_soon_threadsafe` to place events in an asyncio queue, then a task calls `sio.emit(event.__event_name__, event.model_dump(mode=\"json\"))`. CLI progress bars (`cli/progress.py`) subscribe to the same events.","locale":"en"},"8245":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-216","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#events","content":"See API and events for payload details.","locale":"en"},"8246":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-217","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#database","content":"`core/db/database.py`: one shared `sqlite3` connection with an `RLock`; WAL mode, foreign keys enabled, `synchronous=NORMAL`, `busy_timeout=5000` (the CLI reads the same file while the server writes it; for example, `rvc-next jobs list` can see the running server's jobs). Migrations are SQL scripts in the `MIGRATIONS` list: **append only; never change published entries**. `PRAGMA user_version` records how many have run. There are currently two: the first creates `voice_models`, `presets`, `jobs`, `outputs`, `audio_files`, `client_state`; the second adds `catalog_id` to `voice_models` (marking voices downloaded from the demo voice catalog).","locale":"en"},"8247":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-218","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#database","content":"Database contents have two roles:","locale":"en"},"8248":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-219","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#database","content":"**Cache**: `voice_models` can be fully rebuilt from the `models/` directory and legacy RVC installation directories (`models.rescan()`).","locale":"en"},"8249":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-220","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#database","content":"**Record**: job history and output provenance (inputs, voice, parameters).","locale":"en"},"8250":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-221","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#database","content":"Deleting the database loses job history, output provenance, custom presets (defaults are recreated) and the server-side copy of UI preferences; the voice library is rebuilt from disk. Experiments, base models, separation models and unassigned indexes are not in the database at all: they are directories with JSON sidecars, scanned on every listing, so they cannot disagree with the files on disk.","locale":"en"},"8251":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-222","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#data-directory","content":"`default_data_dir()` in `core/paths.py` chooses `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` first, then `%APPDATA%\\rvc-next` on Windows, `~/Library/Application Support/rvc-next` on macOS, and `$XDG_DATA_HOME/rvc-next` on other platforms (default `~/.local/share/rvc-next`).","locale":"en"},"8252":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-223","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#data-directory","content":"`server.json` has another purpose: at startup, `JobService` marks jobs still active as `interrupted`, but skips this if `server.json` shows that another server is using the data directory, avoiding misclassifying that server's jobs as interrupted.","locale":"en"},"8253":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"page","content":"Assets and model repositories","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets","locale":"en"},"8254":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets","content":"Assets are model files RVC Next needs at runtime but does not distribute with its Python package: HuBERT, RMVPE (including ONNX), FCPE, CREPE, training base models, and vocal separation weights.","locale":"en"},"8255":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"The asset catalog: `catalog.json`","locale":"en"},"8256":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#current-assets","content":"Current assets","locale":"en"},"8257":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#two-download-repositories","content":"Two download repositories","locale":"en"},"8258":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#rvc-model-layout","content":"rvc-model layout","locale":"en"},"8259":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#downloads-resume-and-verification","content":"Downloads, resume, and verification","locale":"en"},"8260":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#status","content":"Status","locale":"en"},"8261":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#demo-voices","content":"Demo voices","locale":"en"},"8262":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#models-found-only-in-official-distributions","content":"Models found only in official distributions","locale":"en"},"8263":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-assets#adding-or-updating-assets","content":"Adding or updating assets","locale":"en"},"8264":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets","content":"Assets are model files RVC Next needs at runtime but does not distribute with its Python package: HuBERT, RMVPE (including ONNX), FCPE, CREPE, training base models, and vocal separation weights. A set of demo voices is also available to download. This page describes the `catalog.json` asset catalog format, the two download repositories, download and verification implementation, and how to add or update assets. See Core services for how other core services call `AssetService`.","locale":"en"},"8265":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`rvc_next/core/assets/catalog.json` is distributed as package data (`package-data` in `pyproject.toml`), read by `core/assets/service.py:load_catalog()`, and validated into records from `core/assets/models.py`. It has three top-level keys:","locale":"en"},"8266":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"Record","locale":"en"},"8267":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"8268":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"8269":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`Repository`","locale":"en"},"8270":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`id` (`rvc-model` or `official`), `repo`, `revision`, `title`","locale":"en"},"8271":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"A Hugging Face repository. `selected` is computed from settings, not stored in the catalog","locale":"en"},"8272":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`AssetSpec`","locale":"en"},"8273":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`id`, `title`, `description`, `group` (`inference`/`training`/`separation`), `files`","locale":"en"},"8274":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"A unit that can be downloaded and have its status determined independently","locale":"en"},"8275":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`AssetFile`","locale":"en"},"8276":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`path`, `size`, `sha256`, `sources`","locale":"en"},"8277":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`path` is relative to the asset directory (`paths.assets_dir`), using **the original's `assets/` layout**; `sources` maps repository IDs to the file's path in each repository","locale":"en"},"8278":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`CatalogVoice`","locale":"en"},"8279":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`id`, `name`, `description`, `sample_rate`, `version`, `pitch_guidance`, `files`","locale":"en"},"8280":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"A demo voice; `size`, `has_index`, and `repositories` (repositories hosting all its files) are computed at load time","locale":"en"},"8281":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`CatalogVoiceFile`","locale":"en"},"8282":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"`role` (`model`/`index`), `size`, `sha256`, `sources`","locale":"en"},"8283":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#the-asset-catalog-catalogjson","content":"Imported into the voice library after download, rather than stored in the asset directory","locale":"en"},"8284":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#current-assets","content":"id","locale":"en"},"8285":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#current-assets","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"8286":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#current-assets","content":"Files in the asset directory","locale":"en"},"8287":{"id":"/en/docs/development-assets-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-assets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-assets#current-assets","content"