ation, training, live voice conversion, settings, events and database","locale":"en"},"10192":{"id":"/en/docs/development-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"API and events","locale":"en"},"10193":{"id":"/en/docs/development-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"FastAPI routing conventions, uploads, security model, socket.io events and payloads, OpenAPI → TypeScript type generation and port selection","locale":"en"},"10194":{"id":"/en/docs/development-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Web UI","locale":"en"},"10195":{"id":"/en/docs/development-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Vue 3 frontend: directory structure, `ui/` components and MD3 motion, unified experience contract, data flow, layout rules, internationalisation, tests and adding a page","locale":"en"},"10196":{"id":"/en/docs/development-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"CLI implementation","locale":"en"},"10197":{"id":"/en/docs/development-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Typer factory, command registration, errors to exit codes, `--json`, foreground jobs and adding a command","locale":"en"},"10198":{"id":"/en/docs/development-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Assets and model repositories","locale":"en"},"10199":{"id":"/en/docs/development-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"`catalog.json` format, two download repositories, verification and resumable downloads, adding an asset, models found only in distribution packages","locale":"en"},"10200":{"id":"/en/docs/development-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Parity with the original","locale":"en"},"10201":{"id":"/en/docs/development-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Porting rules, golden tests, behaviour differences from the original and their reasons, torchaudio / torchfcpe ports","locale":"en"},"10202":{"id":"/en/docs/development-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"Tests and checks","locale":"en"},"10203":{"id":"/en/docs/development-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"`dev.py check`, pytest markers and environment variables, tiny models, test layout and CI","locale":"en"},"10204":{"id":"/en/docs/development-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#page-map","content":"If you are new to the code, read Development environment → Architecture → the layer relevant to your work.","locale":"en"},"10205":{"id":"/en/docs/development-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"RVC Next is a rewrite of Retrieval-based-Voice-Conversion-WebUI (called “the original” below, based on the local checkout at `81eed5e`, a heavily modified 2026 branch that replaces fairseq with `transformers` HuBERT, replaces UVR5 with PyMSS, and adds CUDA Graphs, multi-speaker training and a VST plugin). The original spreads its features across five entry points: the Gradio WebUI, a desktop live voice conversion GUI, a VST plugin, CLI scripts for each training stage, and the bundled PyMSS CLI. Each has its own settings, model selection and progress display. The rewrite combines them into one application: **Convert**, **Live**, **Separate**, **Train** and **Models**, behind one FastAPI server, one Vue 3 Web UI and one Typer CLI.","locale":"en"},"10206":{"id":"/en/docs/development-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"The code has three sources, each handled differently:","locale":"en"},"10207":{"id":"/en/docs/development-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"10208":{"id":"/en/docs/development-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"What was taken","locale":"en"},"10209":{"id":"/en/docs/development-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"How it was handled","locale":"en"},"10210":{"id":"/en/docs/development-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"SD Model Hub (via Hanaikada)","locale":"en"},"10211":{"id":"/en/docs/development-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Application skeleton: settings, event bus, SQLite database, security middleware, port binding, CLI factory, Web UI theme, `ui/` component library, motion system and rule tests","locale":"en"},"10212":{"id":"/en/docs/development-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Renamed and reused; Hanaikada's `embed.py` (embedding in other applications) was left out because no host application needs to embed RVC Next","locale":"en"},"10213":{"id":"/en/docs/development-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Original RVC","locale":"en"},"10214":{"id":"/en/docs/development-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Synthesizer and discriminator networks, RMVPE, TorchGate, CUDA Graph cache, numerical code for offline / streaming / training pipelines","locale":"en"},"10215":{"id":"/en/docs/development-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"**Ported rather than rewritten**, with golden tests comparing against the original bit for bit so existing voices sound exactly the same (see Parity with the original)","locale":"en"},"10216":{"id":"/en/docs/development-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"torchaudio, torchfcpe","locale":"en"},"10217":{"id":"/en/docs/development-58","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"The windowed sinc resampler in `transforms.Resample`; FCPE inference path (mel frontend, convolution-only `CFNaiveMelPE`, decoders and loader)","locale":"en"},"10218":{"id":"/en/docs/development-59","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Ported step by step to `engine/audio/sinc_resample.py` and `engine/f0/fcpe_model.py`; tests verify bit-identical results when the original libraries are installed. RVC Next therefore no longer depends on torchaudio (whose final release is 2.11) or torchfcpe","locale":"en"},"10219":{"id":"/en/docs/development-60","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#project-origins","content":"Orchestration, storage, process control and all user interfaces were written from scratch.","locale":"en"},"10220":{"id":"/en/docs/development-61","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"RVC Next is released under **GPL-3.0-only** (`LICENSE`, `license = \"GPL-3.0-only\"` in `pyproject.toml`), because its skeleton comes from the GPLv3 projects SD Model Hub and Hanaikada. Ported code retains its original licence notices, collected in `NOTICE`:","locale":"en"},"10221":{"id":"/en/docs/development-62","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"Original RVC: MIT;","locale":"en"},"10222":{"id":"/en/docs/development-63","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"torchaudio: BSD 2-Clause, with the full text also retained in `engine/audio/sinc_resample.py`;","locale":"en"},"10223":{"id":"/en/docs/development-64","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"FCPE / torchfcpe: MIT (its conformer comes from Diffusion-SVC, also MIT);","locale":"en"},"10224":{"id":"/en/docs/development-65","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"PyMSS is used as a dependency (MIT); sources for RMVPE, DDSP-SVC's SOLA crossfade and TorchGate are also credited there.","locale":"en"},"10225":{"id":"/en/docs/development-66","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#licence","content":"Model weights downloaded at runtime (HuBERT, RMVPE, FCPE, base models, separation models and demo voices) have their own terms and are outside this repository's licence. When porting new code, record its source and licence both in the file header and in `NOTICE`.","locale":"en"},"10226":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"page","content":"First run","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run","locale":"en"},"10227":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-0","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run","content":"After installing RVC Next, follow the entire first-run process: start the web interface, learn where data is stored, download HuBERT and RMVPE for conversion, get a demo voice and complete a conversion. Each step includes both web interface and command-line instructions.","locale":"en"},"10228":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-1","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Start the web interface","locale":"en"},"10229":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-2","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Data folder","locale":"en"},"10230":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-3","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Download HuBERT and RMVPE","locale":"en"},"10231":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-4","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"Get a demo voice","locale":"en"},"10232":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-5","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Complete your first conversion","locale":"en"},"10233":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-6","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Next steps","locale":"en"},"10234":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-7","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Run this in a terminal with the RVC Next environment activated:","locale":"en"},"10235":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-8","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Once the server starts, the terminal prints a line like:","locale":"en"},"10236":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-9","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"The browser will open this address automatically shortly afterward. The default port is **7868** (separate from the original RVC's 7865). To stop the server, press ctrl+c in the terminal.","locale":"en"},"10237":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-10","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Common options for `rvc-next webui`:","locale":"en"},"10238":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-11","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"10239":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-12","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10240":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-13","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--port <port>`","locale":"en"},"10241":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-14","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"First port to try, read from settings by default (7868); `0` picks any free port","locale":"en"},"10242":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-15","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--strict-port` / `--no-strict-port`","locale":"en"},"10243":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-16","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Fail instead of trying the next port when it is occupied (by default, it tries the next port and reports the port actually used)","locale":"en"},"10244":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-17","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--open` / `--no-open`","locale":"en"},"10245":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-18","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Open the web UI in a browser automatically (enabled by default; configurable in settings)","locale":"en"},"10246":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-19","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--host <address>`","locale":"en"},"10247":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-20","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Address to bind; defaults to `127.0.0.1`, allowing access only from the local machine","locale":"en"},"10248":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-21","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--data-dir <directory>`","locale":"en"},"10249":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-22","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Data directory for this run","locale":"en"},"10250":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-23","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"`--debug`","locale":"en"},"10251":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-24","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Print debug logs","locale":"en"},"10252":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-25","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"If you set `--host` to a non-local address such as `0.0.0.0`, other devices on the local network can access the server without an access token. Anyone who can connect can use every feature, so do this only on a trusted network or add protection of your own, such as a firewall or a VPN; you can also set an optional access token with `rvc-next config set server.access_token <secret>`. See Remote access and security.","locale":"en"},"10253":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-26","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#start-the-web-interface","content":"Once the page opens, you will see the navigation bar on the left (at the bottom in narrow windows): **Convert**, **Live**, **Separate**, **Train**, **Models**, and **Settings** at the bottom. The first visit opens **Convert**; subsequent visits return to the page you last used. See Interface overview for explanations of each part of the interface.","locale":"en"},"10254":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-27","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Settings, the database, voice library, training experiments, conversion results and downloaded models are all stored in a **data folder**:","locale":"en"},"10255":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-28","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"System","locale":"en"},"10256":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-29","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Default location","locale":"en"},"10257":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-30","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"10258":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-31","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`%APPDATA%\\rvc-next`","locale":"en"},"10259":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-32","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"10260":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-33","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`~/Library/Application Support/rvc-next`","locale":"en"},"10261":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-34","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10262":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-35","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`$XDG_DATA_HOME/rvc-next`; `~/.local/share/rvc-next` when `XDG_DATA_HOME` is unset","locale":"en"},"10263":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-36","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Set the `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` environment variable to use another location (or specify it with `rvc-next webui --data-dir`). `rvc-next doctor` shows the current data folder; you can also find it in **Settings › About**.","locale":"en"},"10264":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-37","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"The main contents are:","locale":"en"},"10265":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-38","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"10266":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-39","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"10267":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-40","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`settings.toml`","locale":"en"},"10268":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-41","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Settings file (`rvc-next config path` prints its path)","locale":"en"},"10269":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-42","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`rvc-next.db`","locale":"en"},"10270":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-43","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Database: voice library cache and records of jobs and results","locale":"en"},"10271":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-44","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`models/`","locale":"en"},"10272":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-45","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Voice library (`models/voices/<voice>/`), base models, separation models, etc.","locale":"en"},"10273":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-46","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`assets/`","locale":"en"},"10274":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-47","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Downloaded HuBERT, RMVPE, base model and separation model weights","locale":"en"},"10275":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-48","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`experiments/`","locale":"en"},"10276":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-49","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Training experiments","locale":"en"},"10277":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-50","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`outputs/`","locale":"en"},"10278":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-51","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Conversion and separation results, in folders by date and job","locale":"en"},"10279":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-52","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"`jobs/`","locale":"en"},"10280":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-53","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"Logs for each job","locale":"en"},"10281":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-54","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#data-folder","content":"You can move the voice, experiment, result and asset folders elsewhere in **Settings › Storage**. See Configuration and environment variables for more configuration methods.","locale":"en"},"10282":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-55","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Conversion needs two foundational models:","locale":"en"},"10283":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-56","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"**HuBERT** (about 180 MB): extracts speech content features; required for every conversion;","locale":"en"},"10284":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-57","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"**RMVPE** (about 173 MB): the default pitch method; required when converting with a voice that has pitch guidance.","locale":"en"},"10285":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-58","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"There are also optional pitch models, needed only when you select their method: **FCPE** (about 41 MB), **CREPE** (about 85 MB) and **CREPE tiny** (about 2 MB). The `pm` and **SwiftF0** methods need no download (SwiftF0's small model comes with RVC Next).","locale":"en"},"10286":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-59","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Choose any of these download methods:","locale":"en"},"10287":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-60","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"RVC Next keeps missing models from causing errors. Whenever an operation on a page needs a model that has not been downloaded, its button is replaced by a notice such as “**Needs HuBERT, RMVPE**”, with a **Download (353 MB)** button beside it. Click once to start downloading. Progress appears in the same place, and the original button returns automatically when the download finishes.","locale":"en"},"10288":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-61","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Click **Models** in the navigation bar and switch to the **Assets** tab.","locale":"en"},"10289":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-62","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"In the **Conversion** group, click **Download everything for Conversion**, or click **Download** on the individual HuBERT and RMVPE rows.","locale":"en"},"10290":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-63","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Each row shows download progress, downloaded/total size, speed and time remaining; when complete, its status becomes **Installed**.","locale":"en"},"10291":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-64","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"For installed files, click **Verify** to check their SHA-256 again.","locale":"en"},"10292":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-65","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"Downloads support resuming, retry automatically on failure and verify SHA-256 on completion. By default, they use the licyk/rvc-model repository on Hugging Face. If accessing Hugging Face is difficult, change **Download endpoint** to **hf-mirror.com** in **Settings › Downloads**, or use the command line:","locale":"en"},"10293":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-66","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#download-hubert-and-rmvpe","content":"You can reuse models already downloaded in the original's `assets/` without downloading them again. See Migrating from the original RVC.","locale":"en"},"10294":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-67","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"The voice library starts empty. RVC Next can download the official RVC demo voices, together with their indexes, in one click for you to try:","locale":"en"},"10295":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-68","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"Click **Models**, switch to the **Assets** tab and scroll to the **Demo voices** group.","locale":"en"},"10296":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-69","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"If the **Voices** tab shows “No voices yet”, its **Get the demo voices** button also takes you here.","locale":"en"},"10297":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-70","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"Each row shows the sample rate, version, whether it is **with index**, and size. Click **Download** on the voice you want, or **Download all** at the top right of the group.","locale":"en"},"10298":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-71","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"When the download finishes, the row shows **Installed** and an **In library** button; click it to open the voice's details. The voice also appears in **Models › Voices**.","locale":"en"},"10299":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-72","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"The catalog currently contains `kikiV1`, `keruanV1`, `guanguanV1` (v1, 40 kHz), `zhanzhanv2-xi` (v2, 40 kHz) and `youzhanv2-xi` (v2, 48 kHz; no index was officially released for it).","locale":"en"},"10300":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-73","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#get-a-demo-voice","content":"You can drag your own `.pth` models directly into the import area at the top of **Models › Voices**; see Model management.","locale":"en"},"10301":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-74","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Click **Convert** in the navigation bar.","locale":"en"},"10302":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-75","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"In **Inputs**, drag an audio file onto “Drop audio files here”, or click it to choose a file. WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG and other formats are supported. The file uploads to the server; once uploaded, click the play button on the left to listen.","locale":"en"},"10303":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-76","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Click the voice picker (showing “Choose a voice”) and select the demo voice you just downloaded from the list. Its sample rate, version and whether it has **pitch guidance** appear beneath the picker.","locale":"en"},"10304":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-77","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Adjust **Voice parameters**. For your first conversion, focus only on **Pitch**:","locale":"en"},"10305":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-78","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"For a male voice to a female voice model, use around **+12**; for a female voice to a male voice model, use around **−12**;","locale":"en"},"10306":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-79","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"For conversion between voices of the same gender, keep **0**.","locale":"en"},"10307":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-80","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Leave the other parameters at their defaults for now; see Voice parameters for their meanings.","locale":"en"},"10308":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-81","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Check the fixed action bar at the bottom of the page. If it shows “**Needs HuBERT, RMVPE**”, click **Download** first and wait for it to finish.","locale":"en"},"10309":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-82","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Click **Preview 15 s** first to convert only the first 15 seconds and hear the result in a few seconds. Once satisfied, click **Convert** to process the whole file.","locale":"en"},"10310":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-83","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"A job card appears in the action bar, showing status and progress. Once complete, the output appears in **Results**:","locale":"en"},"10311":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-84","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Click play to listen, or click the waveform to jump to a position;","locale":"en"},"10312":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-85","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Use the **Result / Source** toggle to compare the original and converted audio at the same position;","locale":"en"},"10313":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-86","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Click **More actions** (⋮) on the right to **Download** the file.","locale":"en"},"10314":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-87","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Result files are saved in `outputs/<date>/<job id>/` in the data folder, with names in the form `<original name>.<voice>.<format>`, such as `song.kikiv1.wav`; preview filenames include `.preview`.","locale":"en"},"10315":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-88","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"To perform the same conversion from the command line:","locale":"en"},"10316":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-89","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#complete-your-first-conversion","content":"Converting a song with accompaniment directly usually gives poor results. On the **Convert** page, expand **Optional steps** and enable **Separate first** and **Add accompaniment back** to perform “separate vocals → convert → mix accompaniment back in” in one operation. See Conversion.","locale":"en"},"10317":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-90","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Learn the interface layout, jobs and results list: Interface overview","locale":"en"},"10318":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-91","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Learn more about each page: User guide","locale":"en"},"10319":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-92","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Batch process from the command line: Command line","locale":"en"},"10320":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-93","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Encountered a problem? FAQ","locale":"en"},"10321":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"page","content":"Conversion","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","locale":"en"},"10322":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"The Convert page changes audio files to the selected voice. It handles single files, multiple files or an entire folder, and can separate vocals before conversion and add the accompaniment back afterward to make a song cover in one operation.","locale":"en"},"10323":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#inputs","content":"Add inputs","locale":"en"},"10324":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#drop-or-select-files","content":"Drop or select files","locale":"en"},"10325":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"Server files","locale":"en"},"10326":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#earlier-results","content":"Earlier results","locale":"en"},"10327":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#tts","content":"Text to speech","locale":"en"},"10328":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#manage-the-input-list","content":"Manage the input list","locale":"en"},"10329":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"Choose a voice","locale":"en"},"10330":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#adjust-voice-parameters","content":"Adjust voice parameters","locale":"en"},"10331":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#optional-steps","content":"Optional steps","locale":"en"},"10332":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Separate first","locale":"en"},"10333":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#output","content":"Output","locale":"en"},"10334":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"Effects","locale":"en"},"10335":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Preview and convert","locale":"en"},"10336":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"Jobs","locale":"en"},"10337":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#results","content":"Results","locale":"en"},"10338":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#where-files-are-saved-and-how-they-are-named","content":"Where files are saved and how they are named","locale":"en"},"10339":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"Batch conversion","locale":"en"},"10340":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"The page has three sections from top to bottom, with a fixed action bar at the bottom:","locale":"en"},"10341":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"**Inputs**: audio to convert;","locale":"en"},"10342":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"Voice picker, **Voice parameters** and collapsed **Optional steps**;","locale":"en"},"10343":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"**Results**: results produced on this page in the current session;","locale":"en"},"10344":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert","content":"Bottom action bar: job cards, **Preview 15 s** and **Convert** buttons.","locale":"en"},"10345":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#inputs","content":"The **Inputs** section offers three ways to add audio, which you can combine:","locale":"en"},"10346":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#drop-or-select-files","content":"Drag files onto “Drop audio files here”, or click the area to choose files in a dialog; you can select several at once. Common audio formats (WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG, OPUS, AAC, WMA, etc.) are supported. You can also drop video files directly; their audio track will be used.","locale":"en"},"10347":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#drop-or-select-files","content":"Files upload to the server, with upload progress beneath each file. Once uploaded, a play button appears on the left and the duration on the right. Failed uploads show “Could not upload …” and the reason.","locale":"en"},"10348":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"When browser and server are on the same computer (or the server has an access token set), a **Server files** button appears. It uses files directly from the server's disk, **without uploading**, making it suitable for large files or large numbers of files:","locale":"en"},"10349":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"Click **Server files**; the dialog first lists the **Folders** you can browse.","locale":"en"},"10350":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"Click a folder to enter it, or **Up** to go back. The dialog lists only folders and audio files.","locale":"en"},"10351":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"Select the files you want and click **Add N**; or click **Add this folder** within a folder to add the entire folder as one input.","locale":"en"},"10352":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"When a folder is an input, conversion processes all audio files at its **top level**, excluding subfolders.","locale":"en"},"10353":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#server-files","content":"By default, browsable folders include your home folder, added original RVC installations, the data folder and each disk partition. Change them in **Folders the browser may open** under **Settings › Storage** (one per line).","locale":"en"},"10354":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#earlier-results","content":"Click **Earlier results** to select from all historical results (including other pages and earlier sessions), then click **Add N** to add them as inputs. For example, convert vocals produced by **Separate**, or convert a conversion result again.","locale":"en"},"10355":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#tts","content":"Click **Text to speech** to type text and have an online voice speak it; the speech is added as an input, ready to convert to your voice (Applio's TTS tab). Choose the **Language** and **Speaker** (Microsoft Edge's read-aloud voices, over 300 in about 140 languages; the last speaker is remembered), and adjust **Speed** (−50 to +100 %) and **Pitch** (−50 to +50 Hz) if needed. Up to 5000 characters at a time.","locale":"en"},"10356":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#tts","content":"The text is sent to Microsoft's speech service over the internet; nothing is sent until you click **Add**.","locale":"en"},"10357":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#tts","content":"The server needs `pip install \"rvc-next[tts]\"` (edge-tts); without it the dialog says so.","locale":"en"},"10358":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#tts","content":"On the command line: `rvc-next tts speak \"text\" --voice en-US-AriaNeural -o hello.mp3`, then convert `hello.mp3` (`tts`).","locale":"en"},"10359":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#manage-the-input-list","content":"Click the play button on the left of each item to listen;","locale":"en"},"10360":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#manage-the-input-list","content":"Click **Remove** (×) on the right to remove an item;","locale":"en"},"10361":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#manage-the-input-list","content":"With more than one input, click **Clear** to remove them all at once.","locale":"en"},"10362":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"Click the voice picker (showing “Choose a voice” when nothing is selected) to open the voice list:","locale":"en"},"10363":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"**Search voices** at the top filters by name or tag;","locale":"en"},"10364":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"Each voice shows its sample rate, version (v1/v2), **pitch guidance** or **no pitch guidance**, and speaker count for multi-speaker voices;","locale":"en"},"10365":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"Voices without an index have a **no index** label; voices from an original RVC installation (read directly, without copying into the library) have a **legacy** label.","locale":"en"},"10366":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"If the voice library is empty, this shows “No voices yet” and an **Open Models** button. See Model management for importing and downloading voices.","locale":"en"},"10367":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"**Multi-speaker voices** add a **Speaker** dropdown beneath the picker, where you choose the speaker to use. Selecting a new voice automatically selects its first speaker.","locale":"en"},"10368":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#choose-a-voice","content":"When you select a voice, **Voice parameters** loads that voice's default preset automatically, so the same voice sounds consistent in conversion and live voice conversion. RVC Next remembers the last voice you selected on this page.","locale":"en"},"10369":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#adjust-voice-parameters","content":"The **Voice parameters** panel contains **Pitch method**, **Pitch**, **Formant**, **Index strength**, **Consonant protection** and **Loudness match**. The **Presets** menu at the top right applies or saves presets. On Convert, the panel says “Changes apply to the next conversion.” Click **Preview 15 s** or **Convert** after editing to use the new values.","locale":"en"},"10370":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#adjust-voice-parameters","content":"See Voice parameters for each parameter's meaning, range, default and adjustment tips. **Pitch** is the most commonly adjusted: around +12 for a male voice to a female voice model, or −12 for a female voice to a male voice model.","locale":"en"},"10371":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#optional-steps","content":"Expand **Optional steps** to configure the following.","locale":"en"},"10372":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Enable **Separate first** (described as “Convert only the vocals of a song.”) to split the audio with a separation model before conversion and convert only the vocals. This reveals:","locale":"en"},"10373":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"**Preset**: the separation preset to use, defaulting to **Vocals**. See Vocal separation for differences between presets.","locale":"en"},"10374":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"**Add accompaniment back**: mix the converted vocals over the separated accompaniment to output a complete song.","locale":"en"},"10375":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"**Accompaniment level**: accompaniment gain when adding it back, from −24 to +12 dB, default 0 dB. Lower it if the accompaniment overwhelms the vocals, or raise it for the opposite.","locale":"en"},"10376":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Keep in mind:","locale":"en"},"10377":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Conversion uses the preset's “primary stem”: `vocals` for **Vocals** and **Vocals, aggressive**, lead vocals `main_vocal` for **Lead vocal** and **Lead vocal, clean**, and dereverberated `vocals` for **Vocals, clean**.","locale":"en"},"10378":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"The “accompaniment” added back is preferably the `instrumental` stem; if the preset has no accompaniment stem, the other stem is used. For example, with **Remove reverb**, the separated reverb is added back, equivalent to “convert the dry vocals, then add the original reverb back”.","locale":"en"},"10379":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Adding accompaniment back produces stereo output; if mixing would clip, the overall level is automatically lowered to prevent clipping.","locale":"en"},"10380":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Intermediate separated stems are deleted after conversion. If you also need these stems, use the Vocal separation page first, then send the vocals to Convert.","locale":"en"},"10381":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#separate-first","content":"Enabling **Separate first** adds the selected preset's separation models to the required-download check. Separation models are large (300–440 MB each).","locale":"en"},"10382":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#output","content":"**Format**: WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A or OGG (Opus, a small file; always 48 kHz). The default comes from **Result format** under **Settings › Training defaults** (initially WAV).","locale":"en"},"10383":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#output","content":"**Sample rate**: defaults to **The voice's own** (for example, a 40 kHz voice outputs 40 kHz); you can also choose 22.05, 32, 40, 44.1 or 48 kHz, and the result is resampled to that rate.","locale":"en"},"10384":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#output","content":"**Noise reduction**: 0–1, default 0 (off). Removes hiss and background noise from the converted voice with a spectral gate that follows the noise as it changes (Applio's \"clean audio\"); higher values remove more and can dull the voice.","locale":"en"},"10385":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"**Effects** under **Output** add a chain of studio effects to the converted voice, applied top to bottom, before the accompaniment is added back: high-pass and low-pass filters, noise gate, compressor, pitch shift, distortion, bitcrusher, clipping, chorus, phaser, delay, reverb, gain and limiter (the plugins of Spotify's pedalboard, as Applio's post-processing uses them, but in any order and as many as 16). **Add effect** appends one with its default settings; each one's sliders show its parameters, and the arrows and the bin move and remove it.","locale":"en"},"10386":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"A reverb or delay rings out past the end of the voice: the result is longer by its audible tail.","locale":"en"},"10387":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"The limiter also raises the level as it limits (pedalboard's limiter has make-up gain); put a **Gain** before it to aim it.","locale":"en"},"10388":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"The server needs `pip install \"rvc-next[effects]\"`; without it the section says so and a conversion with effects is refused.","locale":"en"},"10389":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#effects","content":"The effects are not stored in presets; the command line takes them as `--effect` (`convert`).","locale":"en"},"10390":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"The bottom action bar has two buttons:","locale":"en"},"10391":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Button","locale":"en"},"10392":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10393":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"**Preview 15 s**","locale":"en"},"10394":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Convert only the first 15 seconds of each input. Preview jobs go ahead of other queued jobs, making them useful for trying parameters quickly. Results have a **preview** label and `.preview` in the filename","locale":"en"},"10395":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"**Convert**","locale":"en"},"10396":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Convert every input in full","locale":"en"},"10397":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"When buttons are unavailable, the left side explains why: “Choose a voice.” or “Add audio to convert.” You also cannot start while inputs are still uploading. If required models are missing (HuBERT, the selected pitch method's model, separation models), the buttons are replaced by “**Needs …**” and a **Download** button; see Interface overview.","locale":"en"},"10398":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Recommended workflow:","locale":"en"},"10399":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Add inputs, choose a voice and set **Pitch**;","locale":"en"},"10400":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Click **Preview 15 s** and compare using **Result / Source** in **Results**;","locale":"en"},"10401":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Adjust parameters based on the result (see Voice parameters) and preview again;","locale":"en"},"10402":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#preview-and-convert","content":"Once satisfied, click **Convert**.","locale":"en"},"10403":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"Each click on **Convert** (or **Preview 15 s**) creates **one** job containing all current inputs. Its card appears in the bottom action bar:","locale":"en"},"10404":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"Titles look like `Convert song.wav · kikiV1`, or `Convert song.wav and 4 more · kikiV1` for multiple inputs; previews use `Preview ……`;","locale":"en"},"10405":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"With **Separate first** enabled, the first step is `Separate` (processing all inputs at once), followed by one step per input;","locale":"en"},"10406":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"You can **Cancel** at any time, or **Retry** after failure, cancellation or interruption. Click **Log** for details. For example, if the voice has no index and **Index strength** is above 0, the log records `No index for this voice; index strength has no effect`.","locale":"en"},"10407":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#jobs","content":"After clicking, you can continue changing parameters or inputs and submit again; the new job is queued afterward. See Interface overview › Jobs for general information about jobs.","locale":"en"},"10408":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#results","content":"Completed outputs appear in **Results**, labeled **converted**, **remix** (accompaniment added back) or **preview**. See Interface overview › Results list for playback, waveform seeking, **Result / Source** comparison and the **More actions** menu. Two actions are especially useful here:","locale":"en"},"10409":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#results","content":"**Use as input**: add the result back to this page's inputs, for example to process a conversion result again;","locale":"en"},"10410":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#results","content":"**Re-run with these settings**: restore the voice and parameters used to generate the result and add its source file back to the inputs, making it easy to fine-tune from earlier settings.","locale":"en"},"10411":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#where-files-are-saved-and-how-they-are-named","content":"Results are saved in `outputs/<date>/<job id>/` in the data folder (you can change the results folder in **Settings › Storage**). The filename pattern is:","locale":"en"},"10412":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#where-files-are-saved-and-how-they-are-named","content":"For example, converting `song.flac` with `kikiV1` to WAV produces `song.kikiv1.wav`. The voice name is lowercased, spaces and symbols become `-`, and text such as Chinese characters is preserved. A preview is named `song.kikiv1.preview.wav`.","locale":"en"},"10413":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#where-files-are-saved-and-how-they-are-named","content":"RVC Next **never overwrites existing files**: if a filename already exists (for example, both `song.wav` and `song.flac` are in the same batch), a number is appended automatically, such as `song.kikiv1_1.wav`.","locale":"en"},"10414":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#where-files-are-saved-and-how-they-are-named","content":"Results are kept indefinitely by default. To clean up old results automatically, set “Delete results after days (0: keep)” in **Settings › Storage**.","locale":"en"},"10415":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"There are several ways to convert many files at once:","locale":"en"},"10416":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"**Select or drop multiple files**: they are converted sequentially in one job;","locale":"en"},"10417":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"**Add a folder**: use **Add this folder** in **Server files** to convert all audio files at the folder's top level;","locale":"en"},"10418":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"**Use the command line**: recurse into subfolders and specify an output folder.","locale":"en"},"10419":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"The command line starts from the voice's default preset. Use `--preset` to choose another preset, then override individual values with `--pitch`, `--index-rate`, etc. `--overwrite` can overwrite matching filenames only when you specify an output folder with `-o`. See Command reference for all options.","locale":"en"},"10420":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-convert-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-convert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-convert#batch-conversion","content":"Conversion uses the **Device** selected in **Settings › Compute**. The default is **Automatic**: select a GPU using the original RVC's rules, or use CPU if no suitable GPU is available. Conversion results on CPU are bit-identical to the original.","locale":"en"},"10421":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"page","content":"Interface overview","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface","locale":"en"},"10422":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface","content":"The overall layout of the RVC Next web interface and the parts shared across pages: navigation, top bar, bottom action bar, job cards, results list and handoffs between pages. Learning these makes the guides for individual pages much easier to follow.","locale":"en"},"10423":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#overall-layout","content":"Overall layout","locale":"en"},"10424":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#what-is-kept-when-switching-pages","content":"What is kept when switching pages","locale":"en"},"10425":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"Page structure","locale":"en"},"10426":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#missing-models","content":"When models are missing","locale":"en"},"10427":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#when-an-error-occurs","content":"When an error occurs","locale":"en"},"10428":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs","content":"Jobs","locale":"en"},"10429":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Job cards","locale":"en"},"10430":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs-sheet-and-jobs-page","content":"Jobs sheet and jobs page","locale":"en"},"10431":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Results list","locale":"en"},"10432":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Handoffs between pages","locale":"en"},"10433":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#other-top-bar-buttons","content":"Other top-bar buttons","locale":"en"},"10434":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#gpu-memory","content":"GPU memory","locale":"en"},"10435":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#theme","content":"Theme","locale":"en"},"10436":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#live-status-chip","content":"Live status chip","locale":"en"},"10437":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#access-token","content":"Access token","locale":"en"},"10438":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"Keyboard controls","locale":"en"},"10439":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#overall-layout","content":"The interface has three parts:","locale":"en"},"10440":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#overall-layout","content":"**Navigation**: in wider windows, a vertical bar on the left lists **Convert**, **Live**, **Separate**, **Train** and **Models**, with **Settings** at the bottom. Below 600 pixels wide (for example, on a phone or in a narrow window), navigation moves to the bottom as a row of six buttons.","locale":"en"},"10441":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#overall-layout","content":"**Top bar**: the application name **RVC Next** always appears on the left; the right contains the live status chip (only while live voice conversion is running), jobs button, GPU memory button and theme button.","locale":"en"},"10442":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#overall-layout","content":"**Content area**: the current page. Only this area fades in and out when switching pages; navigation and the top bar stay still.","locale":"en"},"10443":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#what-is-kept-when-switching-pages","content":"Each page **stays as you left it**: added inputs, selected voice, adjusted parameters and scroll position are preserved, so you can resume when you return.","locale":"en"},"10444":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#what-is-kept-when-switching-pages","content":"Navigation buttons return to your last location within that page. For example, if you open an experiment in **Train**, switch to **Convert**, then click **Train**, you return to that experiment.","locale":"en"},"10445":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#what-is-kept-when-switching-pages","content":"**Refreshing the browser resets** all temporary page state. Only actual preferences are saved: theme, last page, last voice selected in **Convert**, last preset selected in **Separate**, etc. These preferences are stored on the server, so they are the same in another browser.","locale":"en"},"10446":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"Pages such as **Convert**, **Separate** and **Live** share the same structure:","locale":"en"},"10447":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"**One column of sections**: arranged from top to bottom. For example, **Convert** contains **Inputs**, a voice and **Voice parameters**, then **Results**. Each section fills the page width, and its fields wrap automatically to fit.","locale":"en"},"10448":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"**Bottom action bar**: fixed at the bottom of the page and visible wherever you scroll. It contains:","locale":"en"},"10449":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"Errors from this page;","locale":"en"},"10450":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"Cards for unfinished jobs started from this page (scrollable when there are multiple jobs);","locale":"en"},"10451":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#page-structure","content":"Run buttons such as **Preview 15 s** and **Convert**. When unavailable, a short line on the left explains why, such as “Add audio to convert.” or “Choose a voice.”","locale":"en"},"10452":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#missing-models","content":"If a model needed for the current operation has not been downloaded, the run button in the action bar is replaced by a notice such as “**Needs HuBERT, RMVPE**” and a **Download (353 MB)** button. Clicking shows download progress in place; the run button returns automatically when the download finishes. You do not need to remember which files each feature requires beforehand.","locale":"en"},"10453":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#when-an-error-occurs","content":"Errors appear where they occur (in the action bar, a job card or a dialog). The title is the translated error type (for example, “A required model file is not installed” or “The GPU is not available or ran out of memory”), followed by the server's specific message (in English). When more information is available, a **Details** button opens the full content, which you can include in a problem report.","locale":"en"},"10454":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs","content":"Time-consuming operations such as conversion, separation, training, downloads, merging and extraction run as **jobs** on the server. Jobs are queued in the background without blocking the interface; they continue running even if you close the browser tab.","locale":"en"},"10455":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Job cards appear in the action bar of the page that started them and in the **Jobs** sheet. Each card shows:","locale":"en"},"10456":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Title**: generated by the server, currently in English, such as `Convert song.wav · kikiV1` or `Preview song.wav · kikiV1`;","locale":"en"},"10457":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Status**: **Queued**, **Waiting** (specifically **Waiting for the GPU**, **Waiting for the CPU** or **Waiting for a download**), **Running**, **Cancelling**, **Cancelled**, **Failed**, **Done** or **Interrupted**;","locale":"en"},"10458":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"The current step and the completed step count for multi-step jobs, such as `2/5`;","locale":"en"},"10459":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"A progress bar while running; download jobs also show downloaded/total size, speed and time remaining.","locale":"en"},"10460":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Buttons on the right of the card:","locale":"en"},"10461":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Button","locale":"en"},"10462":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10463":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Cancel** (×)","locale":"en"},"10464":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Stop an unfinished job","locale":"en"},"10465":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Retry** (↻)","locale":"en"},"10466":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Run the exact same request again; available for **Failed**, **Cancelled** and **Interrupted** jobs","locale":"en"},"10467":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Log**","locale":"en"},"10468":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"Expand or collapse this job's log inside the card; once opened, the button becomes **Hide log**","locale":"en"},"10469":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"A few special cases:","locale":"en"},"10470":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Interrupted**: if the server shuts down while a job is running, the job is marked interrupted at the next startup. Its request is saved, so you can **Retry** directly.","locale":"en"},"10471":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Run anyway**: while live voice conversion is using the GPU, new GPU jobs wait. The card shows “Live is using the GPU. Running both may cause audio glitches.” and offers a **Run anyway** button.","locale":"en"},"10472":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#job-cards","content":"**Preview priority**: preview jobs go ahead of other queued jobs to deliver results sooner.","locale":"en"},"10473":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs-sheet-and-jobs-page","content":"Click **Jobs** in the top bar to open the **Jobs** sheet. When no jobs are running, the button shows a checklist icon; while jobs are running, the icon spins and a badge shows the running job count (the tooltip reads “N running”).","locale":"en"},"10474":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs-sheet-and-jobs-page","content":"The sheet lists jobs from all pages: jobs started in this session (with live progress) come first, followed by recent history recorded by the server, up to 30 jobs. Click **All jobs** at the top right to open the full jobs page, where you can filter by **All**, **Active** or **Finished**, or click **Clear finished**.","locale":"en"},"10475":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#jobs-sheet-and-jobs-page","content":"When a job started on another page finishes or fails, a notification appears at the bottom of the screen, such as “… finished”. Failure notifications include an **Open log** button that opens the jobs sheet.","locale":"en"},"10476":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Convert** and **Separate** (and **Test** in voice details) use the same **Results** list. It shows only results from jobs **started on this page in the current session**, newest first. Refreshing the browser clears the list, but the files remain and can be found again through **Earlier results** in the input section.","locale":"en"},"10477":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Each result occupies one row, with:","locale":"en"},"10478":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"A **Play** button: all results share one player, so playing one stops the other;","locale":"en"},"10479":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Filename, type label (**converted**, **remix**, **stem**, **preview**), stem name (such as `vocals`) and duration;","locale":"en"},"10480":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Waveform**: shows playback progress; click to jump to a position;","locale":"en"},"10481":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Result / Source** toggle: switch between converted and original audio at the same playback position for A/B comparison;","locale":"en"},"10482":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**More actions** (⋮) menu.","locale":"en"},"10483":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Items in the **More actions** menu:","locale":"en"},"10484":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"10485":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10486":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"When available","locale":"en"},"10487":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Download**","locale":"en"},"10488":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Download the file to the computer running the browser","locale":"en"},"10489":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"10490":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Show in folder**","locale":"en"},"10491":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Locate the file in the server computer's file manager","locale":"en"},"10492":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"When browser and server are on the same computer","locale":"en"},"10493":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Use as input**","locale":"en"},"10494":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Add this result to the current page's inputs for another pass","locale":"en"},"10495":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"10496":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Analyse**","locale":"en"},"10497":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Open its spectrogram and pitch curve, beside its source's (see below)","locale":"en"},"10498":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"10499":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Convert this**","locale":"en"},"10500":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Send this stem to **Convert**","locale":"en"},"10501":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Stem results","locale":"en"},"10502":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Re-run with these settings**","locale":"en"},"10503":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Restore the voice and parameters used to generate it on **Convert**, and add its source file back to the inputs","locale":"en"},"10504":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Conversion results","locale":"en"},"10505":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Delete**","locale":"en"},"10506":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Move the file to the system trash and remove its record","locale":"en"},"10507":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"10508":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"**Analyse** opens a window with the result's **spectrogram** (time left to right, frequency bottom to top, brighter is louder) and its **pitch** curve, with the source's when the result has one: **Result** and **Source** switch the spectrogram, and the pitch chart draws both. It also lists the duration, format and median pitch, and how many semitones the result sits from the source. A spectrogram shows what the ears have to search for: a voice's sample rate as the top of its sound (a 32k voice stops at 16 kHz), hiss and buzz as haze, and separation bleed as the accompaniment's pattern. The pitch curve shows octave jumps and how a parameter moved the pitch. The pitch comes from SwiftF0 on the processor, so analysing never waits for the GPU; files over 30 minutes are not analysed. On the command line: `rvc-next analyse <file> [--csv curve.csv]`.","locale":"en"},"10509":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#results","content":"When there is more than one result, **Download all** appears at the top right of the list to download them as a zip.","locale":"en"},"10510":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Audio and voices can pass directly between pages without downloading and uploading them again:","locale":"en"},"10511":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Choose **Convert this** on a **Separate** result: the stem is added to **Convert**'s inputs, and the interface switches to **Convert** automatically.","locale":"en"},"10512":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Click **Earlier results** in any page's input section: select results from the full history to add as inputs.","locale":"en"},"10513":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Click **Try** on a checkpoint in **Train**: a temporary voice is generated from the checkpoint, and **Convert** opens with that voice selected so you can try the training result directly.","locale":"en"},"10514":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#handoffs-between-pages","content":"Choose **Re-run with these settings** on a **Convert** result: restore the voice and parameters used at the time.","locale":"en"},"10515":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#gpu-memory","content":"The memory-module icon in the top bar shows GPU memory usage. Hover over it to see “GPU memory: used of total · Loaded: …” (or the device in use when there is no GPU). Its badge shows the number of models currently loaded in memory.","locale":"en"},"10516":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#gpu-memory","content":"Click to open a menu with one item, **Free GPU memory**: unload all cached models, including HuBERT, voices and pitch models, and have PyTorch return GPU memory. It is available whenever no jobs or live voice conversion are running; otherwise, it is disabled and shows the reason, such as “Free GPU memory (wait: a job is running)”. Success is reported as “GPU memory freed”.","locale":"en"},"10517":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#gpu-memory","content":"Models also unload automatically after an idle period, configured with “Unload models after idle minutes (0: never)” in **Settings › Compute**, defaulting to 10 minutes. When GPU memory runs out, RVC Next automatically unloads all models not currently in use and reports “The GPU is not available or ran out of memory”.","locale":"en"},"10518":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#theme","content":"The rightmost button cycles through **Light** → **Dark** → **System**, with its icon showing the current choice. More appearance options (**Colour**, **Contrast**, **Motion**) are in **Settings › Appearance**.","locale":"en"},"10519":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#live-status-chip","content":"While live voice conversion is running, a chip appears before the buttons on the right of the top bar, visible on every page. It shows “Live · N ms” (estimated latency) while running, or the current state during startup, loading or reconnection, such as “Loading the voice…” or “Reconnecting the device…”. Click the chip to open **Live**; click the square **Stop** button beside it to stop live voice conversion directly. See Live voice conversion.","locale":"en"},"10520":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#access-token","content":"The access token is optional; other computers can reach the server without one. If the server has an access token set, an **Access token** dialog appears when the browser first connects; enter it to proceed. Only operations such as **Show in folder** require the browser and server to be on the same computer. See Remote access and security.","locale":"en"},"10521":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"esc closes the topmost dialog, menu or sheet (one layer at a time).","locale":"en"},"10522":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"Focus a drop zone with tab, then press enter or space to open the file picker.","locale":"en"},"10523":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"Focus a result's waveform with tab, then use arrow-left / arrow-right to move backward or forward by 5% at a time.","locale":"en"},"10524":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"Focus a clickable card (such as a preset in **Separate** or a voice in the library), then press enter to activate it.","locale":"en"},"10525":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-interface-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-interface","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-interface#keyboard-controls","content":"To reduce interface animations, select **Reduced** in **Settings › Appearance › Motion**.","locale":"en"},"10526":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"page","content":"Use Live in other apps","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","locale":"en"},"10527":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Send the converted voice from Live into Discord, Zoom, OBS, a game or any other program as if it were a microphone: a virtual audio device on Windows (VB-CABLE or Voicemeeter), macOS (BlackHole) and Linux (a PipeWire or PulseAudio virtual microphone), set up step by step.","locale":"en"},"10528":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"Before you start","locale":"en"},"10529":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-vb-cable","content":"Windows: VB-CABLE","locale":"en"},"10530":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Install","locale":"en"},"10531":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"Set up rvc-next","locale":"en"},"10532":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program","content":"Set up the other program","locale":"en"},"10533":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-voicemeeter","content":"Windows: Voicemeeter","locale":"en"},"10534":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Device names","locale":"en"},"10535":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-1","content":"Install","locale":"en"},"10536":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"Set up Voicemeeter","locale":"en"},"10537":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"Set up rvc-next","locale":"en"},"10538":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program-1","content":"Set up the other program","locale":"en"},"10539":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#latency-and-troubleshooting","content":"Latency and troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"10540":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#voicemeeter-editions","content":"Standard and Potato","locale":"en"},"10541":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Windows: turn off exclusive control (optional, recommended)","locale":"en"},"10542":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-microphone-access-and-ducking","content":"Windows: microphone access and ducking","locale":"en"},"10543":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#macos","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"10544":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"Install","locale":"en"},"10545":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#allow-the-microphone","content":"Allow the microphone","locale":"en"},"10546":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"Set up rvc-next","locale":"en"},"10547":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program-2","content":"Set up the other program","locale":"en"},"10548":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"10549":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10550":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#1-find-your-sound-server","content":"1\\. Find your sound server","locale":"en"},"10551":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#2-create-the-virtual-sink-and-microphone","content":"2\\. Create the virtual sink and microphone","locale":"en"},"10552":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#3-add-the-alsa-device-for-rvc-next","content":"3\\. Add the ALSA device for rvc-next","locale":"en"},"10553":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"4\\. Set up rvc-next","locale":"en"},"10554":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#5-set-up-the-other-program","content":"5\\. Set up the other program","locale":"en"},"10555":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"Make it permanent","locale":"en"},"10556":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remove","content":"Remove","locale":"en"},"10557":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Settings in the other program","locale":"en"},"10558":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"Day-to-day use","locale":"en"},"10559":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"rvc-next on another computer","locale":"en"},"10560":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"10561":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Live plays the converted voice on an output device. To make another program hear it as a microphone, you need a **virtual audio device**: a device with a *playback side*, which rvc-next plays into, and a *recording side*, which the other program records from. Whatever is played into one side comes out of the other.","locale":"en"},"10562":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"System","locale":"en"},"10563":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Virtual device","locale":"en"},"10564":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"rvc-next **Output**","locale":"en"},"10565":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"The other program's microphone","locale":"en"},"10566":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"10567":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"VB-CABLE (simplest)","locale":"en"},"10568":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**CABLE Input (VB-Audio Virtual Cable)**","locale":"en"},"10569":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**CABLE Output (VB-Audio Virtual Cable)**","locale":"en"},"10570":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"10571":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Voicemeeter Banana (to mix in other sound)","locale":"en"},"10572":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**Voicemeeter AUX Input**","locale":"en"},"10573":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**Voicemeeter Out B1**","locale":"en"},"10574":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"10575":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"BlackHole 2ch","locale":"en"},"10576":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**BlackHole 2ch**","locale":"en"},"10577":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**BlackHole 2ch**","locale":"en"},"10578":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10579":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"A PipeWire / PulseAudio virtual microphone","locale":"en"},"10580":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**rvc-next-virtual** (an ALSA device you add)","locale":"en"},"10581":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","content":"**RVC-Next-Microphone**","locale":"en"},"10582":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Run rvc-next on the computer the other program runs on.** Live opens the devices of the server's computer (**Server devices**). If rvc-next runs on another computer, see rvc-next on another computer.","locale":"en"},"10583":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Get Live working with headphones first.** Choose your microphone as **Input** and your headphones as **Output**, check that **Input level** moves, press **Test**, then **Start** and listen. Once that works, switch **Output** to the virtual device as described below.","locale":"en"},"10584":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Wear headphones.** With speakers, the microphone picks up the other people's voices and converts them too.","locale":"en"},"10585":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Keep your real headphones or speakers as the system's default output**, and choose the virtual device only inside rvc-next and the other program. Making the virtual device the default output sends every sound the computer plays, including the call itself, into your \"microphone\".","locale":"en"},"10586":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Choose your microphone by name in rvc-next's Input menu, not System default**, if you ever make the virtual device the system's default input (some games have no microphone setting). Otherwise rvc-next records its own output.","locale":"en"},"10587":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#before-you-start","content":"**Hear yourself through Monitor.** rvc-next's **Monitor** is a second output: set it to your headphones with **Monitor source** set to **Converted** to hear what the other side hears. **Test** on Output plays into the virtual device, so you hear nothing from it; use **Test** on Monitor to check your headphones.","locale":"en"},"10588":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-vb-cable","content":"VB-CABLE is a free (donationware) single virtual cable from VB-Audio. Together with rvc-next's Monitor, it is all you need for voice chat.","locale":"en"},"10589":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Download the **VB-CABLE Driver Pack** from vb-audio.com/Cable and extract the whole zip.","locale":"en"},"10590":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Right-click **VBCABLE_Setup_x64.exe** (VBCABLE_Setup.exe on 32-bit Windows), choose **Run as administrator**, then click **Install Driver**.","locale":"en"},"10591":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Restart Windows.","locale":"en"},"10592":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Open the Sound Control Panel (**Settings › System › Sound › More sound settings**). The **Playback** tab now has **CABLE Input**, the **Recording** tab **CABLE Output**. Check that your real headphones (Playback) and microphone (Recording) are still the defaults; if the installer made the cable the default, right-click your real device and choose **Set as Default Device**.","locale":"en"},"10593":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Optional, for the lowest latency: open **Properties › Advanced** of **CABLE Input** and of **CABLE Output**, and set both to the same **Default Format**, for example 2 channel, 24 bit, 48000 Hz.","locale":"en"},"10594":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install","content":"Optional, recommended: turn off exclusive control for the microphone, the headphones and both sides of the cable.","locale":"en"},"10595":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"Open **Live** and click **Refresh devices**.","locale":"en"},"10596":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Input**: your microphone.","locale":"en"},"10597":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Output**: **CABLE Input (VB-Audio Virtual Cable)**, marked **virtual**.","locale":"en"},"10598":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Monitor**: your headphones; **Monitor source**: **Converted**.","locale":"en"},"10599":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"Under **Advanced**, leave the drivers on the recommended ones (WASAPI) and **Exclusive mode (WASAPI)** off, so the other program can use the cable at the same time.","locale":"en"},"10600":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next","content":"Click **Start** and speak. In the Sound Control Panel's **Recording** tab, the level bar next to **CABLE Output** moves while you speak.","locale":"en"},"10601":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program","content":"Choose **CABLE Output (VB-Audio Virtual Cable)** as its microphone, and your headphones as its speaker. See Settings in the other program for the processing to turn off.","locale":"en"},"10602":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program","content":"Many VB-CABLE guides tell you to tick **Listen to this device** in **CABLE Output › Properties › Listen** to hear the cable. rvc-next's **Monitor** already does that; with both on, you hear yourself twice, the second time with extra delay.","locale":"en"},"10603":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-voicemeeter","content":"Voicemeeter (free, donationware, from VB-Audio) is a virtual mixer. Use it instead of VB-CABLE when the call or stream should get more than your voice, for example music or game sound mixed in, or when you want its equalizer and compressor on your voice. The steps use **Voicemeeter Banana**; notes for Standard and Potato follow.","locale":"en"},"10604":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Voicemeeter adds virtual playback devices (rvc-next plays into these) and virtual recording devices (the other program records from these). Since the 2024 release, which installed a new driver, the recording devices are called **Out B1/B2/B3**; older installs show the old names:","locale":"en"},"10605":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Voicemeeter strip or bus","locale":"en"},"10606":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Playback device (rvc-next **Output**)","locale":"en"},"10607":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Recording device, current name","locale":"en"},"10608":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Recording device, before 2024","locale":"en"},"10609":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual input **VAIO**","locale":"en"},"10610":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter Input**","locale":"en"},"10611":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10612":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10613":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual input **AUX** (Banana, Potato)","locale":"en"},"10614":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter AUX Input**","locale":"en"},"10615":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10616":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10617":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual input **VAIO3** (Potato)","locale":"en"},"10618":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter VAIO3 Input**","locale":"en"},"10619":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10620":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10621":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual bus **B1**","locale":"en"},"10622":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10623":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter Out B1**","locale":"en"},"10624":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter Output**","locale":"en"},"10625":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual bus **B2** (Banana, Potato)","locale":"en"},"10626":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10627":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter Out B2**","locale":"en"},"10628":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter AUX Output**","locale":"en"},"10629":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Virtual bus **B3** (Potato)","locale":"en"},"10630":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10631":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter Out B3**","locale":"en"},"10632":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"**Voicemeeter VAIO3 Output**","locale":"en"},"10633":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#device-names","content":"Each name is followed by the driver's name in brackets, for example *(VB-Audio Voicemeeter VAIO)*. After an update from an older version, choose the devices again in every program that used them.","locale":"en"},"10634":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-1","content":"Download Voicemeeter Banana from vb-audio.com/Voicemeeter/banana.htm, run the setup program **as administrator**, and restart Windows.","locale":"en"},"10635":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-1","content":"Start Voicemeeter Banana. It has to be running for any of its devices to pass sound: turn on **Menu › Run on Windows Startup**.","locale":"en"},"10636":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"Voicemeeter's window has the input strips on the left (three hardware inputs, then the two virtual inputs **VOICEMEETER VAIO** and **VOICEMEETER AUX**) and the outputs on the right. The **A1 A2 A3 B1 B2** buttons on each input strip choose which buses that input goes to: **A** buses are your real outputs, **B** buses are the virtual recording devices.","locale":"en"},"10637":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"**Choose A1 first.** Click **A1** under **HARDWARE OUT** (top right) and choose your headphones, preferably the **WDM** entry (**KS** also works; **MME** is the fallback). A1 is Voicemeeter's main output: the sample rate and buffer of the whole mixer follow it.","locale":"en"},"10638":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"**Leave the hardware inputs alone.** rvc-next opens your microphone itself. Don't select the microphone as **Hardware Input 1**; if it is already there, turn that strip's **B1** off. Otherwise the call hears your real voice as well as the converted one, and Voicemeeter may hold the microphone so that rvc-next reports it as **In use by another program**. Turning off exclusive control for the microphone and the Voicemeeter devices helps too.","locale":"en"},"10639":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"**VOICEMEETER AUX** strip (rvc-next plays into it): turn **B1** on, so the converted voice goes to **Voicemeeter Out B1**. Turn **A1** on as well if you want to hear yourself through Voicemeeter, and then leave rvc-next's **Monitor** empty (with both, you hear yourself twice).","locale":"en"},"10640":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"**VOICEMEETER VAIO** strip: this one receives Windows sounds if you make **Voicemeeter Input** the default playback device, as VB-Audio's own guides suggest. Turn **A1** on and **B1** off, so the computer's sounds reach your headphones but not the call. To send music or game sound into the call on purpose, turn its **B1** on.","locale":"en"},"10641":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-voicemeeter","content":"Using AUX for rvc-next keeps the two apart: with rvc-next on VAIO, every Windows sound would go into the call along with your voice whenever VAIO is the default playback device.","locale":"en"},"10642":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"Open **Live** and click **Refresh devices**.","locale":"en"},"10643":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"**Input**: your microphone.","locale":"en"},"10644":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"**Output**: **Voicemeeter AUX Input**.","locale":"en"},"10645":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"**Monitor**: **No monitor** if Voicemeeter's A1 lets you hear yourself; otherwise your headphones.","locale":"en"},"10646":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-1","content":"Click **Start** and speak: the level meters of the **VOICEMEETER AUX** strip and of bus **B1** move.","locale":"en"},"10647":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program-1","content":"Choose **Voicemeeter Out B1** (before 2024: **Voicemeeter Output**) as its microphone. For OBS, add **Voicemeeter Out B1** as an **Audio Input Capture** source.","locale":"en"},"10648":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#latency-and-troubleshooting","content":"Voicemeeter adds its own buffering to rvc-next's latency. **Menu › System Settings / Options** sets the buffering per driver type; smaller buffers mean less delay, but crackles mean they are too small for your computer.","locale":"en"},"10649":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#latency-and-troubleshooting","content":"After changing devices in Windows, or if a strip stays silent, use **Menu › Restart Audio Engine**.","locale":"en"},"10650":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#latency-and-troubleshooting","content":"All Voicemeeter devices run at A1's sample rate. Set Voicemeeter's playback and recording devices to the same format (48000 Hz) in the Sound Control Panel; then rvc-next shows **one duplex stream** when your microphone uses 48 kHz too.","locale":"en"},"10651":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#voicemeeter-editions","content":"**Voicemeeter (Standard)** has one virtual input (**VAIO**) and one virtual bus (**B**). Use **Voicemeeter Input** as rvc-next's Output, turn the VAIO strip's **B** on, and record **Voicemeeter Out B1**. Don't make **Voicemeeter Input** the default playback device, or every Windows sound goes into the call.","locale":"en"},"10652":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#voicemeeter-editions","content":"**Voicemeeter Potato** has a third virtual input and bus (**VAIO3**, **B3**). The Banana steps work unchanged; VAIO3 can carry a second source.","locale":"en"},"10653":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Windows lets a program take a device for itself (*exclusive mode*): while it holds the device, no other program can play or record through it. By default every device allows this, and an exclusive request even takes the device away from programs already using it (\"Give exclusive mode applications priority\"). Some games, voice chat programs and audio players ask for exclusive mode, and then rvc-next loses the microphone or the virtual device in the middle of a session (Live goes to **Reconnecting the device…**), or cannot open it at all (**In use by another program**). The other program can lose it to rvc-next the same way.","locale":"en"},"10654":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Turning exclusive control off for the devices in your chain prevents this. It is optional: do it if you see those symptoms, or before you rely on the setup for a stream or a call.","locale":"en"},"10655":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Press **Win + R**, type `mmsys.cpl` and press Enter. (Or **Settings › System › Sound › More sound settings**.)","locale":"en"},"10656":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"On the **Recording** tab, double-click your **microphone**.","locale":"en"},"10657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Open the **Advanced** tab. Under **Exclusive Mode**, clear **Allow applications to take exclusive control of this device**. **Give exclusive mode applications priority** below it is greyed out with it. Click **Apply**, then **OK**.","locale":"en"},"10658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Do the same for the other devices in the chain:","locale":"en"},"10659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"**Recording** tab: the recording side the other program uses (**CABLE Output**, or **Voicemeeter Out B1**);","locale":"en"},"10660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"**Playback** tab: your **headphones** (rvc-next's Monitor, Voicemeeter's A1), and the playback side rvc-next plays into (**CABLE Input**, or **Voicemeeter Input** / **Voicemeeter AUX Input**).","locale":"en"},"10661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Stop and start Live, and restart the other program, so both open the devices again.","locale":"en"},"10662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Newer Windows 11 releases (from 26H2) also have this switch in the Settings app: **Settings › System › Sound**, choose the device, then **Exclusive mode** under **Advanced**. The control panel route above works on every Windows 10 and 11 release.","locale":"en"},"10663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Notes:","locale":"en"},"10664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Leave rvc-next's own **Advanced › Exclusive mode (WASAPI)** off (its default). Windows refuses it on a device whose exclusive control you turned off; if you turned it on, the device panel reports the problem and offers **Turn off exclusive mode**.","locale":"en"},"10665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"Keep exclusive control on for a device you deliberately use in exclusive mode with another program (a music player that plays bit-perfect, a DAW). ASIO drivers don't go through these Windows settings at all.","locale":"en"},"10666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-exclusive","content":"The same **Advanced** tab sets the device's **Default Format** (step 5 of VB-CABLE › Install). Some devices also show **Enable audio enhancements** (or a separate **Enhancements** tab) there; turning it off on the microphone keeps the driver's own processing from colouring the voice rvc-next converts.","locale":"en"},"10667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-microphone-access-and-ducking","content":"**Settings › Privacy & security › Microphone**: **Microphone access** and **Let desktop apps access your microphone** must be on, or rvc-next (a Python program) gets silence or **Microphone permission denied**.","locale":"en"},"10668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#windows-microphone-access-and-ducking","content":"While a voice chat program records, Windows may lower every other sound. To stop that, open the Sound Control Panel's **Communications** tab and choose **Do nothing**.","locale":"en"},"10669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#macos","content":"macOS has no virtual audio device of its own. **BlackHole** (free, open source, from Existential Audio) adds one. **BlackHole 2ch**, a single stereo device, is the one to use for voice: it appears both as an output (rvc-next plays into it) and as an input (the other program records from it).","locale":"en"},"10670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"Quit any programs that use audio.","locale":"en"},"10671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"Install BlackHole 2ch, either:","locale":"en"},"10672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"with the installer from existential.audio/blackhole, restarting when it asks, or","locale":"en"},"10673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"with Homebrew: `brew install blackhole-2ch`.","locale":"en"},"10674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"Open **Audio MIDI Setup** (**Applications › Utilities**). **BlackHole 2ch** is in the list on the left. Select it and set **Format** to **48,000 Hz**, the rate most microphones use.","locale":"en"},"10675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"Keep your headphones as the system output (**System Settings › Sound › Output**).","locale":"en"},"10676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#install-2","content":"If BlackHole does not appear, restart Core Audio with `sudo killall -9 coreaudiod`, or restart the Mac.","locale":"en"},"10677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#allow-the-microphone","content":"The first time rvc-next opens the microphone, macOS asks whether the program that started rvc-next (Terminal, iTerm2, VS Code…) may use it. Allow it. If you refused, or rvc-next reports **Microphone permission denied**, turn that program on in **System Settings › Privacy & Security › Microphone**, then quit it completely and start rvc-next again.","locale":"en"},"10678":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"Open **Live** and click **Refresh devices**.","locale":"en"},"10679":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"**Input**: your microphone (for example **MacBook Pro Microphone** or a USB microphone). Never choose **BlackHole 2ch** here: that records rvc-next's own output.","locale":"en"},"10680":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"**Output**: **BlackHole 2ch**, marked **virtual**.","locale":"en"},"10681":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"**Monitor**: your headphones; **Monitor source**: **Converted**.","locale":"en"},"10682":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-rvc-next-2","content":"Click **Start** and speak.","locale":"en"},"10683":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#set-up-the-other-program-2","content":"Choose **BlackHole 2ch** as its microphone. See Settings in the other program.","locale":"en"},"10684":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"**You don't need a Multi-Output Device.** Many BlackHole guides create one in Audio MIDI Setup so that the Mac's own sound goes to BlackHole and your speakers at once. That is for recording the computer's sound; for your converted voice, rvc-next's **Monitor** does the listening part.","locale":"en"},"10685":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"**Converting the Mac's own sound** (a video, a game) as Live's input needs a *second* loopback device, because one device can't be rvc-next's input and output at once. Install **BlackHole 16ch** as well (`brew install blackhole-16ch`), create a **Multi-Output Device** of your headphones and BlackHole 16ch, make it the system output, and choose **BlackHole 16ch** as rvc-next's Input; BlackHole 2ch stays the Output.","locale":"en"},"10686":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"**Bluetooth headsets**: when their microphone is in use, AirPods and most Bluetooth headsets switch to a low-quality call mode, and Bluetooth adds latency. Use the Mac's built-in or a USB microphone as Input.","locale":"en"},"10687":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"**Alternatives**: Loopback by Rogue Amoeba (paid) creates named virtual devices and can mix several sources; VB-CABLE for Mac works like VB-CABLE on Windows. Use either the same way: rvc-next plays into its output side, the other program records its input side.","locale":"en"},"10688":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#notes","content":"**Uninstall**: `sudo rm -R /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/BlackHole2ch.driver`, then `sudo killall -9 coreaudiod`.","locale":"en"},"10689":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux","content":"On a Linux desktop, the sound server (PipeWire on most current distributions, PulseAudio on older ones) owns the sound cards. You create a **virtual sink** for rvc-next to play into, and a **virtual microphone** that carries the sink's sound, for the other program to record.","locale":"en"},"10690":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux","content":"There are two Linux-specific points:","locale":"en"},"10691":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux","content":"**Browsers and Electron apps (Discord, Slack…) hide \"Monitor of …\" sources** from their microphone lists. That is why the steps add a real virtual microphone (a *remapped source*) rather than relying on the sink's monitor.","locale":"en"},"10692":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux","content":"**rvc-next does not list PipeWire or PulseAudio sinks one by one.** The PortAudio library most distributions ship talks to ALSA (and JACK); the sound server appears only as the ALSA devices **pipewire**, **pulse** and **default**, which play to the *default* sink. So you add one small ALSA device, **rvc-next-virtual**, that plays to the virtual sink.","locale":"en"},"10693":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#1-find-your-sound-server","content":"`PulseAudio (on PipeWire 1.x.x)` means PipeWire; `pulseaudio` means PulseAudio. If `pactl` is missing, install `pulseaudio-utils` (Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora) or `libpulse` (Arch); it works with both servers.","locale":"en"},"10694":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#2-create-the-virtual-sink-and-microphone","content":"The first command creates the sink **RVC-Next** (`rvc_next`), the second the source **RVC-Next-Microphone** (`rvc_next_mic`), which carries whatever is played into the sink. Check them with `pactl list short sinks` and `pactl list short sources`.","locale":"en"},"10695":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#2-create-the-virtual-sink-and-microphone","content":"These two work on PipeWire and PulseAudio alike, but last only until you log out or restart the sound server. To keep them, see Make it permanent.","locale":"en"},"10696":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#3-add-the-alsa-device-for-rvc-next","content":"Add one of these blocks to `~/.asoundrc` (create the file if it doesn't exist; keep anything already in it). Choose by what rvc-next's **Output** menu already lists: **pipewire** means the PipeWire ALSA plugin is installed (package `pipewire-alsa`), **pulse** means the PulseAudio one (`libasound2-plugins` on Debian and Ubuntu, `alsa-plugins-pulseaudio` on Fedora, `alsa-plugins` on Arch).","locale":"en"},"10697":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#3-add-the-alsa-device-for-rvc-next","content":"This also works on PipeWire, through its PulseAudio server.","locale":"en"},"10698":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#3-add-the-alsa-device-for-rvc-next","content":"Both define an ALSA device named **rvc-next-virtual** that plays into the `rvc_next` sink. Restart rvc-next after editing the file: ALSA reads it when a program starts.","locale":"en"},"10699":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"Open **Live** and click **Refresh devices**.","locale":"en"},"10700":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Input**: **pipewire** or **pulse** (the system's default microphone), or **System default**. These go through the sound server, so other programs can use the microphone at the same time. Choose the microphone you want as the default input in your desktop's sound settings.","locale":"en"},"10701":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Output**: **rvc-next-virtual**, marked **virtual**.","locale":"en"},"10702":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"**Monitor**: **pipewire** or **pulse**, which play to your default output (your headphones); **Monitor source**: **Converted**.","locale":"en"},"10703":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"Under **Advanced**, set **Sample rate** to **48 kHz** (PipeWire's usual rate) instead of **Automatic**.","locale":"en"},"10704":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#4-set-up-rvc-next","content":"Click **Start** and speak. In `pavucontrol` (PulseAudio Volume Control) the **Input Devices** tab shows **RVC-Next-Microphone**'s level moving; its **Playback** tab shows rvc-next's two streams, one on **RVC-Next** and the monitor on your headphones.","locale":"en"},"10705":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#5-set-up-the-other-program","content":"Choose **RVC-Next-Microphone** as its microphone. Flatpak and Snap packages of Discord, Zoom or OBS see it too. Avoid **Default** in Discord: it may follow a different device.","locale":"en"},"10706":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#5-set-up-the-other-program","content":"Don't make **RVC-Next-Microphone** the system's default input: rvc-next's **pipewire**, **pulse** and **System default** inputs record the default input, so rvc-next would record its own output. For a program without a microphone setting, start it, then move its stream to **RVC-Next-Microphone** in `pavucontrol`'s **Recording** tab; the sound server remembers that for the next time.","locale":"en"},"10707":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"`~/.asoundrc` stays. For the sink and microphone:","locale":"en"},"10708":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"Create `~/.config/pipewire/pipewire-pulse.conf.d/rvc-next.conf`:","locale":"en"},"10709":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"Then restart the sound server (or log out and back in):","locale":"en"},"10710":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"Create `~/.config/pulse/default.pa` (if it exists, add the last two lines):","locale":"en"},"10711":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#linux-permanent","content":"Then restart PulseAudio with `pulseaudio -k` (it starts again by itself).","locale":"en"},"10712":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remove","content":"These remove *every* remapped source and null sink, including any you made for other purposes. Then delete the `rvc-next-virtual` block from `~/.asoundrc` and the file from **Make it permanent**.","locale":"en"},"10713":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Voice chat programs process the microphone to clean up a real voice. On a converted voice that is already clean, that processing tends to eat consonants, pump the level or cut words, so turn it off.","locale":"en"},"10714":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Program","locale":"en"},"10715":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Microphone","locale":"en"},"10716":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Turn off / change","locale":"en"},"10717":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Discord**","locale":"en"},"10718":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**User Settings › Voice & Video › Input Device**","locale":"en"},"10719":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Noise Suppression**: None (or Standard; Krisp is the harshest); **Echo Cancellation**: off when you wear headphones; **Automatic Gain Control**: off; **Automatically determine input sensitivity**: off, then set the slider so the bar turns green when you speak","locale":"en"},"10720":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Zoom**","locale":"en"},"10721":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Settings › Audio › Microphone**","locale":"en"},"10722":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Automatically adjust microphone volume**: off; **Suppress background noise**: Low","locale":"en"},"10723":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**OBS Studio**","locale":"en"},"10724":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Sources › + › Audio Input Capture › Device**, or **Settings › Audio › Mic/Auxiliary Audio**","locale":"en"},"10725":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Leave noise filters off on that source","locale":"en"},"10726":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Browser apps** (Google Meet, Teams on the web, Discord in a browser)","locale":"en"},"10727":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"The meeting's audio settings, or the site's microphone permission","locale":"en"},"10728":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"The app's own noise cancellation, where it has one","locale":"en"},"10729":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"**Games and programs without a microphone setting**","locale":"en"},"10730":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"They use the system's default input: make the recording side the default in **Settings › System › Sound › Input** (Windows) or **System Settings › Sound › Input** (macOS). Linux: move the program's stream in `pavucontrol › Recording` instead (Linux, step 5)","locale":"en"},"10731":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Windows, macOS: rvc-next's **Input** must then name your real microphone, not **System default**","locale":"en"},"10732":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#apps","content":"Use the program's own microphone test (Discord's **Let's Check**, Zoom's **Test Mic**) to hear what others will hear.","locale":"en"},"10733":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"**Push to talk.** rvc-next adds about half a second of delay (the latency shown on Live). If you release the key as soon as you stop speaking, the end of the sentence is cut off: raise the program's push-to-talk release delay (Discord: **Push to Talk Release Delay**) above that latency, or hold the key a moment longer.","locale":"en"},"10734":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"**Voice activity.** With voice activation instead, use Live's **Input gate** (under **Buffering and clean-up**) so background noise is not converted into voice-like sound that keeps the call's voice activation open.","locale":"en"},"10735":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"**One sample rate everywhere.** With the microphone and the virtual device both at 48 kHz, the device panel shows **one duplex stream**, which saves one block of latency over **split streams**.","locale":"en"},"10736":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"**Measure the software chain.** **Measure latency** can run through the virtual device itself: Input = the recording side (**CABLE Output**, **BlackHole 2ch**), Output = the playback side (Windows and macOS). Live must be stopped; set Input and Output back afterwards.","locale":"en"},"10737":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#day-to-day-use","content":"**Starting order doesn't matter.** The other program can keep the virtual microphone selected while Live is stopped; it hears silence until you click **Start**.","locale":"en"},"10738":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"The virtual device must be on the computer whose devices Live uses:","locale":"en"},"10739":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"**Server devices**: install the virtual device on the server computer, and run the other program there too.","locale":"en"},"10740":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"**This browser**: the converted voice plays on the computer with the browser, through the browser's output. To send it into a program on that computer, play the *browser* into the virtual device:","locale":"en"},"10741":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"Windows: **Settings › System › Sound › Volume mixer**, choose the browser, set its **Output device** to **CABLE Input**.","locale":"en"},"10742":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"Linux: in `pavucontrol`'s **Playback** tab, move the browser's stream to **RVC-Next**.","locale":"en"},"10743":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"macOS has no per-program output; use Rogue Amoeba's Loopback, or make BlackHole 2ch the system output while you talk and set the call program's speaker to your headphones (every other sound the Mac plays then goes into the call too).","locale":"en"},"10744":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#remote","content":"The browser's microphone must then be your real microphone, and every other sound the browser plays goes into the virtual device too.","locale":"en"},"10745":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom","locale":"en"},"10746":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"10747":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The other side hears nothing","locale":"en"},"10748":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The other program must use the *recording* side (**CABLE Output**, **Voicemeeter Out B1**, **BlackHole 2ch**, **RVC-Next-Microphone**), rvc-next's Output the *playback* side. Live must be **Running**. Voicemeeter: the AUX strip's **B1** is on, and Voicemeeter is running","locale":"en"},"10749":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"They hear my real voice too, or only my real voice","locale":"en"},"10750":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The other program records the real microphone (or **Default**); in Voicemeeter, the microphone's strip sends to **B1**","locale":"en"},"10751":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"They hear the call, music or system sounds","locale":"en"},"10752":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The virtual device is the system's default output, or (Voicemeeter) the VAIO strip's **B1** is on","locale":"en"},"10753":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"I hear myself twice","locale":"en"},"10754":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"rvc-next's Monitor and Voicemeeter's **A1** (or Windows' **Listen to this device**) are both on; keep one","locale":"en"},"10755":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Robotic, choppy or crackling","locale":"en"},"10756":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Check **Load** and **underruns** on Live first (Live › Tips); then the sample rates (48 kHz everywhere) and, with Voicemeeter, a larger buffer","locale":"en"},"10757":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-230","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The virtual device is missing from rvc-next's menus","locale":"en"},"10758":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-231","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Restart the computer after installing the driver (Windows, macOS), then click **Refresh devices**. Linux: restart rvc-next after editing `~/.asoundrc`","locale":"en"},"10759":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-232","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Linux: **rvc-next-virtual** fails to open","locale":"en"},"10760":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-233","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"The block's `type` must match a plugin you have: `type pipewire` needs the **pipewire** device, `type pulse` the **pulse** device. `pactl list short sinks` must list `rvc_next`","locale":"en"},"10761":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-234","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Windows: Live loses a device (**Reconnecting the device…**) or reports **In use by another program** when a game or another program starts","locale":"en"},"10762":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-235","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"That program takes the device in exclusive mode: turn off exclusive control for it","locale":"en"},"10763":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-236","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"**Microphone permission denied**","locale":"en"},"10764":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-237","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"Windows: **Let desktop apps access your microphone**. macOS: allow the terminal in **Privacy & Security › Microphone** and restart it","locale":"en"},"10765":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing-238","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live-routing#troubleshooting","content":"See also Live for devices, buffering and latency, and Hardware and performance for latency figures.","locale":"en"},"10766":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"page","content":"Live","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live","locale":"en"},"10767":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live","content":"The Live page converts microphone audio into the selected voice in real time, then sends it to headphones, speakers or a virtual audio device (for streaming or voice chat, for example). From top to bottom, the page has three sections: audio devices, voice and parameters, and buffering and noise reduction. The Start / Stop button and status bar stay fixed at the bottom.","locale":"en"},"10768":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"Quick start","locale":"en"},"10769":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"Use this browser's microphone","locale":"en"},"10770":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#audio-devices","content":"Audio devices","locale":"en"},"10771":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Input, output and monitor","locale":"en"},"10772":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Record an output device (loopback)","locale":"en"},"10773":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#hear-yourself","content":"Hear yourself","locale":"en"},"10774":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Advanced","locale":"en"},"10775":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"Measure the real latency","locale":"en"},"10776":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Device problems and repair buttons","locale":"en"},"10777":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#what-if-the-output-device-is-missing","content":"What if the output device is missing?","locale":"en"},"10778":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"Voice and parameters","locale":"en"},"10779":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Buffering and noise reduction","locale":"en"},"10780":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#effects","content":"Effects","locale":"en"},"10781":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Start, stop and the status bar","locale":"en"},"10782":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"Record","locale":"en"},"10783":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#the-live-chip-in-the-top-bar","content":"The Live chip in the top bar","locale":"en"},"10784":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"Device disconnection and automatic reconnection","locale":"en"},"10785":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#sharing-the-gpu-with-other-jobs","content":"Sharing the GPU with other jobs","locale":"en"},"10786":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"Tips for reducing latency","locale":"en"},"10787":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#asio-windows","content":"ASIO (Windows)","locale":"en"},"10788":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-live#run-from-the-command-line","content":"Run from the command line","locale":"en"},"10789":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live","content":"Live voice conversion runs in a separate background process, independently of the server and conversion jobs. It opens audio devices on **the server machine**, rather than the device running your browser.","locale":"en"},"10790":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live","content":"This means `sounddevice` (the Python wrapper for PortAudio) is not installed in the server's Python environment. Linux also needs the system package `libportaudio2`. See Installation.","locale":"en"},"10791":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"Open **Live** in the left navigation.","locale":"en"},"10792":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"In **Audio devices**, select **Input** (microphone) and **Output** (headphones, or a virtual audio device to use the voice in Discord, OBS and other programs: see Use Live in other apps). Speak into the microphone: the **Input level** meter should move. Click **Test** beside **Output**; you should hear a tone.","locale":"en"},"10793":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"Choose a voice in the **Voice** picker and adjust **Voice parameters** as needed (for example, set **Pitch** to about +12 for a male-to-female voice conversion).","locale":"en"},"10794":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"On first use, the start button may be replaced by **Needs …** and a **Download (size)** button. Live voice conversion always needs HuBERT. If the voice has pitch guidance and the pitch method is RMVPE, FCPE or CREPE, it also needs that model (pm and SwiftF0 need no extra download). Click download; the button returns when it finishes.","locale":"en"},"10795":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"Click **Start** at the bottom. The button shows each step as it happens (checking the audio devices, loading PyTorch, the voice and the models, then **Warming up…**). Once it shows **Running**, you can start speaking.","locale":"en"},"10796":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"Click **Stop** when finished.","locale":"en"},"10797":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#quick-start","content":"The next time you open the page, your previous devices, voice, parameters and buffer settings are restored automatically. Just click **Start**.","locale":"en"},"10798":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"At the top of the page, **Server devices** and **This browser** choose where the audio comes from and goes to. **This browser** uses the microphone and speakers of the device the page is open on — a laptop or phone talking to an rvc-next on another computer, or a server without any sound card (then it is the only choice): the browser sends its microphone to the server over a WebSocket and plays the converted voice from a small jitter buffer (60 ms, refilled after a dropout; more than 250 ms waiting is dropped).","locale":"en"},"10799":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"**Start** asks for the microphone the first time; allow it. The browser's own echo cancellation, noise suppression and automatic gain are turned off, as they would fight the conversion — wear headphones.","locale":"en"},"10800":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"The session runs at the browser's audio rate (usually 48 or 44.1 kHz). Voice, parameters, buffering, effects, gains (from **Settings › Audio**) and recording work as with server devices; monitoring, the input meter and **Test** belong to server devices.","locale":"en"},"10801":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"The latency is the one shown plus the network's round trip and the 60 ms buffer. A wired or good Wi-Fi network on the same site keeps it small; the line under the title shows the buffer and the dropouts.","locale":"en"},"10802":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"Browsers allow the microphone only over HTTPS or on `localhost`; see Remote access to serve HTTPS.","locale":"en"},"10803":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#browser-audio","content":"Closing the tab, or losing the connection for 3 seconds, stops the session. Only one browser can be connected at a time: a newer one takes over.","locale":"en"},"10804":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#audio-devices","content":"The device panel is titled **Audio devices on \\{host}**, reminding you that these devices belong to the server machine. If you open the page remotely from another computer, it also shows: **These devices belong to the server machine, not this browser.** The **Refresh devices** button at the top right rescans devices. While stopped, the panel also refreshes automatically every 5 seconds when the page is visible.","locale":"en"},"10805":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#audio-devices","content":"The same device panel appears in **Settings › Audio**. Both edit the same settings.","locale":"en"},"10806":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"10807":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10808":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"**Input**","locale":"en"},"10809":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"The microphone. The **Input level** meter below it shows its volume in real time whenever the device panel is shown, before the first **Start**, during a session and after it stops (an error included). It opens in the background, so the page never waits for it, and it comes back by itself once an unplugged or busy microphone is available again. You can turn it off in **Settings › Audio › Show the input meter while stopped**.","locale":"en"},"10810":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"**Output**","locale":"en"},"10811":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"The converted audio goes here. **Output level** below it shows what rvc-next sends to this device (the converted voice, or the input with **Hear yourself**); it reads **—** while nothing plays. The **Test** button beside it plays a tone on this device. To send the audio to another program, choose a virtual cable's playback side (Use Live in other apps); to convert what an output device plays, see Record an output device.","locale":"en"},"10812":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"**Monitor**","locale":"en"},"10813":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"An optional second output, set to **No monitor** by default. Useful for sending output to a virtual audio device while listening through headphones. Selecting a monitor device reveals its **Monitor level** meter, a **Test** button and the following controls:","locale":"en"},"10814":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Monitor source","locale":"en"},"10815":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"**Converted** / **Input** / **Both** (the original and converted audio mixed together)","locale":"en"},"10816":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"**Monitor level**","locale":"en"},"10817":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"−60 to +12 dB, default 0 dB","locale":"en"},"10818":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Device menus are arranged as follows:","locale":"en"},"10819":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Each device takes a full row; its menu opens as wide as the row, and long names wrap rather than being cut off. Under each name is a second line: the recommended driver, the channel count and the default sample rate.","locale":"en"},"10820":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"While the server is still listing the devices (a moment, longer with many drivers installed), each menu says **Looking for audio devices…**.","locale":"en"},"10821":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"A long list (nine items or more, usual on Windows) has a search field at the top.","locale":"en"},"10822":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"The first item is always **System default**, following the operating system's current default device.","locale":"en"},"10823":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Next comes the system's default device (marked **default**), followed by devices sorted by name. Virtual audio devices are marked **virtual**.","locale":"en"},"10824":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Each menu item represents one **physical device**, showing its full name. On Windows, the same microphone can appear under several drivers, such as MME, DirectSound and WASAPI. rvc-next combines these into one item and automatically selects the recommended driver (in order of preference: ASIO, WASAPI, WDM-KS, DirectSound, MME on Windows; JACK, ALSA, PulseAudio on Linux; the PortAudio most Linux distributions ship has no PulseAudio driver, so PulseAudio and PipeWire appear as the ALSA devices **pulse**, **pipewire** and **default**).","locale":"en"},"10825":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#input-output-and-monitor","content":"Previously saved devices that are now disconnected remain visible in gray, marked **not connected**.","locale":"en"},"10826":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"To convert what the computer plays rather than a microphone (a video, a game, a call), turn on **Settings › Audio › Record output devices as inputs (loopback)**. The input menu then also lists every output device, marked **loopback**; choosing one makes whatever that device plays the input.","locale":"en"},"10827":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"System","locale":"en"},"10828":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"How it records","locale":"en"},"10829":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"10830":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"10831":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"WASAPI loopback","locale":"en"},"10832":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Works with any output device, at any sample rate; silence while nothing plays","locale":"en"},"10833":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10834":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"The PulseAudio/PipeWire monitor of each output (“Monitor of …”)","locale":"en"},"10835":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Needs a running PulseAudio or PipeWire (pipewire-pulse)","locale":"en"},"10836":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"10837":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Not possible with the system alone","locale":"en"},"10838":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Install a loopback driver such as BlackHole, send the sound to it, and choose its input (an ordinary input device)","locale":"en"},"10839":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"When recording is not possible, the device panel says why. Send the converted voice to a **different** device than the one being recorded (headphones, or a virtual cable for another program): recording the output that plays the voice would feed it back into itself, so rvc-next refuses it (**Records its own output**). Turning the setting off hides these inputs again.","locale":"en"},"10840":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#loopback","content":"Nothing can play *into* an input device, so the output menu lists only outputs. To send the converted voice to another program, choose the playback side of a virtual cable (for example **CABLE Input**) as the output; the other program records its recording side (**CABLE Output**). Use Live in other apps sets this up step by step on Windows, macOS and Linux.","locale":"en"},"10841":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#hear-yourself","content":"The **Hear yourself** switch sends the original input straight to the monitor device (or to the output if no monitor is set), so you can check the “microphone → headphones” routing.","locale":"en"},"10842":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#hear-yourself","content":"When enabled while stopped: passes audio through without loading a voice.","locale":"en"},"10843":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#hear-yourself","content":"When enabled while running: with a monitor device, the monitor receives the original audio while the output stays converted; without one, the output switches directly to the original audio (temporarily bypassing conversion).","locale":"en"},"10844":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Expand **Advanced** to see:","locale":"en"},"10845":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"10846":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"10847":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Input · Driver** / **Output · Driver**","locale":"en"},"10848":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Shown only when a physical device has several drivers (host APIs). The recommended one is marked **… (recommended)**.","locale":"en"},"10849":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Input · Channels** / **Output · Channels**","locale":"en"},"10850":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"The selected input channels are mixed to mono; output is written to the selected channels. Defaults are **Default (channel 1)** for input and **Default (channel 1+2)** for output (channel 1 for a mono device). You can also select **Channel N** or **Mix 1+2**.","locale":"en"},"10851":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Sample rate**","locale":"en"},"10852":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Automatic** (default) or a fixed rate supported by the device. Automatic uses the output device's default rate (48 kHz if unsupported).","locale":"en"},"10853":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Exclusive mode (WASAPI)**","locale":"en"},"10854":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Shown only when output uses the WASAPI driver. Exclusive mode can reduce latency, but prevents other programs from using the device at the same time.","locale":"en"},"10855":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Input level**","locale":"en"},"10856":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"−24 to +24 dB, default 0 dB. Applies to the input before it is metered and converted: raise a quiet microphone, lower a hot one.","locale":"en"},"10857":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**Output level**","locale":"en"},"10858":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"−60 to +12 dB, default 0 dB. Applies to converted audio sent to the output device.","locale":"en"},"10859":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"Changing a level (or the monitor's source) while running applies from the next block without reopening the devices.","locale":"en"},"10860":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"By default, input reads only **channel 1**. If your microphone is connected to channel 2 (common on multichannel interfaces), explicitly select **Channel 2** or **Mix 1+2**.","locale":"en"},"10861":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"The bottom of the panel has a status line, for example `48 kHz · one duplex stream · est. latency 640 ms`:","locale":"en"},"10862":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**one duplex stream**: input and output use the same driver and sample rate, sending and receiving through one stream for the lowest latency.","locale":"en"},"10863":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#advanced","content":"**split streams**: the two cannot share a stream (different drivers or sample rates). An extra buffer adds one block of latency.","locale":"en"},"10864":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"The estimate relies on the latency the drivers report, which is often optimistic. **Measure latency** (below the status line) measures it instead:","locale":"en"},"10865":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"Connect the output to the input: an audio cable from the output to the input, a virtual cable's own loopback, or speakers near the microphone.","locale":"en"},"10866":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"Click **Measure latency**. For a few seconds, four short noise bursts play on the output while the input listens. Live must be stopped (and **Hear yourself** off); the input meter pauses meanwhile.","locale":"en"},"10867":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"The result reads, for example, `Measured latency 620 ms: round trip 560 ms through the devices + conversion 60 ms (estimated 580 ms)`.","locale":"en"},"10868":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"The **round trip** is measured: the bursts go through the same buffers a session uses (the output prefill, the device's buffers both ways, the cable or the air). The **conversion** part is the converter's own delay (crossfade + 10 ms, plus min(crossfade, 40 ms) with input noise reduction). It depends only on the settings, so it is computed, and SOLA may take up to 10 ms off it. Inference time adds nothing as long as there are no underruns.","locale":"en"},"10869":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"The measurement stays valid while you keep the same input, output and block length. While a session runs with them, the status bar shows **measured N ms** beside the estimate, and the Live chip uses it. Changing the crossfade or noise reduction only recomputes the conversion part; changing a device or the block clears the measurement.","locale":"en"},"10870":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#measure-latency","content":"If no burst comes back, the panel says so: check the connection and raise the levels. If the bursts come back at different times (dropouts, a drifting clock between two devices), try a longer block or devices on one driver. With speakers and a microphone the measurement includes the sound's travel through the air (about 3 ms per metre).","locale":"en"},"10871":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Whenever you change devices, rvc-next actually tries to open them with the current configuration in the background: it checks the settings with the driver and, while Live is stopped, runs the output and monitor for a moment (the input is already open for the **Input level** meter). Problems therefore appear below the relevant device before you click **Start**, and so does a failed **Test** sound or **Hear yourself**. The format is **reason: explanation from the server** (the explanation is supplied by the server in English, naming the device):","locale":"en"},"10872":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Reason","locale":"en"},"10873":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"10874":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Action","locale":"en"},"10875":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Not connected**","locale":"en"},"10876":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The device cannot be found","locale":"en"},"10877":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Choose another**: select a different device in the menu","locale":"en"},"10878":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**In use by another program**","locale":"en"},"10879":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Another program is using the device","locale":"en"},"10880":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"If exclusive mode is on, a **Turn off exclusive mode** button appears; otherwise, **Choose another** is suggested","locale":"en"},"10881":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Records its own output**","locale":"en"},"10882":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The input records the output (or monitor) that plays the converted voice","locale":"en"},"10883":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Choose another** input or output","locale":"en"},"10884":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Refuses this channel count**","locale":"en"},"10885":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The driver will not open the device with this many channels (rvc-next already picks a count the device reported accepting, so this usually means exclusive mode or a device that changed)","locale":"en"},"10886":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"If exclusive mode is on, a **Turn off exclusive mode** button appears; otherwise, **Choose another** is suggested (another driver of the same device usually works)","locale":"en"},"10887":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Refuses this format**","locale":"en"},"10888":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The device rejects the current sample rate","locale":"en"},"10889":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"Click **Use 48 kHz**","locale":"en"},"10890":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Stops right after it starts**","locale":"en"},"10891":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The driver accepts the settings but ends the stream once it runs (a disabled or disconnected device, one held exclusively by another program, or a driver fault)","locale":"en"},"10892":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Choose another** (another driver of the same device often works); with exclusive mode on, **Turn off exclusive mode**","locale":"en"},"10893":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Microphone permission denied**","locale":"en"},"10894":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The system has not granted microphone access","locale":"en"},"10895":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**How to grant access**: allow it in the system's privacy settings","locale":"en"},"10896":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Falling back to the default**","locale":"en"},"10897":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"The saved device is missing, so the system default will be used","locale":"en"},"10898":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"**Choose another** is suggested","locale":"en"},"10899":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-problems-and-repair-buttons","content":"A note may also appear below a device explaining how the saved device was found again, such as **\\{name} was found under another driver.** (a different driver, but the same device), or **\\{name} was not found: using the system default.**","locale":"en"},"10900":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#what-if-the-output-device-is-missing","content":"When you click **Start**, if the saved **Output** device is missing but the system default is available, rvc-next asks for confirmation before sending audio there (it could be your speakers): **The saved output device is missing; the system default would be used.** It continues only after you click **Start with the default output**. If the input or monitor device cannot be found at all, it reports an error; select another device first.","locale":"en"},"10901":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"The middle section contains the **Voice** picker and **Voice parameters** panel, using the same controls as **Convert**. See Voice parameters for their meanings. On the Live page:","locale":"en"},"10902":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"The panel says **Changes apply as you drag.** While running, adjusting **Pitch**, **Formant**, **Index strength**, **Consonant protection** or **Loudness match**, or switching **Pitch method**, immediately affects the converted audio without interrupting it.","locale":"en"},"10903":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"Switching to a pitch model that has not been downloaded keeps the current method active and reports the missing model.","locale":"en"},"10904":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"**Voice changes are hot swaps**: the new voice loads in the background while the old voice keeps converting. Once loaded, it switches seamlessly between blocks; HuBERT and the pitch model stay loaded. If loading fails, the original voice stays active and the picker returns to it.","locale":"en"},"10905":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"Voices with several speakers show a **Speaker** menu that can also be changed while running. Changing voices resets the speaker to the new voice's first speaker. If that speaker has a dedicated index (`spk<N>`), it switches to that index as well.","locale":"en"},"10906":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#voice-and-parameters","content":"Selecting a voice loads its default preset. The **Presets** button loads or saves presets; see Voice parameters.","locale":"en"},"10907":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Buffering and clean-up** controls how audio is divided into blocks for the model. Each slider's help ends with `(+N ms)`, showing its contribution to estimated latency.","locale":"en"},"10908":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"10909":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Range (default)","locale":"en"},"10910":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10911":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Latency contribution","locale":"en"},"10912":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Change while running","locale":"en"},"10913":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Block**","locale":"en"},"10914":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"20–1500 ms (250)","locale":"en"},"10915":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Audio processed per step. Longer is steadier; shorter is faster","locale":"en"},"10916":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"2 × block length","locale":"en"},"10917":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Rebuffer","locale":"en"},"10918":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Crossfade**","locale":"en"},"10919":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"10–150 ms (50)","locale":"en"},"10920":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Overlap between blocks for smooth joins","locale":"en"},"10921":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Equal to the crossfade","locale":"en"},"10922":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Rebuffer","locale":"en"},"10923":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Context**","locale":"en"},"10924":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"50–5000 ms (2500)","locale":"en"},"10925":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Past audio supplied with each block. More is smoother, but takes longer","locale":"en"},"10926":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"No extra latency, but more computation","locale":"en"},"10927":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Rebuffer","locale":"en"},"10928":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Input gate**","locale":"en"},"10929":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"−60–0 dB (−60)","locale":"en"},"10930":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Input below this level is muted; −60 dB disables it","locale":"en"},"10931":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"None","locale":"en"},"10932":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Immediate","locale":"en"},"10933":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Reduce input noise**","locale":"en"},"10934":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"On / Off (Off)","locale":"en"},"10935":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Reduces input noise before conversion","locale":"en"},"10936":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"min(crossfade, 40 ms)","locale":"en"},"10937":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Immediate","locale":"en"},"10938":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Reduce output noise**","locale":"en"},"10939":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"On / Off (Off)","locale":"en"},"10940":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Reduces noise in converted audio","locale":"en"},"10941":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"None","locale":"en"},"10942":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Immediate","locale":"en"},"10943":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Noise reduction strength**","locale":"en"},"10944":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"0–1 (0.9)","locale":"en"},"10945":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Shown while either noise reduction is on: how much quieter the noise gets; 1 removes the most and can take some voice with it","locale":"en"},"10946":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"None","locale":"en"},"10947":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Immediate","locale":"en"},"10948":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"**Phase-vocoder crossfade**","locale":"en"},"10949":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"On / Off (Off)","locale":"en"},"10950":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Joins blocks with a phase vocoder (from RVC's later realtime GUI, as Applio uses it) instead of the plain crossfade: when two blocks render a sound with different phase, a plain crossfade dips in level in the middle of the join; this one does not","locale":"en"},"10951":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"None","locale":"en"},"10952":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Immediate","locale":"en"},"10953":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"“Rebuffer” means that changing block length, crossfade or context while running closes the audio stream and reopens it with the new buffers. There is a brief interruption, but the voice is not reloaded.","locale":"en"},"10954":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Estimated latency ≈ block length + crossfade + 10 ms (alignment search) + block length (output prefill) + the device's input and output latency. Split streams add another block length; input noise reduction adds min(crossfade, 40 ms). The default settings (250 ms block length, 50 ms crossfade) give about 560 ms plus device latency with a duplex stream.","locale":"en"},"10955":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#buffering-and-noise-reduction","content":"Buffer changes made while stopped are saved directly to settings. Changes made while running are sent immediately to the active session and saved as well.","locale":"en"},"10956":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#effects","content":"Below the buffering settings, **Effects** is the same chain as on Convert (Effects), applied to each converted block before it plays; a reverb's tail and a compressor's envelope carry over from block to block. Changes apply from the next block without a rebuffer and are saved with the other Live settings; **Hear yourself** passes the input without them. **Pitch shift** is not offered here: in a stream pedalboard's pitch shift holds back about a second of audio; use the voice's **Pitch**.","locale":"en"},"10957":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"A bar stays fixed at the bottom of the page:","locale":"en"},"10958":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"The **Start / Stop** button. From the moment you click it, it shows each step of starting: **Checking the audio devices…**, **Starting the live process…** (first start only), **Loading PyTorch and the compute device…** (first start only), **Loading the voice…**, **Loading the index…**, **Loading HuBERT…**, **Loading the pitch model…**, **Warming up…**; steps with nothing to do are skipped. While stopping it shows **Stopping…**. With no voice selected, it is disabled and says **Choose a voice to start.**","locale":"en"},"10959":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"On error, an explanation appears above the button (**Stopped by an error**). It stays until the next **Start**, or until you close it with its **×** button.","locale":"en"},"10960":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"An audio device problem names the device at fault: **The input device is not available**, **The output device is not available** or **The monitor device is not available**, then the reason (in use by another program, not connected, refuses this format…) and the device's name, for example *The output device “Speakers (Realtek)” is in use by another program, or refused to open: …*. When the input and output share one stream and neither can be singled out, the message names both.","locale":"en"},"10961":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"If the live process itself stops (a crash in a driver or GPU library, the system running out of memory), the title is **A background process stopped unexpectedly**, and the message says how it ended (its exit code or signal) and, when its output shows it, why.","locale":"en"},"10962":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**Details** lists every field (device, driver, the driver's own message, exception, exit code…), with the traceback and the process's last output in full. **Copy** copies all of it as text, ready to paste into a bug report.","locale":"en"},"10963":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"The status bar updates 10 times per second and includes:","locale":"en"},"10964":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"10965":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"10966":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**Input** / **Output** meters","locale":"en"},"10967":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Input and converted output levels (RMS and peak)","locale":"en"},"10968":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**Load**","locale":"en"},"10969":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Inference time (the 95th percentile of the last 50 blocks; the median until 10 blocks are in) ÷ block length. Above 80%, the bar turns a warning color, indicating the model is close to falling behind real time; above 100% it reads **>100%** and the output has gaps. If a block is ever late, the session skips the stale input and trims the output buffer, so the delay does not stay","locale":"en"},"10970":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**Increase block to N ms**","locale":"en"},"10971":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Appears when load is too high. Uses the 95th percentile of recent inference times to estimate a block length that brings load back to about 70% (up to 1500 ms). Click to apply","locale":"en"},"10972":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**Latency N ms**","locale":"en"},"10973":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Current estimated end-to-end latency","locale":"en"},"10974":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**measured N ms**","locale":"en"},"10975":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"The measured latency, when a measurement fits the session's devices and block length","locale":"en"},"10976":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**N underruns** / **N overruns**","locale":"en"},"10977":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"Counts of the output buffer running empty (audible gaps) / the input buffer overflowing. Shown only after they occur","locale":"en"},"10978":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"**GPU N MB**","locale":"en"},"10979":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#start-stop-and-the-status-bar","content":"GPU memory used by the live process","locale":"en"},"10980":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"While Live runs, **Record** beside the start button writes the session to a WAV file in the outputs folder (`<date>/live/`). Choose what to keep:","locale":"en"},"10981":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"Choice","locale":"en"},"10982":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"File","locale":"en"},"10983":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"**Voice and input (stereo)**","locale":"en"},"10984":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"The input on the left channel, the converted voice on the right: for comparing them, or for editing either one later","locale":"en"},"10985":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"**Converted voice**","locale":"en"},"10986":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"The converted voice alone, mono","locale":"en"},"10987":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"**Input only**","locale":"en"},"10988":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"Your input alone, mono (after **Input level**)","locale":"en"},"10989":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#record","content":"The button then reads **Stop recording · 0:12**. The recording ends when you stop it, when Live stops, or when the sample rate changes; it then appears under **Recordings** on the Live page and in every outputs list, with the voice and parameters it was made with. Recording happens off the audio thread and never makes a block late. Output and monitor levels do not apply to it.","locale":"en"},"10990":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#the-live-chip-in-the-top-bar","content":"While a session is active (running, loading, reconnecting, etc.), every page's top bar shows a Live chip, for example **Live · 620 ms**. During loading and similar operations, it shows the current state instead. Click the chip to return to **Live**; the button on its right stops the session from any page. The chip turns red on reconnection or error.","locale":"en"},"10991":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"If you unplug headphones or a USB microphone while running:","locale":"en"},"10992":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"The session enters **Reconnecting the device…**. The top-bar chip shows this state and turns red, and the bar at the bottom says which device went: **The output device was lost**, with its name.","locale":"en"},"10993":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"The server rescans devices every 2 seconds.","locale":"en"},"10994":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"When the original device reappears (including under another driver), the stream reopens automatically and returns to **Running**, without reloading the voice.","locale":"en"},"10995":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#device-disconnection-and-automatic-reconnection","content":"This is controlled by **Settings › Audio › Reconnect a lost device automatically** (on by default). When disabled, a device disconnection stops the session immediately, and the error says which device was lost.","locale":"en"},"10996":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#sharing-the-gpu-with-other-jobs","content":"Live voice conversion holds the GPU while running on it:","locale":"en"},"10997":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-230","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#sharing-the-gpu-with-other-jobs","content":"Queued GPU jobs (conversion, separation, training, etc.) show **Waiting for the GPU** with a **Run anyway** button and the message **Live is using the GPU. Running both may cause audio glitches.**","locale":"en"},"10998":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-231","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#sharing-the-gpu-with-other-jobs","content":"**Free GPU memory** in the top bar is unavailable while the session is active. After stopping, the idle live process keeps its loaded models for a faster next start. You can then use **Free GPU memory** to unload them.","locale":"en"},"10999":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-232","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#sharing-the-gpu-with-other-jobs","content":"If GPU memory runs out, the session stops with **The GPU is not available or ran out of memory**. Both the live process and server automatically unload their loaded models. Close other programs using GPU memory and retry, or switch to CPU in **Settings › Compute**.","locale":"en"},"11000":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-233","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Get smooth audio first, then reduce latency.** Start with the default 250 ms block length and watch **Load**. Reduce the block length gradually only if load stays below 50%; increase it if load exceeds 80% or you see **underruns** (or click **Increase block to N ms**).","locale":"en"},"11001":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-234","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Use the same driver and sample rate for input and output**. A status of **one duplex stream** saves one block of latency.","locale":"en"},"11002":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-235","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Use a low-latency driver**: prefer WASAPI or ASIO on Windows, JACK or ALSA on Linux. Select it in **Advanced › Driver**.","locale":"en"},"11003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-236","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Context** adds no latency but increases computation per block. If load is high, try reducing it from 2500 ms.","locale":"en"},"11004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-237","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Crossfade** contributes directly to latency; 50 ms is usually enough. **Reduce input noise** adds up to another 40 ms.","locale":"en"},"11005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-238","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"For pitch methods, pm is fastest and RMVPE has the best quality. Try pm on a weaker GPU.","locale":"en"},"11006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-239","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#tips-for-reducing-latency","content":"**Settings › Compute › CUDA Graph for Live** is enabled by default on GPU and can reduce per-block overhead.","locale":"en"},"11007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-240","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#asio-windows","content":"Professional audio interfaces often provide ASIO drivers, usually with lower latency than WASAPI. ASIO is not listed by default. To enable it:","locale":"en"},"11008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-241","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#asio-windows","content":"Open **Settings › Audio** and enable **Enable ASIO drivers (Windows)**.","locale":"en"},"11009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-242","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#asio-windows","content":"Return to **Live** and click **Refresh devices**. Devices supporting ASIO will use it as the recommended driver; you can also select it manually in **Advanced › Driver**.","locale":"en"},"11010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-243","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#asio-windows","content":"The live background process starts on first use and stays running. If ASIO devices fail to open after toggling the ASIO setting, restart the rvc-next server so the live process picks up the new setting.","locale":"en"},"11011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-244","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#run-from-the-command-line","content":"You can use live voice conversion without opening the web UI. Devices and parameters default to the settings saved there:","locale":"en"},"11012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-live-245","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-live#run-from-the-command-line","content":"`live run` also supports `--block-ms`, `--crossfade-ms`, `--context-ms`, `--threshold-db`, `--denoise-strength`, `--phase-vocoder`, `--input-gain`, `--record both|converted|input`, `--allow-fallback` and other options. See Command reference for the full list.","locale":"en"},"11013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"page","content":"Model management","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models","locale":"en"},"11014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"The Models page manages all model files used by rvc-next: your voices, base models for training, vocal separation models, and required assets such as HuBERT and RMVPE. There are five tabs at the top:","locale":"en"},"11015":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-library","content":"Voice library","locale":"en"},"11016":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#browse-and-filter","content":"Browse and filter","locale":"en"},"11017":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Voice details","locale":"en"},"11018":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Delete and hide","locale":"en"},"11019":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-voice-library-on-disk","content":"The voice library on disk","locale":"en"},"11020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-models","content":"Import models","locale":"en"},"11021":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#recognized-files","content":"Recognized files","locale":"en"},"11022":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-steps","content":"Import steps","locale":"en"},"11023":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":