":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**About**","locale":"en"},"11061":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Edit **Name**, **Description** and **Tags** (separated by commas). For voices with several speakers, you can also name each **Speaker N**. Click **Save** when finished.","locale":"en"},"11062":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Below are **Sample rate**, **Version**, **Pitch guidance**, **Speakers**, **File**, **Size** and **Stored info**. Voices with one speaker show **Single speaker · N embedding slots**. Trained voices usually have 109 embedding slots; this does not mean they have several speakers. A voice counts as having several speakers only if speaker information is recorded in the model.","locale":"en"},"11063":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Index**","locale":"en"},"11064":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Lists attached indexes: `default` is the index for the whole voice; `spk<N>` is dedicated to one speaker. Click **Detach** to remove one.","locale":"en"},"11065":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Voices with several speakers show an **Index** dropdown to select whether the next attached index is `default` or a speaker-specific index.","locale":"en"},"11066":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Attach index**: drop an `.index` file here or click to select one.","locale":"en"},"11067":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Server path to an .index**: enter a server path directly, then click **Add** (shown only on the server machine or when an access token is set).","locale":"en"},"11068":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Build from experiment**: select a training experiment and build an index for this voice from its extracted features (the experiment must have completed **Features**).","locale":"en"},"11069":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Every attachment checks that the index fits the voice. Empty indexes with no vectors (the original's `trained_*.index`) and indexes with a mismatched version (256 dimensions for v1, 768 for v2) are rejected.","locale":"en"},"11070":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Default parameters**","locale":"en"},"11071":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"Each voice has a default preset, created on import from the default parameters in settings. Selecting the voice on another page automatically loads these parameters. Adjust them here and click **Save**. See Voice parameters for their meanings.","locale":"en"},"11072":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Test**","locale":"en"},"11073":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#voice-details","content":"**Convert a short clip with the default parameters.** Select audio and click **Preview 15 s**. Results appear below, ready to play or compare with the source audio.","locale":"en"},"11074":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Library voices: **Delete** asks **Move \\{name} to the trash?** The voice folder is moved to `trash/` in the data folder.","locale":"en"},"11075":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Legacy voices: the button becomes **Hide**, asking **Hide \\{name}? The file in the RVC install is not touched.** Use **Show hidden** to see them again.","locale":"en"},"11076":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#delete-and-hide","content":"Downloaded demo voices: after deletion, you can download them again in **Assets**.","locale":"en"},"11077":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-voice-library-on-disk","content":"By default, the voice library is in `models/` in the data folder (change this in **Settings › Storage › Voices**):","locale":"en"},"11078":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#import-models","content":"The **Voices**, **Base models** and **Separation models** tabs each have a drop zone at the top. All three use the same import workflow, so **any drop zone works**: rvc-next identifies each file by its **contents** (rather than its name or extension), then decides where it belongs.","locale":"en"},"11079":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models