k (tested on CPU).","locale":"en"},"11483":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"page","content":"Vocal separation","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate","locale":"en"},"11484":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate","content":"The Separate page uses RoFormer models to split audio: separate songs into vocals and accompaniment, remove reverb from vocals, and separate lead and backing vocals. Multiple steps can be chained into one preset, and any resulting stem can be sent directly to Convert.","locale":"en"},"11485":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#usage-steps","content":"Usage steps","locale":"en"},"11486":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#presets","content":"Presets","locale":"en"},"11487":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#how-to-choose","content":"How to choose","locale":"en"},"11488":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#imported-separation-models","content":"Imported separation models","locale":"en"},"11489":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#download-separation-models","content":"Download separation models","locale":"en"},"11490":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#jobs","content":"Jobs","locale":"en"},"11491":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#results","content":"Results","locale":"en"},"11492":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#command-line","content":"Command line","locale":"en"},"11493":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate","content":"From top to bottom, the page has three sections: **Inputs**, **Preset** (including **Format**) and **Results**. The fixed bottom action bar contains job cards and the **Separate** button.","locale":"en"},"11494":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate","content":"If your goal is “separate vocals → convert → add accompaniment back”, you do not need to start here: enable **Separate first** and **Add accompaniment back** on **Convert** to do it in one operation; see Convert › Optional steps. Use this page when you need to **keep** the separated stems, or inspect or process them first.","locale":"en"},"11495":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#usage-steps","content":"Add audio in **Inputs**: drop files, click **Server files** to choose server files or an entire folder (processing audio files at its top level), or click **Earlier results**. This works exactly as on Convert's input section.","locale":"en"},"11496":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#usage-steps","content":"Select a card in **Preset**. Each card shows the preset name, description and output stems, such as “Stems: vocals, instrumental”.","locale":"en"},"11497":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-separate-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-separate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-separate#usage-steps","content":"Choose an output **Format**: WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A or OGG (Opus, always 