ersion**","locale":"en"},"11876":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"v1 / v2","locale":"en"},"11877":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"v2 uses 768-dimensional features and is recommended; v1 uses 256 dimensions","locale":"en"},"11878":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Content features**","locale":"en"},"11879":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"ContentVec (RVC, default) / SPIN / SPIN v2 / Chinese, Japanese, Korean HuBERT","locale":"en"},"11880":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"The model that reads what is said. The others come from Applio: SPIN keeps less of the speaker's own voice in the features, the language HuBERTs suit those languages. All but ContentVec and SPIN are for v2 only. The voice records its choice, so conversion uses the same; the model downloads on first use (about 380 MB)","locale":"en"},"11881":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Pitch method**","locale":"en"},"11882":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"RMVPE (best) / pm (fast) / FCPE / CREPE / CREPE tiny / SwiftF0","locale":"en"},"11883":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Method for extracting pitch from training data; unavailable when pitch guidance is off. New experiments default to RMVPE with an available CUDA GPU, otherwise pm. The original offers only pm and RMVPE for training; the others are the conversion methods of the same names (see Pitch method)","locale":"en"},"11884":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Epochs**","locale":"en"},"11885":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"≥ 1","locale":"en"},"11886":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Total training epochs","locale":"en"},"11887":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Batch size**","locale":"en"},"11888":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"≥ 1; leave blank for **Automatic**","locale":"en"},"11889":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Automatic takes the smallest GPU's memory (GiB) ÷ 2, rounded down, as in the original; 1 without a GPU. It is per GPU: with two GPUs each one trains on this many clips at a time (the original gave each GPU this times the number of GPUs)","locale":"en"},"11890":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Save every N epochs**","locale":"en"},"11891":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"≥ 1","locale":"en"},"11892":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Number of epochs between checkpoints","locale":"en"},"11893":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**GPUs**","locale":"en"},"11894":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"`auto`, `cpu` or GPU IDs such as `0-1`","locale":"en"},"11895":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"GPUs used for training, saved in the experiment. New experiments use `training.gpus` from settings. `auto` uses all available CUDA GPUs; `cpu` uses only CPU","locale":"en"},"11896":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Pitch guidance**","locale":"en"},"11897":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11898":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"When off, the trained voice has no pitch guidance (suited to speech rather than singing), and the **Pitch** stage is skipped","locale":"en"},"11899":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Cache the dataset in GPU memory**","locale":"en"},"11900":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11901":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Stores the entire training dataset in GPU memory; can speed up training for small datasets with enough GPU memory","locale":"en"},"11902":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Save a voice at every save point**","locale":"en"},"11903":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11904":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Saves a small, directly usable model in `weights/` alongside each checkpoint, for comparing different epochs","locale":"en"},"11905":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Keep only the latest checkpoint**","locale":"en"},"11906":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11907":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Keeps only one pair of G/D checkpoints (`G_2333333.pth`/`D_2333333.pth`, as in the original), saving disk space","locale":"en"},"11908":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Render a sample at every save**","locale":"en"},"11909":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On (default) / Off","locale":"en"},"11910":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"At every save, the voice as it is renders one training clip (the longest slice) into `previews/`; **Results › Samples** lists them","locale":"en"},"11911":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Under **Advanced**:","locale":"en"},"11912":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"11913":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Options","locale":"en"},"11914":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"11915":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Precision**","locale":"en"},"11916":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Automatic / Full (fp32) / bf16","locale":"en"},"11917":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Automatic trains in half precision (fp16, with loss scaling) when every chosen GPU supports it, as the original; bf16 needs no loss scaling and suits recent NVIDIA (RTX 30 series on), AMD and Intel GPUs (without bf16 support, training falls back to fp32 and says so in the log); fp32 is the slowest and the most exact","locale":"en"},"11918":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**TF32 maths**","locale":"en"},"11919":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11920":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Lets NVIDIA GPUs from the RTX 30 series on use TF32 for full-precision matrix maths: faster, slightly less exact","locale":"en"},"11921":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Save memory (gradient checkpointing)**","locale":"en"},"11922":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11923":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Recomputes the generator's upsampling and residual blocks and each discriminator in the backward pass instead of keeping their activations: for GPUs with little memory, at the cost of slower steps","locale":"en"},"11924":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**New speaker vectors**","locale":"en"},"11925":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"On / Off","locale":"en"},"11926":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Starts each speaker of the experiment from a new random vector (at the size of the base model's) instead of the base model's own; in every official base model speakers 0 and 1 have the same vector, so two speakers of a multi-speaker voice would start out alike. From Applio","locale":"en"},"11927":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"The fp16 loss scale is saved with the checkpoints, so a resumed run continues from it instead of starting the scale again. Trained voices carry the epoch, step and date, and the author from **Settings › Training › Author** when set; **About** on a voice's page shows them.","locale":"en"},"11928":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"**Base model**: training starts from a base model.","locale":"en"},"11929":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"The default, **Chosen from the rate, version and pitch guidance**, uses the corresponding official base model.","locale":"en"},"11930":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Base models imported in **Models › Base models** also appear here, but **Only base models of this rate, version and pitch guidance are listed.** Models without a discriminator (D) are marked **no D**. If a change to sample rate, version or pitch guidance makes the selected base model incompatible, the selection automatically returns to the default.","locale":"en"},"11931":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-2-settings","content":"Click **Save** when finished. If required files have not been downloaded (official base models, HuBERT, and the RMVPE model when using RMVPE), the **Save** button is replaced by **Needs …** and **Download (size)**. Download them before saving.","locale":"en"},"11932":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Each completed stage records an input “fingerprint.” After saving changes, affected completed stages are marked **Out of date**, with the message **Inputs changed since this stage ran.**","locale":"en"},"11933":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"**Run all** also recalculates every completed stage's fingerprint. Even without changing settings on the page, adding, deleting or replacing recordings directly in the dataset folder causes slicing and all subsequent stages to rerun. Increasing only the **Epochs** continues training without rerunning earlier stages.","locale":"en"},"11934":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Change","locale":"en"},"11935":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"First stage marked out of date","locale":"en"},"11936":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Dataset folder or speaker table","locale":"en"},"11937":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Slice","locale":"en"},"11938":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Clean-up preset","locale":"en"},"11939":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Clean-up","locale":"en"},"11940":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Sample rate, **Slicing**","locale":"en"},"11941":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Slice","locale":"en"},"11942":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Pitch guidance, pitch method","locale":"en"},"11943":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Pitch","locale":"en"},"11944":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Model version","locale":"en"},"11945":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Features","locale":"en"},"11946":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Training parameters such as epochs or batch size","locale":"en"},"11947":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"None (increasing epochs makes **Run all** continue training)","locale":"en"},"11948":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#which-stages-must-rerun-after-settings-change","content":"Rerunning a stage also marks subsequent completed stages **Out of date**.","locale":"en"},"11949":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Run** lists cards for all stages:","locale":"en"},"11950":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Stage","locale":"en"},"11951":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"11952":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"When it runs","locale":"en"},"11953":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Clean-up**","locale":"en"},"11954":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Cleans the dataset with the selected separation preset","locale":"en"},"11955":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Only when a clean-up preset is selected","locale":"en"},"11956":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Slice**","locale":"en"},"11957":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Splits audio at silence and resamples it into training clips","locale":"en"},"11958":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"11959":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Pitch**","locale":"en"},"11960":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Extracts each clip's pitch with pm or RMVPE","locale":"en"},"11961":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Only with pitch guidance enabled","locale":"en"},"11962":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Features**","locale":"en"},"11963":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Extracts content features with HuBERT","locale":"en"},"11964":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"11965":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Train**","locale":"en"},"11966":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Trains the generator and discriminator, saving checkpoints as configured","locale":"en"},"11967":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"11968":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Index**","locale":"en"},"11969":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Builds a retrieval index from features (`added_*.index`)","locale":"en"},"11970":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Always","locale":"en"},"11971":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"Each card shows its state (**Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date**, **Failed**, **Skipped**), processed count and completion time, or an error message on failure.","locale":"en"},"11972":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Run all**: runs only incomplete, out-of-date or failed stages. If **Train** is done but you increased **Epochs**, it continues to the new epoch count. If all stages are done and inputs are unchanged, it reports that no stages need to run.","locale":"en"},"11973":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"A single stage: click **Run this stage** on its card. Completed stages show **Run again**, which forces another run.","locale":"en"},"11974":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"**Stop**: appears while running and cancels the current job. The cancelled stage returns to **Not run**; completed stages are kept.","locale":"en"},"11975":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"When **Train** starts, if the experiment folder already contains G/D checkpoints, training resumes from the latest pair rather than starting over. Create a new experiment to train entirely from scratch.","locale":"en"},"11976":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-3-run","content":"While running, the **Run** step shows a job card and a progress bar appears below the step bar. The same job appears in the top-bar **Jobs** panel, where you can read its log. Training queues as a GPU job: if live voice conversion is using the GPU, it shows **Waiting for the GPU**. You can click **Run anyway** (which may cause live audio glitches).","locale":"en"},"11977":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"The **Loss** chart shows training loss curves (the horizontal axis is step). Total losses `g_total` and `d_total` come first, followed by components such as `mel`, `kl`, `fm` and `gen`. Curves update live during training. **Gradient norms** below shows `grad_g` and `grad_d`, the size of the generator's and the discriminator's gradients at each step: a sudden jump often comes before a run goes wrong.","locale":"en"},"11978":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"**Samples** (with **Render a sample at every save** on) lists the training clip as the voice rendered it at each save, labelled by epoch; A/B plays the clip itself, so you can hear the voice approach it, and hear when more epochs stop helping.","locale":"en"},"11979":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"**Checkpoints** lists the experiment's G checkpoints and small models (`.pth` files in `weights/`). Each entry shows its type, epoch count and file size:","locale":"en"},"11980":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"**Try**: sends this entry to **Convert** as a temporary voice (with the experiment's index), so you can immediately convert a clip and hear the result. Temporary voices do not appear in the voice library. G checkpoints are automatically extracted into small models first (stored in the experiment's `.try/` folder; each checkpoint is extracted only once).","locale":"en"},"11981":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"**Export as voice**: exports this entry to the voice library.","locale":"en"},"11982":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#step-4-results","content":"The **Export as voice** button at the top right of the list exports the latest result (preferring the latest small model, otherwise the latest G checkpoint).","locale":"en"},"11983":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"Click **Export as voice** (at the top of the list or beside a checkpoint).","locale":"en"},"11984":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"Enter a **Voice name**, defaulting to the experiment name.","locale":"en"},"11985":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"Click **Export**. When finished, it shows **Exported as a voice**.","locale":"en"},"11986":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"During export:","locale":"en"},"11987":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"A selected G checkpoint is first extracted into a small model;","locale":"en"},"11988":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"The experiment's indexes (`added_*.index`) are attached to the new voice;","locale":"en"},"11989":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"Experiments with several speakers write the speaker names into the model.","locale":"en"},"11990":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#export-to-the-voice-library","content":"The exported voice appears in **Models › Voices** and can be used in **Convert**, **Live** and other pages.","locale":"en"},"11991":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"Prepare at least 10 minutes of clean recordings without accompaniment and put them in one folder.","locale":"en"},"11992":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"Create a **New experiment**, select the dataset folder, **Scan dataset**, and address problem files such as **clipped** or **silent** recordings.","locale":"en"},"11993":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"In **Settings**, check the sample rate (40k is usually enough), version v2 and pitch guidance (required for singing).","locale":"en"},"11994":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"Download the requested base models and other models, then **Save**.","locale":"en"},"11995":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"Click **Run all** in **Run**, and watch the loss curves in **Results**.","locale":"en"},"11996":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"With **Save a voice at every save point** enabled, **Try** small models from different epochs and **Export as voice** for the best one.","locale":"en"},"11997":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#recommended-workflow","content":"If the result needs improvement, increase **Epochs** and **Run all** again. Training resumes from the previous checkpoint.","locale":"en"},"11998":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#command-line","content":"Training can also be done entirely from the command line, using the same experiments as the web UI:","locale":"en"},"11999":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-train-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-train#command-line","content":"See Command reference for more options.","locale":"en"},"12000":{"id":"/en/docs/guide","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"page","content":"User guide overview","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide","locale":"en"},"12001":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"This section explains how to use each page of the RVC Next web interface.","locale":"en"},"12002":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide#read-these-two-pages-first","content":"Read these two pages first","locale":"en"},"12003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"Pages","locale":"en"},"12004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Where to start for common tasks","locale":"en"},"12005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"This section explains how to use each page of the RVC Next web interface. If you have not installed or started RVC Next yet, read Quick start first. Each page also has corresponding `rvc-next` commands; see Command line.","locale":"en"},"12006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#read-these-two-pages-first","content":"**Interface overview**: the navigation bar; the jobs, GPU memory and theme buttons in the top bar; the fixed action bar at the bottom of each page; and the job cards and results list shared across all pages. Once you have read it, you will not need to relearn the common parts of the other pages.","locale":"en"},"12007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#read-these-two-pages-first","content":"**Voice parameters**: meanings, ranges, defaults and adjustment tips for pitch, formant, pitch method, index strength, consonant protection, loudness match and speaker, plus how to save presets and set a voice's default parameters. **Convert**, **Live** and voice details use the same parameter panel, so this page applies to all of them.","locale":"en"},"12008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Conversion** (**Convert** in the navigation bar): convert audio files or an entire folder to the selected voice. Inputs can be dropped files, files or folders on the server, or earlier results. Optional steps let you separate vocals first and add the accompaniment back, making a cover of an entire song in one operation. You can also choose the output format and sample rate. Listen with **Preview 15 s** before converting in full.","locale":"en"},"12009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Live voice conversion** (**Live** in the navigation bar): convert your voice live through the server computer's microphone and output device. The page includes a device panel (input, output, monitor, level meter and test tone), a voice and parameters (changes apply as you drag), and **Buffering and clean-up** settings that control latency and stability. While running, a live status chip stays visible in the top bar. Use Live in other apps sends the converted voice into Discord, Zoom, OBS or a game through a virtual audio device on Windows, macOS and Linux.","locale":"en"},"12010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Vocal separation** (**Separate** in the navigation bar): use built-in RoFormer models to split songs into vocals and accompaniment, remove reverb, or separate lead and backing vocals. Chain presets perform multiple steps in one operation. Results are grouped by source file, and any stem can be sent directly to Convert.","locale":"en"},"12011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Training** (**Train** in the navigation bar): train a voice on your own dataset. Each experiment is organized into four steps: **Dataset**, **Settings**, **Run** and **Results**. Execution has six stages: clean-up, slicing, pitch, features, training and index. Each can be rerun individually; changing inputs marks the relevant stages as out of date. During training, you can view loss curves, try checkpoints at any time and export them as voices.","locale":"en"},"12012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Model management** (**Models** in the navigation bar): five tabs, **Voices**, **Base models**, **Separation models**, **Assets** and **Tools**. Import `.pth`, `.index` and `.zip` files, attach indexes to voices, read voices from an original RVC installation, download HuBERT, RMVPE, base models, separation models and demo voices, merge two voices or extract a voice from a training checkpoint.","locale":"en"},"12013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#pages","content":"**Settings** (**Settings** at the bottom of the navigation bar): language, server address and port, access token, compute device and precision, audio driver, folder locations, download repository and endpoint, training defaults and appearance.","locale":"en"},"12014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"I want to…","locale":"en"},"12015":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Read","locale":"en"},"12016":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Change the voice in a speech clip","locale":"en"},"12017":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Conversion","locale":"en"},"12018":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Change the voice in a song and keep its accompaniment","locale":"en"},"12019":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Convert › Separate first","locale":"en"},"12020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Get only a song's vocals or accompaniment","locale":"en"},"12021":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Vocal separation","locale":"en"},"12022":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Change my voice while streaming or in voice chat","locale":"en"},"12023":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Live voice conversion, then Use Live in other apps","locale":"en"},"12024":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Fix a voice that is too shrill or muffled, sounds robotic or has unclear articulation","locale":"en"},"12025":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Voice parameters","locale":"en"},"12026":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Import a downloaded model","locale":"en"},"12027":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Model management","locale":"en"},"12028":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Train my own voice","locale":"en"},"12029":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Training","locale":"en"},"12030":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Use models already in the original RVC","locale":"en"},"12031":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide#where-to-start-for-common-tasks","content":"Migrating from the original RVC","locale":"en"},"12032":{"id":"/en/docs","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"page","content":"RVC Next","breadcrumbs":["RVC Next Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs","locale":"en"},"12033":{"id":"/en/docs-0","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"An integrated rewrite of Retrieval-based Voice Conversion (RVC): conversion, live voice conversion, vocal separation, training and model management.","locale":"en"},"12034":{"id":"/en/docs-1","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"What it can do","locale":"en"},"12035":{"id":"/en/docs-2","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs#documentation-sections","content":"Documentation sections","locale":"en"},"12036":{"id":"/en/docs-3","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"RVC Next is an integrated rewrite of Retrieval-based-Voice-Conversion-WebUI (RVC): conversion in **Convert**, live voice conversion in **Live**, vocal separation in **Separate**, training in **Train** and model management in **Models**, provided by one server, one web interface and one command line (`rvc-next`). The numerical code is ported line by line from the original, with comparison tests ensuring identical output.","locale":"en"},"12037":{"id":"/en/docs-4","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Getting started\" href=\"/docs/quick-start\"