e` (`core/models/service.py`) manages them."],[12145,"A voice library, indexes, base models, separation models, required asset downloads and tools for merging voices and extracting voices from checkpoints"],[11159,"A voice trained on another **content-feature model** (Applio's \"embedder\": SPIN, SPIN v2, or the Chinese, Japanese or Korean HuBERT) converts with that model, as it was trained. **About** shows **Content features**; the first conversion asks to download the model (about 380 MB, from Applio's repository; also under **Assets › Content-feature models**)."],[6175,"A voice with speaker information in its `.pth` is multi-speaker. Its card shows **N speakers**, and the parameter panel includes a **Speaker** option. On the command line, use `--speaker <id>`; `rvc-next model info <voice> --speakers` lists speakers. You can name them with `rvc-next model edit <voice> --speaker-name 0=Alice`. Multi-speaker voices can also have a separate index for each speaker (`--speaker`). Live voice conversion uses the selected speaker too."],[11370,"A voice's index (`.index` file) stores features from its training data. During conversion, RVC finds the features closest to the input and mixes them in at this ratio, making the result closer to the training voice."],[11589,"About"],[11193,"About 305–436 MB each"],[11190,"About 350–420 MB per group"],[6312,"Above 80% load, the bar turns red and shows **Increase block to \\{ms} ms** (the suggested value targets about 70% load, capped at 1500 milliseconds). Click to apply;"],[7802,"Access control"],[7906,"Access control has two layers: `SecurityMiddleware` handles who can connect, while `require_local` in routes guards operations that only make sense for a browser on the server machine."],[7917,"Access token"],[10437,"Access token"],[11579,"Access token"],[6401,"Access token (optional)"],[7414,"Access token; once set, all API and WebSocket requests must carry it"],[11548,"Accompaniment"],[6685,"Accompaniment gain in dB"],[10874,"Action"],[10034,"Actual use"],[7740,"Add `--help` at any level to see help. Entering just a group name (such as `rvc-next model`) also shows that group's help."],[8024,"Add a route in the appropriate `api/routers/<resource>.py`: set `operation_id`, use `ServicesDep` in the signature, and add `dependencies=[LocalDep]` for revealing files; use `spool` + `read_chunks` for uploads and declare `openapi_extra=RAW_BODY`. Put fixed paths before wildcard routes."],[11495,"Add audio in **Inputs**: drop files, click **Server files** to choose server files or an entire folder (processing audio files at its top level), or click **Earlier results**. This works exactly as on Convert's input section."],[8433,"Add demo voices to `voices`; never change an `id` once published, since downloaded voices use it to match catalog entries."],[11023,"Add from a link"],[10323,"Add inputs"],[10399,"Add inputs, choose a voice and set **Pitch**;"],[10696,"Add one of these blocks to `~/.asoundrc` (create the file if it doesn't exist; keep anything already in it). Choose by what rvc-next's **Output** menu already lists: **pipewire** means the PipeWire ALSA plugin is installed (package `pipewire-alsa`), **pulse** means the PulseAudio one (`libasound2-plugins` on Debian and Ubuntu, `alsa-plugins-pulseaudio` on Fedora, `alsa-plugins` on Arch)."],[8430,"Add or update an entry in `assets` in `catalog.json`: `path` uses a relative path in the original `assets/` layout; `sources` lists at least one repository; `size` and `sha256` must match the manifest—downloads use size to determine completion and hashes to detect corruption."],[6682,"Add the accompaniment back (needs `--separate`)"],[8515,"Add the command to the user documentation's Command reference."],[10494,"Add this result to the current page's inputs for another pass"],[6465,"Added original RVC installations;"],[11084,"Added to the voice library"],[8444,"Adding a command"],[9948,"Adding a screen"],[10379,"Adding accompaniment back produces stereo output; if mixing would clip, the overall level is automatically lowered to prevent clipping."],[7812,"Adding an endpoint"],[8263,"Adding or updating assets"],[10048,"Adding, removing, and reordering items (`TransitionGroup`)"],[6399,"Address and port"],[11610,"Address the server listens on. **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**"],[6577,"Address to bind"],[10247,"Address to bind; defaults to `127.0.0.1`, allowing access only from the local machine"],[6119,"Address to bind; defaults to the `server.host` setting (`127.0.0.1`)"],[6417,"Address to bind. `0.0.0.0` listens on all IPv4 interfaces; `::` listens on all IPv6 interfaces. You can also specify the address of one interface"],[7398,"Address to bind. A non-local address requires an access token first"],[11690,"Address used to access repositories: **Hugging Face**, **hf-mirror.com** or **Custom**"],[7499,"Address used when `source` is `custom`"],[6091,"Address, port and access token"],[11649,"Adds ASIO drivers to the device list (requires an audio interface with an ASIO driver). After enabling it, click **Refresh devices** on **Live**"],[10304,"Adjust **Voice parameters**. For your first conversion, focus only on **Pitch**:"],[11208,"Adjust **Weight of the first voice** (0–1, default 0.5): result = weight × first + (1 − weight) × second."],[10401,"Adjust parameters based on the result (see Voice parameters) and preview again;"],[10330,"Adjust voice parameters"],[10774,"Advanced"],[12164,"Advanced"],[12118,"After a fresh installation, `doctor` reports that HuBERT and RMVPE are not installed and provides commands such as `rvc-next assets download hubert`. This is normal; the next page covers it. Both commands support `--json` output."],[8887,"After a rerun completes, later `done` stages outside this run are also marked `stale`. Rerunning a `stale` stage passes `clean: true` to the worker to discard old output; indexing also has its own fingerprint file (`index_fingerprint.json`, see Engine) and rebuilds when features change—the original skips whenever any `added_*.index` exists."],[6343,"After adding the original installation as an \"Original RVC installation\" (`paths.legacy_roots` in settings), its voices are **read directly without copying**:"],[11444,"After adjusting parameters, click **Presets** › **Save as preset**."],[10649,"After changing devices in Windows, or if a strip stays silent, use **Menu › Restart Audio Engine**."],[11681,"After changing folders or browsable locations, click **Save** at the bottom right."],[11561,"After choosing a preset, if its models are not downloaded, the **Separate** button in the action bar is replaced by a notice such as “**Needs Separation: Vocals**” and a **Download** button. Click to download."],[10407,"After clicking, you can continue changing parameters or inputs and submit again; the new job is queued afterward. See Interface overview › Jobs for general information about jobs."],[9375,"After device loss, the worker reports `DeviceLost`, stops the session and enters `reconnecting`, then waits for `SetDevices`; core handles re-enumeration and reopening on `exact`/`matched` (see Core services). On a processing-thread error or OOM during loading/prewarming, the worker unloads all its models first, then reports `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason = \"out_of_memory\"`)."],[8941,"After every actual change, `SettingsService` calculates changed dotted keys with `changed_keys()`, notifying `on_change` (new settings) and `on_keys_change` (key names). Changes can come from `update()` or another process writing `settings.toml`: reading `settings` compares mtime and size at most once per `FILE_CHECK_INTERVAL` (1 second), rereading on change (parse or validation failures log a warning and retain previous settings); `update()` forces a check before writing, merging onto current file contents. The key listener registered in `core/context.py` publishes `settings_changed` and calls `models.rescan()` when `paths.*` changes."],[8000,"After FastAPI generates its schema, `RvcNextAPI.openapi()` in `api/openapi.py` adds each event class's JSON Schema (`mode=\"serialization\"`) to `components.schemas`, promotes nested `$defs` to peer components, and adds a `ServerEvents` object: property names are event names, and values reference event schemas. Components are sorted by name for stable output."],[11081,"After import"],[10227,"After installing RVC Next, follow the entire first-run process: start the web interface, learn where data is stored, download HuBERT and RMVPE for conversion, get a demo voice and complete a conversion. Each step includes both web interface and command-line instructions."],[7706,"After its first start, the live worker stays running until the server exits. These settings are read when it starts, so changes require a server restart"],[9326,"Aliases following system defaults, such as `Microsoft Sound Mapper` and `Primary Sound Driver`, are omitted; virtual devices (VB-Audio, VoiceMeeter, BlackHole, Loopback, Soundflower, null sink…) get `is_virtual`."],[7331,"All"],[8965,"All `AssetStatus`"],[12163,"All `rvc-next` commands, configuration files and environment variables"],[6557,"All commands accept these two options, which are omitted from the tables below:"],[8291,"All conversion and feature extraction (transformers format)"],[9596,"All conversion in the callback; `skip_head`/`return_length`; 1024-frame pitch cache"],[11046,"All downloadable files: HuBERT, the pitch models (RMVPE, FCPE, CREPE), base models, separation models and demo voices"],[6467,"All drives (`C:\\`, `D:\\`, etc. on Windows), or mounted volumes (`/Volumes/*` on macOS; `/media/<user>/*`, `/run/media/<user>/*`, `/mnt/*` on Linux). The system root `/` is excluded by default."],[9297,"All entry points share an `RLock`, so control-thread updates cannot interleave with the processing thread's `process()`."],[9617,"All existing user models; models written by rvc-next also work in the original"],[8360,"All files copied from the official repository are unchanged; catalog hashes were recalculated against a full download of the official repository (revision `e6d0c1a`) and all matched."],[8377,"All files exist, but one failed verification"],[7896,"All fixed paths in `routers/models.py` (`/catalog`, `/imports`, `/indexes`, `/base`, `/separation`, `/legacy-roots`…) precede `/{voice_id}`. FastAPI matches in registration order: new fixed paths must go above wildcard routes, or they will be treated as voice IDs. The same applies to `POST /zip` in `outputs`."],[9415,"All four workers use `python -m rvc_next.workers.<name> <request.json>` and share `workers/base.py:run_worker()`:"],[8769,"All import entry points—the Web UI drop zones, `PUT /models/imports/{sid}/files`, `POST /models/imports/{sid}/paths`, `rvc-next model import`, old one-step `PUT /models/import` and `POST /models/import-path`—use the same import session (`core/models/imports.py`). The goal: correctly pair `.pth` and `.index` files even when their names are unrelated, and independently import four model types (voices, indexes, base models, separation models)."],[9257,"All lengths use the device sample rate `sample_rate`, with `zc = sample_rate // 100` (10 ms); millisecond parameters are rounded to whole 10 ms units (`_frames`, the original's rounding):"],[8426,"All remaining model files in the archives are byte-identical to a file in the repository."],[10081,"All screens"],[10090,"All screens"],[7354,"All settings"],[11773,"All settings can also be viewed and changed from the command line. Changes are written to the same `settings.toml`:"],[7120,"All stages that need to run"],[10650,"All Voicemeeter devices run at A1's sample rate. Set Voicemeeter's playback and recording devices to the same format (48000 Hz) in the Sound Control Panel; then rvc-next shows **one duplex stream** when your microphone uses 48 kHz too."],[9209,"All writes use `torch_save()`, writing `.tmp` then `os.replace`, so a crash cannot leave a partial model."],[9183,"All; CPU on DirectML"],[9187,"All; CPU on DirectML"],[9179,"All; mel and decoding on CPU for DirectML"],[6400,"Allow other computers to connect"],[10545,"Allow the microphone"],[6451,"Allowed"],[6452,"Allowed"],[6454,"Allowed"],[6457,"Allowed"],[6460,"Allowed"],[8045,"Allowed `rvc_next` subpackages"],[8046,"Allowed third-party modules"],[6458,"Allowed, but only within the browsing scope"],[6455,"Allowed: nothing needs a folder on the server"],[8151,"Allows hard cancellation and a clean CUDA context; DDP also needs its own processes"],[9762,"Allows numpy 2: numpy 1.x has no Python 3.13 wheels"],[9914,"Alongside component and store unit tests, **rule tests** turn conventions into failing tests: `tokens.test.ts` (no hexadecimal colors outside `src/theme/`), `imports.test.ts` (modules import through `@/` aliases), `layout.test.ts` (text in filename rows gets `min-width: 0`, pages use one column of sections, and other layout rules), `i18n/i18n.test.ts` (matching `zh-CN` and `en` keys and placeholders, fixed terminology), `ui/motion/motion.test.ts` (works with full and reduced motion, view transitions), etc. See Web UI for individual descriptions."],[7685,"Also list output devices in the input menu, recorded as loopback inputs: what an output plays becomes the input (WASAPI loopback on Windows, PulseAudio/PipeWire monitors on Linux; not on macOS)"],[6181,"Also remember: these are devices on **the server computer**. Opening the Web UI from another computer or phone does not show or use that device's microphone; see Remote access and security."],[11772,"Also shows license information: RVC (MIT) · PyMSS (MIT) · rvc-next (GPL-3.0)."],[6382,"Also supported offline, using the live method; a formant value of 0 gives bit-identical results to the original"],[8858,"Always"],[8864,"Always"],[8867,"Always"],[8870,"Always"],[10489,"Always"],[10495,"Always"],[10498,"Always"],[10507,"Always"],[11958,"Always"],[11964,"Always"],[11967,"Always"],[11970,"Always"],[6256,"AMD cards on ROCm