ugging Face is difficult, change **Download endpoint** to **hf-mirror.com** in **Settings › Downloads**, or use the command line:"],[6163,"Downloads support resuming: after an interruption, downloading again continues from the `.part` file, with automatic retries on failure. **Model repository** can switch between `rvc-model` (default, including demo voices) and the official repository; both contain the same model files."],[8259,"Downloads, resume, and verification"],[10346,"Drag files onto “Drop audio files here”, or click the area to choose files in a dialog; you can select several at once. Common audio formats (WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG, OPUS, AAC, WMA, etc.) are supported. You can also drop video files directly; their audio track will be used."],[6356,"Drop `.pth`, `.index`, or `.zip` files into the import area in **Models** › **Voices**. For legacy voices, you can also click **Import all** under **Original RVC installs**."],[11101,"Drop files into a drop zone (or click to select). You can drop several files at once, such as a `.pth` with its `.index`, or a `.zip` containing both."],[10324,"Drop or select files"],[9416,"Duplicate real stdout for events, then redirect fd 1 to stderr—third-party `print` output stays as log text instead of entering the event stream."],[11986,"During export:"],[11166,"Each added install has two buttons:"],[11560,"Each built-in preset needs one or more separation models, about 305 MB each (the two Vocals models) or about 436 MB each (the other three). To get them:"],[11971,"Each card shows its state (**Not run**, **Running**, **Done**, **Out of date**, **Failed**, **Skipped**), processed count and completion time, or an error message on failure."],[9490,"Each change has a reason found in the original code; with default parameters, changes affecting numerical results do not alter golden results."],[10403,"Each click on **Convert** (or **Preview 15 s**) creates **one** job containing all current inputs. Its card appears in the bottom action bar:"],[11565,"Each click on **Separate** creates **one** job for all current inputs, with a title such as `Separate song.flac · Vocals` (or `Separate song.flac and 2 more · Vocals` for multiple inputs). Each input is one step. Separation runs in a separate worker process; you can **Cancel** at any time, **Retry** after failure and click **Log** to view the process."],[11932,"Each completed stage records an input “fingerprint.” After saving changes, affected completed stages are marked **Out of date**, with the message **Inputs changed since this stage ran.**"],[10819,"Each device takes a full row; its menu opens as wide as the row, and long names wrap rather than being cut off. Under each name is a second line: the recommended driver, the channel count and the default sample rate."],[9584,"Each entry point builds its own engine from shared `infer/` code; the live DSP chain exists in three copies in `realtime_gui.py`, `infer/rtrvc.py`, and the VST worker, F0 postprocessing in `pipeline`, `rtrvc`, and `extract_f0`, and PyMSS is both bundled and installed as a pip package (`tools/pymss_webui.py` puts `tools/` first on `sys.path`, selecting the bundled version). rvc-next consolidates these into one copy each."],[8122,"Each feature"],[11674,"Each field shows **Default: \\{path}** below it. Leave it empty to use the default location within the data folder."],[9324,"Each group is a physical device, with `variants` sorted by driver rank and the recommended driver first. Ranks (`HOST_API_RANKS`, lower is better): Windows ASIO → WASAPI → WDM-KS → DirectSound → MME; macOS Core Audio; Linux JACK → ALSA → Pulse → OSS."],[10824,"Each menu item represents one **physical device**, showing its full name. On Windows, the same microphone can appear under several drivers, such as MME, DirectSound and WASAPI. rvc-next combines these into one item and automatically selects the recommended driver (in order of preference: ASIO, WASAPI, WDM-KS, DirectSound, MME on Windows; JACK, ALSA, PulseAudio on Linux; the PortAudio most Linux distributions ship has no PulseAudio driver, so PulseAudio and PipeWire appear as the ALSA devices **pulse**, **pipewire** and **default**)."],[10633,"Each name is followed by the driver's name in brackets, for example *(VB-Audio Voicemeeter VAIO)*. After an update from an older version, choose the devices again in every program that used them."],[8072,"Each operation has exactly one core method, accepting and returning `Record` models (`core/record.py`). Routes and commands do only three things: parse input, call that method and shape the output. For conversion, the route body in `api/routers/convert.py` only checks access to server paths, rejects CLI-only fields, then calls `return services.conversion.convert(body)`; the CLI's `convert` command constructs the same `ConvertRequest` and calls the same method (`foreground=True`)."],[10443,"Each page **stays as you left it**: added inputs, selected voice, adjusted parameters and scroll position are preserved, so you can resume when you return."],[10477,"Each result occupies one row, with:"],[10290,"Each row shows download progress, downloaded/total size, speed and time remaining; when complete, its status becomes **Installed**."],[11195,"Each row shows name, description, size (checked files are marked **verified**) and state: **Installed**, **Not installed**, **Partly downloaded**, **Checksum mismatch**, **Downloading**. Available actions:"],[10297,"Each row shows the sample rate, version, whether it is **with index**, and size. Click **Download** on the voice you want, or **Download all** at the top right of the group."],[8066,"Each rule has a purpose:"],[11244,"Each slider shows its current value and a line of help beneath it. When the value differs from the default, a **Reset to default** (↺) button appears beside it. If a parameter has no effect on the current voice, its slider is dimmed and explains why."],[9383,"Each stage is a function: it accepts a frozen request dataclass, writes to the experiment folder, reports progress and logs through callbacks, and skips completed work. Stages run in `workers.train` subprocesses (one process per stage; cancellation kills the process tree); parallel portions use `train/parallel.py:run_parts()` to start subprocesses with `spawn` (fork breaks CUDA and some BLAS implementations), running in-process when there is only one part."],[8890,"Each stage starts a `workers.train` subprocess (except `clean`, which calls separation's `run_files()` and writes each speaker's primary stem to `dataset_clean/<speaker id>/`). Separate processes have the same rationale as the original: cancellation kills the process tree, CUDA contexts stay clean, and DDP needs its own processes anyway. Worker `metric` events become `train_metrics` (sent to the Web UI's Pinia store for loss curves); full metrics are in the experiment's `metrics.jsonl`, read by `metrics(name, since)`."],[11071,"Each voice has a default preset, created on import from the default parameters in settings. Selecting the voice on another page automatically loads these parameters. Adjust them here and click **Save**. See Voice parameters for their meanings."],[8761,"Each voice has at most one index per speaker key: `default` or `spk<N>`, with filenames `model.index` and `spkid<N>.index`; attaching another replaces the old one (multiple indexes per key are unsupported, decided during import planning). `index_for(voice, speaker_id)` tries `spk<N>`, then `default`; a multi-speaker voice without the appropriate key does not fall back to another speaker's index."],[10364,"Each voice shows its sample rate, version (v1/v2), **pitch guidance** or **no pitch guidance**, and speaker count for multi-speaker voices;"],[11234,"Each voice's default preset"],[10326,"Earlier results"],[11061,"Edit **Name**, **Description** and **Tags** (separated by commas). For voices with several speakers, you can also name each **Speaker N**. Click **Save** when finished."],[8467,"Effect"],[9284,"Effect"],[7365,"Effective settings are merged from four layers, with later layers overriding earlier ones:"],[10334,"Effects"],[10780,"Effects"],[7705,"Effects of `compute.device`, `compute.precision`, `compute.cuda_graph_live`, and `live.enable_asio` on live voice conversion"],[7309,"Effects over the converted voice, as `convert --effect`; replaces the saved chain, `none` clears it"],[7823,"Embedded mode (`RvcNextServer` in `embed.py`) takes the same path: `build_services(data_dir, config_dir, settings_path, settings_overrides, start_background=True)`, bind the port, `create_app(..., api_prefix=...)`, run uvicorn on a background thread, and write `server.json` as `rvc-next webui` does. `normalize_prefix()` turns `voice` and `/voice/` into `/voice`; `SecurityMiddleware` matches its protected paths under the prefix. For usage, see Embedding in another program."],[6086,"Embedding in another program"],[6940,"Empty"],[6963,"Empty"],[7413,"Empty"],[7498,"Empty"],[7514,"Empty"],[7592,"Empty"],[7604,"Empty"],[7608,"Empty"],[7668,"Empty"],[11736,"Empty"],[11745,"Empty"],[7445,"Empty (`<data directory>/assets`)"],[7437,"Empty (`<data directory>/experiments`)"],[7433,"Empty (`<data directory>/models`)"],[7441,"Empty (`<data directory>/outputs`)"],[7628,"Empty (no monitoring)"],[8237,"Empty directory settings mean “inside the data directory”: `SettingsService.models_dir`, `experiments_dir`, `outputs_dir`, `assets_dir` resolve them. `paths.assets_dir` can point directly to an original RVC `assets/` directory to avoid duplicate downloads."],[8940,"Empty folder settings mean “inside the data directory”: `models_dir`, `experiments_dir`, `outputs_dir` (`convert.output_dir` takes precedence), `assets_dir`. The data directory itself comes from `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` or the platform user data directory (`core/paths.py`)."],[11718,"Empty: written into the voices you train (with their epoch, step and date), for all experiments"],[10372,"Enable **Separate first** (described as “Convert only the vocals of a song.”) to split the audio with a separation model before conversion and convert only the vocals. This reveals:"],[7689,"Enable the ASIO driver (Windows)"],[10381,"Enabling **Separate first** adds the selected preset's separation models to the required-download check. Separation models are large (300–440 MB each)."],[10320,"Encountered a problem? FAQ"],[7495,"Endpoint for accessing the repository: `https://huggingface.co`, `https://hf-mirror.com`, or custom"],[6814,"Endpoint: `huggingface`, `hf-mirror`, or `custom` (saved to settings)"],[9010,"Engine"],[10188,"Engine"],[9649,"Engine has no UI dependencies"],[9648,"Engine returns Gradio update dictionaries and Chinese statuses"],[8584,"Engine runtime, GPU lease, GPU memory release"],[10170,"English"],[11209,"Enter a **New voice name** and click **Merge**."],[11213,"Enter a **New voice name**."],[11984,"Enter a **Voice name**, defaulting to the experiment name."],[11445,"Enter a name in **Preset name**."],[11810,"Enter a path in **Dataset folder**, or click **Browse…** to select one."],[11615,"Enter a sufficiently long random string in **Access token**."],[11797,"Enter an **Experiment name**."],[11163,"Enter the original's root directory in **RVC folder** (it should contain an `assets` folder), or click **Browse…** to select it."],[11804,"Enter the path in **Original experiment folder (logs/\\<name>)**. Optionally enter a new **Experiment name** (defaults to the folder name)."],[8947,"Entire `Job`"],[8127,"Entry point"],[9563,"Entry point"],[9446,"Entry points"],[7214,"Enumerate devices again"],[9037,"Enumeration and grouping (`devices.py`)"],[9917,"Environment"],[9828,"Environment variable"],[7352,"Environment variables"],[7370,"Environment variables and overrides apply only in memory and **are not written back** to `settings.toml`. Folder settings overridden by environment variables are marked **Set by an environment variable** in the Web UI, and those pinned by a host program **Set by the application rvc-next runs in**. When `rvc-next config set` changes an overridden setting, it reports \"An environment variable overrides this setting.\"."],[8233,"Environment variables use `__` to separate levels, for example `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000`, `RVC_NEXT_COMPUTE__DEVICE=cpu`; values are parsed as JSON if possible, otherwise as strings, with `null` / `none` meaning empty. Environment variables and overrides are never written back to the file. `RVC_NEXT_DATA_DIR` is not a setting: it determines the data directory itself."],[7585,"Epochs, `[1, 10000]`"],[10921,"Equal to the crossfade"],[9905,"Error shapes, Host / Origin / token, raw uploads, Range, peaks, browse roots, submitting conversion through the API, events listed in OpenAPI"],[8037,"Errors and exit codes"],[8439,"Errors and exit codes"],[10453,"Errors appear where they occur (in the action bar, a job card or a dialog). The title is the translated error type (for example, “A required model file is not installed” or “The GPU is not available or ran out of memory”), followed by the server's specific message (in English). When more information is available, a **Details** button opens the full content, which you can include in a problem report."],[7849,"Errors are defined in `core/errors.py`; `api/errors.py` only maps them. HTTP status codes and CLI exit codes come from the same exception class (see Architecture for the full table). `ERROR_RESPONSES` declares the `ErrorResponse` model for 400/403/404/409, so the generated client knows the error body shape. A few API-specific conventions:"],[10449,"Errors from this page;"],[8228,"Errors reach this table from three sources:"],[7851,"Errors written directly by `SecurityMiddleware` (`bad_host` 400, `bad_origin` 403, `auth_required` 401) bypass exception handlers but have the same shape."],[10521,"esc closes the topmost dialog, menu or sheet (one layer at a time)."],[4436,"esc 关闭最上层的对话框、菜单或侧边栏（一次只关一层）。"],[10954,"Estimated latency ≈ block length + crossfade + 10 ms (alignment search) + block length (output prefill) + the device's input and output latency. Split streams add another block length; input noise reduction adds min(crossfade, 40 ms). The default settings (250 ms block length, 50 ms crossfade) give about 560 ms plus device latency with a duplex stream."],[11843,"Even out each piece (default) / Even out each file / Leave as recorded"],[7938,"Event"],[8943,"Event"],[7937,"Event classes are defined in `core/events/models.py`; all inherit `EventBase` and set `__event_name__`. `EventBase.get_events()` recursively collects all named subclasses."],[8010,"Event schemas use serialization mode, but event fields with defaults may still be optional in TypeScript; comments in `api/types.ts` record this (the server always sends them)."],[8039,"Events"],[8557,"Events"],[7807,"Events and payloads"],[8161,"Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@rvc ` (`protocol/jsonl.py`), with types in `protocol/messages.py`: `progress`, `step`, `log`, `metric`, `output`, `result`, `error`. Lines without the prefix are always treated as `info` logs."],[9417,"Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@rvc ` (`protocol/jsonl.py`); `parse_line()` treats unprefixed lines as info logs. Types are in `protocol/messages.py`: `progress`, `step`, `log`, `metric`, `output`, `result`, `error`."],[8688,"Events carry the full `Job` snapshot, so cannot be sent per audio block"],[7808,"Events in OpenAPI"],[8697,"Events only signal new logs; full contents use REST"],[8690,"Every 2 seconds (`DB_PROGRESS_INTERVAL`)"],[11069,"Every attachment checks that the index fits the voice. Empty indexes with no vectors (the original's `trained_*.index`) and indexes with a mismatched version (256 dimensions for v1, 768 for v2) are rejected."],[7929,"Every client that passes the middleware may name paths on the server (browsing, resolving audio paths, importing models or indexes by path, creating experiments or updating datasets, importing legacy experiments, adding legacy RVC installations, and so on). Only `reveal` requires a local client: a remote browser has no reason to open the file manager on the server's desktop."],[7779,"Every command level accepts `--debug` to enable debug logs:"],[8488,"Every command that lists or displays data has `--json`. `print_json()` serializes `Record` with `model_dump(mode=\"json\")` (recursively handling lists and dictionaries, converting `Path` to strings), so output exactly matches API JSON. This is more than a convention: commands and routes call the same core method and return the same `Record`. `test_model_json_matches_api_shape` directly compares `rvc-next model list --json` with `GET /api/v1/models`."],[8375,"Every file exists with the correct size, with no recorded verification failures"],[8324,"Every file RVC Next uses, organized by category, plus demo voices and `manifest.json`"],[8639,"Every lengthy operation is a job (`core/jobs/`): one card, one cancel button, one log, consistently across the Web UI, API and CLI. This replaces the original's separate progress displays in each tab and global `TRAIN_TASK` lock."],[8718,"Every model type under `models/` (`paths.models_dir`, inside the data directory by default) is a folder with a JSON sidecar:"],[11598,"Every setting can be overridden by an environment variable in the form `RVC_NEXT_<GROUP>__<FIELD>`, for example `RVC_NEXT_SERVER__PORT=8000` or `RVC_NEXT_PATHS__ASSETS_DIR=D:\\rvc-assets`. Environment variables take precedence over `settings.toml`. The UI shows the effective value; edits in the UI write to `settings.toml`, but the environment variable's value stays effective while it is set. Folders pinned by environment variables in **Storage** are marked **Set by an environment variable**. See Configuration and environment variables for the full list, or run `rvc-next env`."],[6366,"Every slice except the last loses its tail (a regression in the original)"],[9498,"Every slice's tail was silently dropped from the original training dataset"],[11436,"Every voice has a **default preset**, created automatically on import and named `Default`, with initial values from `convert.default_params` in settings (the defaults in the table above)."],[9552,"Evidence"],[9764,"Exact pin: the separation adapter was written for this version's `MSSeparator`"],[8172,"Exception"],[9419,"Exception mapping: `Cancelled` → 130; `MissingAssetError` → `asset_missing` (with `detail.assets`); `ModelFormatError` → `invalid_model`; OOM → `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason = \"out_of_memory\"`); other errors → `internal_error`, first sending the full traceback as a `log` event."],[8548,"Execution"],[8644,"Execution"],[9636,"Existing index skips building"],[9620,"Existing indexes"],[11127,"Existing library voices are considered only when no suitable voice is in this import."],[7749,"Exit code"],[8175,"Exit code"],[7727,"Exit codes"],[8163,"Exit codes: 0 for success; `EXIT_CANCELLED = 130` for cancellation (SIGTERM also maps to it); `EXIT_RETRY = 75` requests a retry in a new process (separation on DirectML tries fp16 first, then fp32 if it fails)."],[10140,"Exits finish under the zero-duration test stylesheet (`test/motion-zero.css`) with both full and reduced motion (no waiting forever for `transitionend` at duration 0); rules cover both reduced-motion sources; destination changes use view transitions; reduced motion uses a short crossfade"],[10844,"Expand **Advanced** to see:"],[10371,"Expand **Optional steps** to configure the following."],[10468,"Expand or collapse this job's log inside the card; once opened, the button becomes **Hide log**"],[10051,"Expand/collapse, height set by `collapseHooks`"],[7889,"Experiment CRUD, `dataset/scan`, `PUT/DELETE dataset/files` (uploaded audio), `speakers`, `speakers/from-folders`, `run` → `Job`, `stop`, `metrics?since=`, `checkpoints`, `samples` (one rendered training clip per save), `export` → `Job`, `try` (temporary voice), `POST /import` (legacy experiment)"],[9624,"Experiment folders