l."],[9800,"It runs these five steps in order, stopping at the first failure. CI runs the same checks (see “CI” below):"],[6275,"It works only on NVIDIA CUDA: on ROCm and XPU the switches have no effect and inference runs normally. Recordings are cached by input shape (up to 8 per call site, adjustable with `RVC_NEXT_CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_CACHE`). If recording fails, inference automatically falls back to normal mode. Offline inputs vary in length, making recordings hard to reuse, so it is disabled by default."],[10484,"Item"],[10806,"Item"],[10845,"Item"],[10964,"Item"],[10483,"Items in the **More actions** menu:"],[9916,"Job"],[10429,"Job cards"],[10455,"Job cards appear in the action bar of the page that started them and in the **Jobs** sheet. Each card shows:"],[8999,"Job history and retry"],[7342,"Job ID (required)"],[8095,"Job queue, resources, runners, history"],[8169,"Job requests are stored as JSON in the database. Factories registered by `kind` reconstruct `JobSpec` from the request, so **Retry** still works after a server restart."],[7948,"Job service, one batch every 0.25 s"],[7944,"Job service; state changes immediately, progress throttled to 4 updates per job per second (`PROGRESS_INTERVAL = 0.25`)"],[8144,"Job thread in the server (or CLI) process, with a `CancelToken`"],[8133,"Jobs"],[8519,"Jobs"],[10336,"Jobs"],[10428,"Jobs"],[11490,"Jobs"],[10149,"Jobs never regress, completion is notified once; preference migration; A/B player; deployment root derivation; proxy error classification"],[7324,"Jobs on this machine, including those from a running server."],[10430,"Jobs sheet and jobs page"],[6201,"Jobs still queued or running when the server exits are marked **Interrupted** at the next start. Their requests are saved in the database; click **Retry** to rerun. Training resumes from the last saved checkpoint."],[6554,"Jobs: `jobs`"],[10950,"Joins blocks with a phase vocoder (from RVC's later realtime GUI, as Applio uses it) instead of the plain crossfade: when 