h operations to allow based on whether the request comes from the local machine:"],[6468,"When allowing other computers to connect, narrow the scope to the folders you need:"],[10427,"When an error occurs"],[6301,"When an experiment's **GPUs** setting is `cpu` (new experiments take the default from `training.gpus`), training also runs as a CPU job."],[8852,"When applicable"],[10486,"When available"],[7912,"When bound to loopback, the `Host` header must be `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1`, the bound hostname, or `extra_hosts` (kept by reference, so names added later count at once, which `RvcNextServer.allow_host()` relies on); otherwise 400 `bad_host`"],[10492,"When browser and server are on the same computer"],[10348,"When browser and server are on the same computer (or the server has an access token set), a **Server files** button appears. It uses files directly from the server's disk, **without uploading**, making it suitable for large files or large numbers of files:"],[6463,"When browsing or using server files, the Web UI (including local browsers) can access only folders in `paths.browse_roots`. Paths outside this scope are rejected (`invalid_path`). By default (an empty list), the scope includes:"],[10397,"When buttons are unavailable, the left side explains why: “Choose a voice.” or “Add audio to convert.” You also cannot start while inputs are still uploading. If required models are missing (HuBERT, the selected pitch method's model, separation models), the buttons are replaced by “**Needs …**” and a **Download** button; see Interface overview."],[11460,"When changes apply"],[11678,"When empty (default), this includes your home folder, added original RVC installs, the data folder and every drive (Windows `C:\\`, `D:\\`…) or mounted volume (macOS `/Volumes/…`; Linux `/media/<user>/…`, `/run/media/<user>/…`, `/mnt/…`). The gray placeholder lists the folders currently allowed. Entering paths restricts access to those folders."],[10843,"When enabled while running: with a monitor device, the monitor receives the original audio while the output stays converted; without one, the output switches directly to the original audio (temporarily bypassing conversion)."],[10842,"When enabled while stopped: passes audio through without loading a voice."],[6711,"When finished, prints output file paths one per line."],[6289,"When inference or training reports an out-of-memory error (CUDA `OutOfMemoryError` or the corresponding MPS or DirectML errors):"],[11952,"When it runs"],[7692,"When it takes effect"],[6133,"When listening only locally, the server accepts only requests whose `Host` is a local name or the bound address. A tunnel (such as a Gradio share link) or a reverse proxy forwards its own public host name, which has to be allowed first. A tunnel's address is often known only once the server has started and its port is fixed, so `allow_host()` can be called after `start()` too and takes effect at once:"],[6306,"When live voice conversion stops, waiting jobs start automatically."],[10426,"When models are missing"],[11898,"When off, the trained voice has no pitch guidance (suited to speech rather than singing), and the **Pitch** stage is skipped"],[8176,"When raised"],[7988,"When re-enumeration finds a change"],[10839,"When recording is not possible, the device panel says why. Send the converted voice to a **different** device than the one being recorded (headphones, or a virtual cable for another program): recording the output that plays the voice would feed it back into itself, so rvc-next refuses it (**Records its own output**). Turning the setting off hides these inputs again."],[10059,"When supported, `App.vue` renders views directly without `<Transition>`; otherwise it falls back to `<Transition mode=\"out-in\">` with `fade-through`."],[11452,"When switching **Pitch method**, the new method's model loads in the background. If it has not been downloaded, conversion continues using the previous method and reports the missing model."],[8899,"When switching voices, the worker replies with a `State` containing `voice_path` for **the voice actually converting now**: the new voice, or the old one retained after loading failure. The service looks it up in `_voice_ids` (model path → voice id), making state follow the worker rather than the request, and updates `live.last_voice` to the actual voice in use. A speaker out of range for the new voice resets to 0. F0 method changes check assets first; if the worker cannot load the new method, it keeps the old one."],[10298,"When the download finishes, the row shows **Installed** and an **In library** button; click it to open the voice's details. The voice also appears in **Models › Voices**."],[6137,"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or any ASGI) application, it can mount RVC Next instead of opening another port:"],[6200,"When the number of GPU jobs reaches **GPU jobs at once**, other jobs queue. While live voice conversion runs, new GPU jobs also wait to avoid affecting live audio. **Run anyway** on the job card starts a job without waiting for live voice conversion to stop (which may cause audio glitches)."],[10994,"When the original device reappears (including under another driver), the stream reopens automatically and returns to **Running**, without reloading the voice."],[6479,"When the server listens only locally, the forwarded `Host` must be `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` (otherwise 400 `bad_host`); a program embedding rvc-next can allow a proxy's or a tunnel's public host name with `extra_hosts` / `allow_host()` (Embedding);"],[10509,"When there is more than one result, **Download all** appears at the top right of the list to download them as a zip."],[9747,"When writing documentation:"],[10900,"When you click **Start**, if the saved **Output** device is missing but the system default is available, rvc-next asks for confirmation before sending audio there (it could be your speakers): **The saved output device is missing; the system default would be used.** It continues only after you click **Start with the default output**. If the input or monitor device cannot be found at all, it reports an error; select another device first."],[10368,"When you select a voice, **Voice parameters** loads that voice's default preset automatically, so the same voice sounds consistent in conversion and live voice conversion. RVC Next remembers the last voice you selected on this page."],[7389,"Whenever a running server reads settings, it checks at most once per second whether another process (`rvc-next config set` or a text editor) has changed `settings.toml`. If so, it reloads the file and notifies open Web UI sessions. When the Web UI saves settings, it also reads the file first, merges with its current contents, and writes it back without overwriting changes made elsewhere. If a manual edit cannot be parsed or fails validation, the server logs a warning and continues using the previous settings."],[10871,"Whenever you change devices, rvc-next actually tries to open them with the current configuration in the background: it checks the settings with the driver and, while Live is stopped, runs the output and monitor for a moment (the input is already open for the **Input level** meter). Problems therefore appear below the relevant device before you click **Start**, and so does a failed **Test** sound or **Hear yourself**. The format is **reason: explanation from the server** (the explanation is supplied by the server in English, naming the device):"],[10338,"Where files are saved and how they are named"],[8138,"Where it runs"],[11577,"Where settings are saved"],[12004,"Where to start for common tasks"],[12115,"Whether `ffmpeg` is found (optional; PyAV can decode without it);"],[12116,"Whether audio devices are available (required for live voice conversion);"],[11743,"Whether new experiments save a voice at every save point"],[6129,"Whether to open a browser after starting; `False` by default"],[7363,"Which changes require a restart"],[11783,"Which stages must rerun after settings change?"],[10990,"While a session is active (running, loading, reconnecting, etc.), every page's top bar shows a Live chip, for example **Live · 620 ms**. During loading and similar operations, it shows the current state instead. Click the chip to return to **Live**; the button on its right stops the session from any page. The chip turns red on reconnection or error."],[10668,"While a voice chat program records, Windows may lower every other sound. To stop that, open the Sound Control Panel's **Communications** tab and choose **Do nothing**."],[10980,"While Live runs, **Record** beside the start button writes the session to a WAV file in the outputs folder (`<date>/live/`). Choose what to keep:"],[10519,"While live voice conversion is running, a chip appears before the buttons on the right of the top bar, visible on every page. It shows “Live · N ms” (estimated latency) while running, or the current state during startup, loading or reconnection, such as “Loading the voice…” or “Reconnecting the device…”. Click the chip to open **Live**; click the square **Stop** button beside it to stop live voice conversion directly. See Live voice conversion."],[11976,"While running, the **Run** step shows a job card and a progress bar appears below the step bar. The same job appears in the top-bar **Jobs** panel, where you can read its log. Training queues as a GPU job: if live voice conversion is using the GPU, it shows **Waiting for the GPU**. You can click **Run anyway** (which may cause live audio glitches)."],[11655,"While the device panel is shown, it keeps the microphone open and shows **Input level** even when Live is stopped. The microphone is released about 15 seconds after the page is closed or hidden. Turn this off if you do not want the microphone kept in use"],[10820,"While the server is still listing the devices (a moment, longer with many drivers installed), each menu says **Looking for audio devices…**."],[12123,"Who it is for"],[9148,"Who unloads what after OOM is a core policy (`release_after_oom`); see Core services."],[9614,"Why"],[8427,"Why not download directly from distributions: these `.7z` files use solid compression; voices share 1.3–1.9 GB compressed blocks with other assets, so fetching one file requires downloading and decompressing at least its entire block. This is a major reason for rvc-model."],[8334,"Why rvc-model exists: the official repository retains an early flat layout, mixing code, Windows executables, and tens of GB of distributions; some models (demo voices) exist only inside `.7z` distributions and cannot be downloaded individually (see below). rvc-model copies the required files unchanged into categories, making each file available separately."],[8782,"Width `d` (256 → v1, 768 → v2), vector count `ntotal` (0 means `trained_` index), `engine/index/inspect.py`"],[1629,"Windows"],[4172,"Windows"],[4481,"Windows"],[4485,"Windows"],[4745,"Windows"],[7714,"Windows"],[10257,"Windows"],[10566,"Windows"],[10570,"Windows"],[10830,"Windows"],[12089,"Windows and Linux:"],[12091,"Windows and Linux:"],[12093,"Windows and Linux:"],[10653,"Windows lets a program take a device for itself (*exclusive mode*): while it holds the device, no other program can play or record through it. By default every device allows this, and an exclusive request even takes the device away from programs already using it (\"Give exclusive mode applications priority\"). Some games, voice chat programs and audio players ask for exclusive mode, and then rvc-next loses the microphone or the virtual device in the middle of a session (Live goes to **Reconnecting the device…**), or cannot open it at all (**In use by another program**). The other program can lose it to rvc-next the same way."],[9582,"Windows VST2/VST3 plugin (iPlug2) driving a Python worker"],[3497,"Windows VST2/VST3 插件（iPlug2）驱动一个 Python worker"],[4568,"Windows 允许一个程序把设备据为己有（*独占模式*）：它占着设备时，其他程序都不能通过这台设备播放或录音。默认情况下每台设备都允许这样做，而且独占请求甚至会把设备从正在使用它的程序手里抢走（“给与独占模式应用程序优先”）。有些游戏、语音聊天程序和播放器会请求独占模式，这时 rvc-next 会在会话中途失去麦克风或虚拟声卡（实时变声进入 **正在重新连接设备…**），或者根本打不开它（**被其他程序占用**）。反过来，其他程序也可能这样被 rvc-next 抢走设备。"],[6004,"Windows 和 Linux："],[6006,"Windows 和 Linux："],[6008,"Windows 和 Linux："],[10731,"Windows, macOS: rvc-next's **Input** must then name your real microphone, not **System default**"],[4646,"Windows、macOS：rvc-next 的 **输入** 必须选真实的麦克风，而不是 **系统默认**"],[10764,"Windows: **Let desktop apps access your microphone**. macOS: allow the terminal in **Privacy & Security › Microphone** and restart it"],[10741,"Windows: **Settings › System › Sound › Volume mixer**, choose the browser, set its **Output device** to **CABLE Input**."],[11593,"Windows: `%APPDATA%\\rvc-next`"],[10761,"Windows: Live loses a device (**Reconnecting the device…**) or reports **In use by another program** when a game or another program starts"],[10542,"Windows: microphone access and ducking"],[10541,"Windows: turn off exclusive control (optional, recommended)"],[10529,"Windows: VB-CABLE"],[10533,"Windows: Voicemeeter"],[4679,"Windows：**允许桌面应用访问你的麦克风**。macOS：在 **隐私与安全性 › 麦克风** 中允许终端，然后重启它"],[4656,"Windows：**设置 › 系统 › 声音 › 音量合成器**，选浏览器，把它的 **输出设备** 设为 **CABLE Input**。"],[5508,"Windows：`%APPDATA%\\rvc-next`"],[4444,"Windows：VB-CABLE"],[4448,"Windows：Voicemeeter"],[4456,"Windows：关闭独占控制（可选，推荐）"],[4676,"Windows：游戏或其他程序启动时，实时变声失去设备（**正在重新连接设备…**）或报告 **被其他程序占用**"],[4457,"Windows：麦克风权限与自动降低音量"],[11447,"With **For this voice only** checked, you can also check **Make it this voice's default** to replace the previous default preset."],[11996,"With **Save a voice at every save point** enabled, **Try** small models from different epochs and **Export as voice** for the best one."],[10405,"With **Separate first** enabled, the first step is `Separate` (processing all inputs at once), followed by one step per input;"],[6476,"With **This browser** at the top of the Live page, the microphone of the phone or computer you opened the page on goes to the server, and the converted voice plays there (Use this browser's microphone). Browsers allow a page to use the microphone only over **HTTPS**, or on the server itself (`localhost`). For other computers, give the server a certificate:"],[6151,"With `--strict-port` (or `server.strict_port` set to `true`), the server fails immediately if the port is in use (exit code 3), without switching ports."],[6300,"With `cpu` as the device, these become CPU jobs, with at most half the CPU core count running concurrently."],[8842,"With `remix`, mix converted vocals at `vocal_gain_db` with accompaniment at `gain_db` (prefer labels `instrumental`/`accompaniment`/`other`/`no_vocals`) into stereo, scaling the whole mix if peak exceeds 0.99."],[8839,"With `separate`, all inputs are separated first in **one** separation worker (first 40% of progress), with intermediate stems in `<output directory>/stems/`."],[10673,"with Homebrew: `brew install blackhole-2ch`."],[10361,"With more than one input, click **Clear** to remove them all at once."],[11180,"With no imported models, the page shows **No separation models imported**. Built-in presets are always available on **Separate**."],[8861,"With pitch guidance"],[9197,"With pitch guidance"],[6309,"With the default **Block** of 250 milliseconds and **Crossfade** of 50 milliseconds, one duplex stream gives about 560 milliseconds plus device latency."],[10672,"with the installer from existential.audio/blackhole, restarting when it asks, or"],[6192,"With Voicemeeter, the strip rvc-next plays into needs **B1** on, and the microphone's own strip **B1** off."],[8489,"Without `--json`, `print_table()` renders a Rich table. Logs (including errors) go to **stderr** through `RichHandler` in `rvc_next/logger.py`, while data goes to **stdout**, so logs do not disrupt `rvc-next model list --json | jq`. The default log level is `INFO`, adjustable with `RVC_NEXT_LOG_LEVEL` or `--debug`."],[7789,"Without `--stage`, `train run` runs all unfinished stages or stages whose inputs have changed (clean, slice, pitch, features, fit, index). Use `--stage fit --stage index` to run only the specified stages, and `--force` to force a rerun."],[7785,"Without `-o`, results go to `outputs/<date>/<job id>/` under the data directory. File names are `<original name>.<voice>.<format>`; existing files are never overwritten (overwriting requires both `-o` and `--overwrite`)."],[7788,"Without `-p`, the default separation preset from settings is used (`separation.default_preset`, default: `vocals`). Separation models must be downloaded before first use, for example with `rvc-next assets download --group separation`."],[11344,"Without a GPU, if speed matters, try **SwiftF0**, **FCPE** or **CREPE tiny**, or **pm** for clean speech."],[6170,"Without an index, **Index strength** has no effect (the UI tells you). Conversion still works, but voice characteristics come entirely from the model itself. To attach an index:"],[9768,"Without it, uvicorn has no WebSocket support and socket.io falls back to long polling"],[9198,"Without pitch guidance"],[8137,"Work"],[3335,"Worker"],[9420,"Worker"],[8932,"Worker `Stats` (about 10 Hz) become `live_stats`, and state changes become `live_state`. When the live worker reports OOM, it unloads its models first, then core calls `release_after_oom(\"Live\")`."],[8551,"Worker and connection"],[8160,"Worker entry points go through `run_worker()` in `workers/base.py`: it duplicates the real stdout exclusively for events, then redirects file descriptor 1 to stderr. Incidental `print` calls in libraries therefore become log text and cannot be mistaken for events."],[8035,"Worker protocol"],[9044,"Worker subprocess entry points"],[2815,"worker 一连上就会宣告一次 `stopped`；`_awaiting_start` 让服务忽略这条，直到 `Start` 被处理，否则界面会在启动时闪回「已停止」。"],[2466,"worker 与连接"],[1950,"worker 协议"],[2817,"worker 回应电平表或直通请求时保留上一个错误：以前会话失败后电平表重新打开，会在用户看清之前把错误清掉。"],[2812,"worker 在会话停止后仍保持运行（为了电平表和快速再启动），模型留在它自己的进程里，这正是「释放显存」要通知它的原因（`P.ReleaseMemory`）。"],[2959,"Worker 子进程的入口"],[3562,"worker 子进程读 JSON 请求文件，用 `sys.executable` 启动"],[2847,"worker 的 `Stats` 消息（约 10 Hz）转成 `live_stats` 事件，状态变化转成 `live_state`。live worker 报告显存不足时，它先卸载自己的模型，核心层再调用 `release_after_oom(\"Live\")`。"],[2075,"worker 的入口经过 `workers/base.py` 的 `run_worker()`：它把真正的 stdout 复制出来专门写事件，再把文件描述符 1 重定向到 stderr。库函数随手 `print` 的内容因此只会变成日志文本，不会被误当作事件。"],[9647,"Workers read JSON request files, launched with `sys.executable`"],[9964,"Works under any subpath without server rewrite rules"],[10832,"Works with any output device, at any sample rate; silence while nothing plays"],[8843,"Write `<stem>.<voice slug>[.preview].<format>`, record outputs (`converted`, `remix` or `preview`), then delete intermediate stems."],[8023,"Write a core method with `Record` parameters and return values; use existing error classes in `core/errors.py`."],[6902,"Write a voice as a zip to import on another machine: `<name>/<name>.pth` (speaker names written into the copy) and its indexes (`<name>.index`, `<name>_spkid<N>.index`)."],[8693,"Write and publish immediately"],[7969,"Write directly to `keys.assets`; invalidate base models and demo voices"],[6768,"Write the MP3 here"],[6716,"Write the pitch curve as `time_s,f0_hz` (0 where there is no pitch)"],[7841,"Write the request body to a temporary file asynchronously, then pass it to the core via `run_in_threadpool`"],[7993,"Write to `keys.computeUsage`"],[7989,"Write to `keys.liveDevices`"],[7945,"Write to the jobs store and `keys.job(id)`; invalidate related lists on completion"],[8745,"Writes first go to a temporary `.<slug>.part` folder, then `rename` the whole folder (`_add_to_library`); sidecars use `.tmp` then `replace`, so failures cannot leave a partial voice. Libraries before 2026-10-04 used `models/<slug>/`; `_migrate_layout()` in `rescan()` moves folders containing `model.pth` whose names are not reserved (`RESERVED`) into `models/voices/`, retaining ids."],[7609,"Written into the voices you train, with the epoch, step and date"],[155,"XPU 版 torch 上的第 N 块 Intel 显卡（Arc、数据中心 GPU、较新的核显）。退回规则与 `cuda:N` 相同"],[6277,"XPU: Intel GPUs appear as `xpu:N`. Conversion, Live, training (fp16 with AMP; several cards train with the `xccl` backend) and pitch and feature extraction run on them. Vocal separation loads the model on the CPU, moves it to the GPU and runs in fp32, because pymss has no XPU support of its own."],[192,"XPU：Intel 显卡显示为 `xpu:N`。转换、实时变声、训练（fp16 使用 AMP；多卡训练使用 `xccl` 后端）以及音高和特征提取都在上面运行。人声分离先在 CPU 上加载模型再移到显卡，并以 fp32 运行，因为 pymss 本身不支持 XPU。"],[8795,"YAML (`.yaml`, `.yml`)"],[2710,"YAML（`.yaml`、`.yml`）"],[8392,"Yes"],[8396,"Yes"],[8400,"Yes"],[8404,"Yes"],[6157,"Yes. Command-line jobs run in their own processes and write records to the same database, so both the Web UI's **Jobs** panel and `rvc-next jobs list` show jobs from either side. Keep two points in mind: command-line jobs do not participate in the server's GPU queue, so concurrent jobs compete for GPU memory; for settings changes, see the previous question."],[6209,"Yes. In **Models** › **Voices**, use **Add an RVC install** under **Original RVC installs**. Voices in the original `assets/weights` appear directly in the voice list (marked **legacy**), with indexes recommended using the original rules. Point `paths.assets_dir` to the original `assets` folder to reuse HuBERT, RMVPE, base models, and separation models. See Migrate from original RVC."],[10406,"You can **Cancel** at any time, or **Retry** after failure, cancellation or interruption. Click **Log** for details. For example, if the voice has no index and **Index strength** is above 0, the log records `No index for this voice; index strength has no effect`."],[11559,"You can also import your own separation models (checkpoint and `.yaml` configuration) in **Models › Separation models**. Each imported model becomes a single-step preset here, with an **imported** label on its card. See Model management for import instructions."],[7780,"You can also set the log level with the `RVC_NEXT_LO